      "exp_en": "The main actions of the formula are to enrich the yin and nourish the Kidneys. The symptoms point to Liver and Kidney yin xu. The lower back is the home of the Kidneys which control the bones and generate marrow. Weak Kidneys will cause a weak and sore lower back. When the Kidneys are weak there is deficiency of essence and when the Liver is weak there is a deficiency of blood. The deficiency in essence and blood fail to nourish the upper ares of the body, the orifices and head. This results in light headedness, vertigo, tinnitus and diminished hearing (Kidney association to the ears). When the yin is deficient, the yin fails to be anchored at night resulting in night sweats and nocturnal and spontaneous emissions in men. If the yin deficiency gives rise to empty fire, there can be hot palms and soles, a flushed face, a dry sore throat, and tooth pain. The yin xu is reflected in the red tongue with less than normal coating. The pulse is thin reflecting yin xu and rapid reflecting empty heat. (出處：Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 365)",
