      "exp_en": "LU-7 (lie que) can treat the shoulder because the Lung divergent channel converges with the Large Intestine channel at the neck. KI-4 (da zhong) can treat back of neck pain because the Kidney divergent goes to the nape. PC-5 (jian shi) can treat voice loss because the Pericardium divergent channel goes to the throat. GB-26 treats genital problems because the Gall Bladder divergent joins the Liver Divergent channel which goes to the pubic area.. Other connections are the use of LI-4 or LI-11 to treat external wind because the Large Intestine divergent connects with the Lungs. Some stomach points (eg ST-25, ST-36) can treat Spleen problems because both the Stomach divergent and primary connect with the Spleen. PC-6 can treat neck and head problems because the Pericardium divergent goes to the neck. GB-34 can treat Liver qi stasis because the Gall Bladder divergent and primary connect with the Liver. BL-57 and BL-58 can treat anal problems such as hemorrhoids because the Bladder divergent channel circles the anus. GB-40 can treat emotional issues arising from Gall Bladder deficiency (timidity, indecision, lack of courage and initiative) because the Gall Bladder divergent channel connects with the Heart. LU-10 can treat diarrhea and constipation because the Lung divergent and primary connect with the Large Intestine. Unlike luo-connecting channels, divergent channels do not have their own points and do not have their pathology. Divergent channels do not have a pathology independent of the primary channel. Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 344-345",
