      "exp_en": "Kidney Yin Deficiency. Without moxa, REN-4 (guan yuan) nourishes Kidney Yin and Kidney essence with moxa it tonifies Kidney yang. KI-3 (tai xi) strengthens the Kidneys. KI-6 (zhao hai) nourishes Kidney yin and benefits the throat. KI-10 (yin gu) tonifies Kidney yin. SP-6 (san yin jiao) tonifies Liver and Kidney yin and calms the spirit. Other points to consider in this formula are REN-7 (yin jiao) which nourishes Kidney yin, KI-9 (zhu bin) which nourishes Kidney yin and is particularly useful when there is anxiety of Kidney origin. Also, the combination of LU-7 (lie que) and KI-6 (zhao hai) can be used to open up the Ren Mai and nourish Kidney yin. Reinforcing needle technique is used. Moxa is not used. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 627; 2005 Edition, page 593; 1989 Edition page 252",
      "exp_hant": "此為腎陰虛證。關元若不施灸，可滋腎陰、養腎精；若加灸則能溫補腎陽。太谿可強腎。照海滋腎陰、利咽喉。陰谷補腎陰。三陰交補肝腎之陰並安神。本方亦可考慮加用陰交以滋腎陰，或加用築賓以滋腎陰，對於腎源性焦慮尤為適用。此外，列缺與照海合用可開通任脈並滋養腎陰。宜用補法，不宜施灸。《中醫基礎學》，Maciocia，2015年，第627頁；2005年版，第593頁；1989年版，第252頁"
