    {
      "number": 174,
      "question_en": "A 34 year-old female has elbow joint pain with soreness and heaviness. She has difficulty flexing the lower arm. Your point prescription is LI-11 (qu chi), TB-10 (tian jing), and TB-5 (wai guan). Which two points would you add to the prescription?",
      "question_hant": "一名34歲女性有肘關節疼痛，並伴有痠痛與沉重感，前臂屈曲困難。您的處方為曲池、天井與外關。您會再加入下列哪兩個穴位？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "BL-11 (da zhu), GB-39 (xuan zhong)",
          "hant": "大杼、懸鐘",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "BL-23 (shen shu), REN-4 (guan yuan)",
          "hant": "腎俞、關元",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "DU-14 (da zhui), LI-5 (yang xi)",
          "hant": "大椎、陽谿",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "GB-34 (yang ling quan), BL-23 (shen shu)",
          "hant": "陽陵泉、腎俞",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is bone bi-syndrome. In addition to being classified in terms of causative pathogens (heat, cold, wind, damp), bi-syndromes can be classified in terms of location such as skin bi (numb skin), muscle bi (soreness, numbness of muscles) tendon bi (tendons and muscles which are sore, stiff), blood vessel bi (pain from blockage in the vessels), and bone bi (heaviness, pain, in joints that fail in performing functions such as lifting, extension, flexion). BL-11 is the meeting point for the bones and benefits the bones and joints. In bone bi there can also be bone deformities that can, for example, manifest in rheumatoid arthritis. BL-11 can be used in various diseases of the bones and rigidity. Clinically, it can also be used with channel obstructions due to wind, cold, damp, or heat. GB-39 is the meeting point for the marrow and benefits the joints and bones. Clinically, GB-39 is not used to treat the sea of marrow (head and brain) but to treat disorders of the bone marrow and sinews such as joint contraction, painful limbs, limb weakness or flaccidity. CAM, 3rd Edition, page 464; CAM, 4th Edition, 1999, page 562-564",
      "exp_hant": "此為骨痹證。痹證除依致病邪氣（熱、寒、風、濕）分類外，亦可依部位分類，如皮痹（皮膚麻木）、肌痹（肌肉痠痛麻木）、筋痹（筋肉痠痛僵硬）、脈痹（血脈阻滯所致疼痛）及骨痹（關節沉重疼痛，導致提舉、伸展、屈曲等功能受損）。大杼為骨之會穴，能益骨利節。骨痹亦可能伴有骨骼變形，如可表現為類風濕性關節炎。大杼可用於治療各種骨病與僵直，臨床上亦可用於風、寒、濕、熱所致之經絡阻滯。懸鐘為髓之會穴，能益關節與骨骼。臨床上，懸鐘並非用以治療髓海（頭腦），而是用於治療骨髓與筋之病症，如關節攣縮、肢體疼痛、肢體痿軟無力等。CAM，第3版，第464頁；CAM，第4版，1999年，第562-564頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 175,
      "question_en": "What qualities of enlarged lymph nodes are required to have for a referral assessment in a patient feeling unwell?",
      "question_hant": "在患者自覺不適的情況下，腫大淋巴結需具備哪些特徵才需轉診評估？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "enlarged nodes of greater than 1 cm diameter or greater, painful red nodes, lasting longer than one week",
          "hant": "腫大淋巴結直徑1公分以上，紅腫疼痛，持續超過一週",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "enlarged nodes of greater than 1 cm diameter, painless nodes, lasting longer than two weeks",
          "hant": "腫大淋巴結直徑大於1公分，不痛，持續超過兩週",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "group of nodes 0.5 cm in diameter, painful nodes associated with fever and malaise",
          "hant": "一群直徑0.5公分的淋巴結，疼痛並伴隨發燒與倦怠",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "single node of greater than 1 cm diameter or greater, painful red nodes, lasting longer than one week",
          "hant": "單一淋巴結直徑1公分以上，紅腫疼痛，持續超過一週",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Lymph nodes are normally non-palpable masses of soft tissue. They can enlarge and become palpable when there is an active infection. When there is an infection, an injury, or cancer, the lymph nodes in the local area can enlarge to filter out the damaged cells. Swollen lymph nodes in themselves are an indication of a disorder but other symptoms can indicate the reason why they are enlarged. The common causes of swollen lymph nodes are measles, an ear infection, colds, a strep throat, or glandular fever (mononucleosis). The common location for swollen lymph nodes are the neck, under the chin, the armpit, and the groin. During an infection the lymph nodes on the neck are both swollen and painful. The other cause of lymph node enlargement (lymphadenopathy) is cancer. Difficulty swallowing (dysphagia) with enlarged lymph nodes on the neck should be referred because it can be due to either cancer or due to an infection/inflammation. Enlarged groups of lymph nodes of 1 cm or more in diameter, are painless, not improving, lasting more than two weeks, and continue to grow larger can be a red flag for possible cancer, particularly if the patient feels unwell. Cancer can be associated enlarged lymph nodes because the cancer can start in the lymph nodes or the cancer can spread to the lymph nodes. More often, the cancer starts somewhere in the body and then spreads to the lymph nodes. That is, cancer cells separate from a tumor and travel to other locations through the bloodstream or through the lymphatic system. Cancer cells grow in the lymph nodes closest to the tumor. The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 49, 16",
      "exp_hant": "淋巴結正常情況下是無法觸摸到的軟組織團塊。當有活動性感染時，淋巴結會腫大而變得可觸及。當發生感染、外傷或癌症時，局部淋巴結會腫大以過濾受損細胞。淋巴結腫大本身即是一種病理徵象，但仍須參考其他症狀以判斷腫大原因。常見造成淋巴結腫大的原因包括麻疹、耳部感染、感冒、鏈球菌性咽喉炎，或腺熱（傳染性單核球增多症）。淋巴結腫大常見的部位為頸部、下巴下方、腋窩與腹股溝。感染時，頸部淋巴結會同時出現腫大與疼痛。另一造成淋巴結腫大（淋巴結病變）的原因則是癌症。若頸部淋巴結腫大合併吞嚥困難，應予轉診，因其可能是癌症或感染／發炎所致。若一群淋巴結腫大，直徑達1公分以上，不痛、未見改善、持續超過兩週且持續增大，即可能為癌症的警示徵象，尤其當患者同時感到不適時更應留意。癌症之所以與淋巴結腫大相關，是因為癌症可能起源於淋巴結，或由其他部位擴散至淋巴結。更常見的情況是，癌症起源於身體其他部位，再擴散至淋巴結，也就是癌細胞自腫瘤脫落，經由血流或淋巴系統轉移至其他部位，並在最接近腫瘤的淋巴結中生長。《輔助療法師紅旗轉診指南》，Stephenson，2013年，第49、16頁"
    },
    {
