          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "DU-16 (feng fu), GB-20 (feng chi), SI-3 (hou xi), BL-62 (shen mai), LI-11 (qu chi), SP-10 (xue hai)",
          "hant": "風府、風池、後谿、申脈、曲池、血海",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "PC-9 (zhong chong), PC-8 (lao gong), HT-9 (shao chong), KI-6 (zhao hai)",
          "hant": "中衝、勞宮、少衝、照海",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "LR-2 (xing jian), BL-17 (ge shu), LI-11 (qu chi), SP-10 (xue hai), HT-9 (shao chong), SP-4 (gong sun), KI-6 (zhao hai)",
          "hant": "行間、膈俞、曲池、血海、少衝、公孫、照海",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is a case developing into viral meningitis. Bacterial meningitis symptoms come on quickly, usually over a period of hours. With viral meningitis, symptoms might appear over several days. From a TCM perspective view the disease progression for this patient can be seen using different methods of analysis involving a mixture of Six Stages, Four Levels, and Sanjiao. It can be seen as defensive qi (wei) level > Qi level > Blood (xue) level. It can be seen as upper burner > Middle burner > Lower burner. And it can be viewed as defensive qi (wei) level > Yang ming stage > Blood (xue) level. The disease starts with external contraction of the pathogen. There are insufficient symptoms to determine if it is wind-heat (wei level, upper burner) or wind-cold (tai yang six stages) or whether it is wind-cold transforming into wind-heat. During the second day there are symptoms that can be classified as patterns in the Six Stages (yang ming heat), Four Levels (qi level Stomach heat), and the Middle Burner (Stomach Heat). On the third day we have symptoms patterns that can be classified as either belonging to the Blood level (Heat Victorious stirring Wind) or to the Lower Burner (Liver Heat stirs Wind). The terminal yin or jue yin stage is characterized by Heat (hot chest, rising energy, thirst) above and Cold below (cold limbs, diarrhea). The treatment principle for Heat Victorious stirring Wind is to Clear Blood Heat and Extinguish Wind. At the blood level the heat affects the Liver which then generates wind. This is wind of the excess type which can manifest as convulsions, limb twitching, rigid neck, teeth clenching, and opisthotonos (severe hyperextension and spasticity of spine and neck). DU-16 and GB-20 extinguish wind. LI-11 and SP-10 cool the blood. Opening up the du mai with SI-3 and BL-62 extinguishes wind and treats the spine. The Rx with LR-8 also treats one of the patterns at the blood level, Empty-Wind Agitating the Interior. Heat Victorious stirring Wind is an excess condition while Empty-Wind Agitating the Interior is rooted in Liver and Kidney yin deficiency with empty wind. The Rx with PC-9 treats heat at the nutritive qi level where the focus is on clearing nutritive level heat and promoting fluids. The Rx with LR-2 treats Heat Victorious agitating Blood which is a pattern at the Blood level. The focus here is to clear blood heat and stop bleeding. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 757, 762, 770, 773, 777, 784",
      "exp_hant": "此病例演變為病毒性腦膜炎。細菌性腦膜炎的症狀通常在數小時內快速出現，而病毒性腦膜炎的症狀則可能歷經數日才顯現。從中醫角度來看，此患者的病情演變可用六經、衛氣營血及三焦等不同辨證方法混合分析：可視為衛分→氣分→血分；亦可視為上焦→中焦→下焦；亦可視為衛分→陽明階段→血分。此病始於外感邪氣，但症狀尚不足以判定究竟屬風熱（衛分、上焦）或風寒（太陽六經），抑或風寒化熱。第二天的症狀可歸類為六經中的陽明熱證、衛氣營血中的氣分胃熱證，以及三焦中的中焦（胃熱）證。第三天的症狀則可歸類為血分證（熱盛動風），或下焦證（肝熱動風）。厥陰階段的特徵為上熱（胸中灼熱、氣上衝、口渴）下寒（四肢冰冷、腹瀉）。熱盛動風的治療原則為清血熱、熄風。在血分階段，熱邪侵犯肝臟因而生風，此為實證之風，可表現為抽搐、肢體震顫、頸項強直、牙關緊閉，以及角弓反張（脊背與頸部嚴重過度伸展並痙攣）。風府與風池能熄風；曲池與血海能涼血；以後谿與申脈開通督脈，能熄風並治療脊背病症。以曲泉為主的處方則治療血分證中的另一證型——虛風內動。熱盛動風屬實證，而虛風內動則根源於肝腎陰虛兼虛風內動。以中衝為主的處方治療營分熱證，其重點在於清營分熱並生津。以行間為主的處方治療熱盛擾血證，此為血分之另一證型，重點在於清血熱、止血。《中醫基礎學》，Maciocia，2015年，第757、762、770、773、777、784頁"
