      "exp_en": "Meeting point of the Governing and Yang Linking vessels, sea of marrow point, window of heaven point. DU-16 (fengfu) is an important point in the treatment of either exterior or interior wind disorders. If exterior wind attacks the body there will be chills, fever, body aches and sweating (if the qi is deficient). If Liver wind moves up there will be dizziness, blurred vision, headache, and wind stroke. In exterior wind DU-16 (fengfu) expels wind from the surface of the body and in interior wind DU-16 (fengfu) descends the pathogenic wind. As a sea of marrow point, DU-16 (fengfu) nourishes the brain and can be used to treat symptoms of marrow deficiency such as dizziness, tinnitus, lower leg pain, poor vision, indolence, and desire to sleep a lot. DU-16 (fengfu) is a main point that has an effect on the head and neck, treating such disorders as headache and neck problems. Since DU-16 (fengfu) enters the brain and a branch of du mai enters the Heart, DU-16 (fengfu) can calm the spirit (mania, always talking and cannot rest, sadness, fear, fright, palpitations). A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 548",
      "exp_hant": "此為督脈與陽維脈之交會穴，亦為髓海穴、天窗穴之一。風府是治療外風或內風病症的重要穴位。若外風侵襲人體，會出現惡寒、發熱、身痛及（氣虛時）自汗；若肝風上擾，則會出現頭暈、視物模糊、頭痛及中風。屬外風者，風府可袪除體表之風；屬內風者，風府則能平息內動之風邪。作為髓海穴，風府能養腦，可用於治療髓海不足之症狀，如頭暈、耳鳴、小腿痛、視力減退、倦怠及嗜睡。風府亦為影響頭頸的主要穴位，可治療頭痛及頸部病症。由於風府與腦相通，且督脈之分支入心，故風府能安神（治療狂躁、多言不止、悲傷、恐懼、驚悸、心悸）。《針灸經典手冊》，Deadman，第2版，第548頁"
