      "exp_en": "From the Western framework, this is chronic fatigue syndrome (CFS) which can be due to excess (intense muscle aches, thick tongue coating, full pulse) or deficiency (absent or mild muscle aches, thin or no tongue coating, weak pulse). True CFS is characterized by five essential symptoms: chronic fatigue, brain-memory changes, pronounced muscle aches, and recurrent flu-like symptoms (sore throat, swollen glands). The TCM causes of CFS are: 1) unresolved pathogenic factors (most often dampness) lodging in the interior, 2) latent internal incubating heat that start as external pathogenic factors (wind-cold/wind-heat) entering the interior without any of the initial symptoms of external attack, 3) shao yang pattern where the pathogenetic factor becomes half interior and half exterior, 4) yin fire which results from a deficiency of Original Qi, 5) deficiency of Qi, Yang, Blood, or yin with involvement of the Lungs, Spleen, Liver, and Kidneys. The original point Rx focused on strengthening the Qi by tonifying the Spleen and Lung. Actually the fatigue was an excess condition arising from an unresolved and internally lodged damp-heat after the meningitis, a febrile disease. The symptoms pointing to damp-heat are fatigue, heavy limbs, tired muscles, thirst (heat stronger than damp), overweight, night sweats (excess heat steaming the dampness) sticky taste, poor memory and concentration, vaginal discharge, sticky (dampness) and yellow (heat) tongue coating, and slippery pulse. The new treatment was to focus at first expelling damp-heat: SP-3 resolved dampness particularly from the brain. LI-11 and DU-14 clear damp-heat with DU-14 being especially effective in clearing chronic and hidden lingering heat. SP-9 and REN-9 transform dampness. TB-7 relieves muscle pain especially that which is due to heat. Other points that could have been used are SP-6 and BL-22 to resolve dampness and ST-8 to treat dampness in the head. The Rx with KI-3 focuses on dampness with Kidney deficiency. The Rx with ST-40 focuses on resolving damp-phlegm only. The Rx with REN-17 focuses on Lung yin Deficiency. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 1149, 1151, 1162",
      "exp_hant": "從西醫角度而言，此為慢性疲勞症候群（CFS），可分為實證（肌肉劇烈痠痛、舌苔厚膩、脈實）或虛證（肌肉痠痛輕微或缺乏、舌苔薄少甚至無苔、脈弱）。真正的慢性疲勞症候群具有五項核心症狀：慢性疲勞、腦力與記憶變化、明顯肌肉痠痛，以及反覆出現的類流感症狀（喉嚨痛、腺體腫大）。慢性疲勞症候群的中醫病因包括：1）未清解之邪氣（多為濕邪）滯留於裡；2）由外感邪氣（風寒／風熱）內傳而未見初期外感症狀所形成的伏邪內熱；3）邪氣半表半裡之少陽證；4）因元氣虧虛所致之陰火；5）肺、脾、肝、腎所涉及之氣、陽、血、陰虧虛。原本的處方著重於健脾補肺以益氣。然而，此患者的疲勞實際上是一種實證，源於腦膜炎（一種熱病）之後未清解、內伏之濕熱。提示濕熱的症狀包括：疲勞、肢體沉重、肌肉痠軟、口渴（熱重於濕）、體胖、盜汗（濕熱蒸騰所致）、口中黏膩感、記憶與注意力減退、陰道分泌物增多，以及黏膩（濕）而黃（熱）之舌苔與滑脈。新的治療方向首先著重於清化濕熱：太白能化濕，尤其針對腦部之濕；曲池與大椎能清濕熱，其中大椎對於清解慢性、深伏之熱邪特別有效；陰陵泉與水分能化濕；會宗則能緩解肌肉疼痛，尤其是熱邪所致者。其他可選用的穴位包括三陰交與三焦俞以化濕，以及頭維以治療頭部濕邪。以太谿為主的處方著重於腎虛兼濕；以豐隆為主的處方僅著重於化痰濕；以膻中為主的處方則著重於肺陰虛。《中醫臨證備要》，Maciocia，2008年，第1149、1151、1162頁"
    },
