        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "DU-3 (yao yang guan), BL-54 (zhi bian), BL-22 (san jiao shu), SP-9 (yin ling quan)",
          "hant": "腰陽關、秩邊、三焦俞、陰陵泉",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "DU-4 (ming men), BL-40 (wei zhong), BL-54 (zhi bian), BL-23 (shen shu)",
          "hant": "命門、委中、秩邊、腎俞",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "KI-3 (tai xi), BL-23 (shen shu), DU-4 (ming men), moxa box on lower back",
          "hant": "太谿、腎俞、命門、腰部灸盒溫灸",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The 8-Principles diagnosis External (Channel-Collateral), Cold, Excess. The etiology is Cold-Damp. The channel pattern is Cold-Damp Retention in the Tai Yang and Du Mai Channels. The treatment principle is Remove Cold-Damp from the Channels-Collaterals. DU-3 removes obstruction from the Governing Vessel locally and alleviates lower back pain by expelling Dampness and Cold. BL-54 is a strong point in removing obstructions from the foot tai yang channel and treats lower back and limb symptoms. Because these two points did not adequately address the retention of Dampness, BL-22 and SP-9 were added. The qi of the Triple Burner accumulates at BL-22 which has an influence on the metabolism of qi and water. Dampness obstructs qi flow which then disorders water metabolism. BL-22 is also a local point for the back pain. SP-9 removes accumulated Dampness and strengthens the Spleen. The other prescriptions tend to target local and near local points to the back pain and treat the Kidneys. Though there are symptoms that can indicate deficient Kidneys (chronic history of back pain and pale tongue), there was no indication that the pulse was either forceless or with force. Though the pulse was thin (usually deficiency) it can also indicate the presence of Dampness as the Dampness is blocking the qi and Blood flow and the Dampness accumulated in the tissues surrounding the blood vessels causes pressure thereby reducing the pulse diameter. Plus, in back pain arising from Kidney deficiency the pain would have been more continuous and not episodic and the general condition of the patient would have been one of weakness. DU-26 is more for acute back pain. The vital signs (BP, respiration, body temp, pulse rate) are normal as is the lower extremity sensory exam. Reflexes are graded from 0-4 with 0 = no reflexes, 1 = present with reinforcement, 2 = normal, 3 = increased but normal. And 4 = markedly hyperactive. Acupuncture Patterns and Practice, Eastland Press, 1993, Xuemai and Jingyi, Pages 83-87",
      "exp_hant": "八綱辨證為表證（經絡）、寒證、實證。病因為寒濕。經絡證型為寒濕滯留於太陽經與督脈。治療原則為袪除經絡中的寒濕。腰陽關能疏通督脈局部阻滯，並藉由袪濕散寒緩解下背疼痛；秩邊則是疏通足太陽經阻滯的要穴，能治療下背與下肢症狀。由於此二穴未能充分處理濕邪滯留的問題，故加入三焦俞與陰陵泉。三焦之氣匯聚於三焦俞，能影響氣與水液之代謝；濕邪阻礙氣機運行，進而擾亂水液代謝；三焦俞同時也是治療背痛的局部穴位。陰陵泉能袪除蓄積之濕邪並健脾。其餘處方多著重於局部及鄰近背痛部位的穴位，並兼顧補腎。雖然部分症狀（慢性背痛病史、舌淡）可能提示腎虛，但並無脈象無力或有力之明確描述。雖然脈細（通常提示虛證），但也可能提示濕邪存在，因濕邪阻滯氣血運行，且濕邪蓄積於血管周圍組織會造成壓迫，使脈管口徑變窄。此外，若下背痛源於腎虛，疼痛通常會較為持續而非陣發性，且患者整體狀況會呈現虛弱之象。人中則較適用於急性背痛。生命徵象（血壓、呼吸、體溫、脈搏）皆正常，下肢感覺檢查亦正常。反射分級為0至4級：0為無反射，1為需加強誘發才出現，2為正常，3為增強但仍屬正常範圍，4為明顯亢進。《針灸證治》，Eastland出版社，1993年，血脈與經義篇，第83-87頁"
    },
