          "hant": "中脘、氣海、足三里",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "DU-14 (da zhui), TB-5 (wai guan), DU-9 (zhi yang)",
          "hant": "大椎、外關、至陽",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The 8-Principles diagnosis is Exterior, Interior (mainly exterior), Excess. According to etiology, the external pattern is Invasion of Superficial Tissues by Pathogenic Cold-Damp. According to zang fu the internal pattern involves the Impairment of Stomach-Spleen Qi by Pathogenic Dampness. The treatment principle is to Expel Pathogenic Cold-Damp and Transform Dampness and Harmonize the Middle Burner. DU-14, the meeting point of the seven yang channels, strengthens the wei qi to expel pathogenic factors. TB-5, the meeting point of the TB and yang linking vessel, improves qi flow in the Triple Burner thereby improving yang qi circulation on the surface of the body helping to push out pathogenic cold and damp. Also, as the Triple Burner regulates water metabolism, TB-5 will help remove internal dampness. As a local point, GB-20 regulates the qi of the head, treats headache and a heavy head sensation. DU-9 promotes the circulation of yang qi to remove Dampness. DU-9 also harmonizes the Spleen-Stomach because it is actually functions as a local point and helps to treat heavy limbs and abdominal symptoms. As the body returned to normal, there was no longer a need to expel pathogenic factors from the surface of the body. Now the treatment focused internally on strengthening the Spleen-Stomach to resolve Dampness. SP-9 tonifies the Spleen to remove excess Dampness. ST-36 helps to strengthen the Middle Burner to and is indicated when there is congested fluids, dampness, and phlegm in the presence of qi or yang xu. When Dampness is transformed, the appetite will return to normal. Together SP-9 and ST-36 strengthen Earth to control Water. REN-11 is selected as a local point helping to harmonize the Stomach to improve appetite. The combination of REN-12 (zhong wan), REN-6 (qi haid), ST-36 (zu san li) aim at strengthening Stomach and Spleen qi. Though there are symptoms (poor appetite, loose stools, pale tongue with white coating) that could point to Spleen Qi xu, but these acute symptoms are caused by Dampness obstructing the qi of the Stomach and Spleen. Blood pressure, pulse, CBC, RBC are all within normal ranges. Acupuncture Patterns and Practice, Eastland Press, 1993, Xuemai and Jingyi, Pages 7-10",
      "exp_hant": "八綱辨證為表證、裡證（以表為主）、實證。就病因而言，此表證屬寒濕邪氣侵犯肌表；就臟腑而言，此裡證則屬濕邪損傷脾胃之氣。治療原則為袪除寒濕邪氣、化濕並調和中焦。大椎為手足三陽經與督脈之交會穴，能強化衛氣以袪除邪氣；外關為三焦經與陽維脈之交會穴，能促進三焦氣機運行，進而改善體表陽氣循環，助於驅散寒濕邪氣；此外，因三焦主司水液代謝，外關亦能協助袪除內在濕邪。風池作為局部穴位，能調理頭部之氣，治療頭痛及頭部沉重感。至陽能促進陽氣運行以袪濕，且因其本身亦具局部治療作用，能協助處理肢體沉重與腹部症狀，兼能調和脾胃。隨著病情恢復正常，已不再需要袪除體表邪氣，此時治療轉為著重於內在健脾胃以化濕。陰陵泉能健脾以袪除過盛之濕邪；足三里能強健中焦，適用於氣虛或陽虛兼有水濕痰飲停滯者。濕邪一旦得化，食欲便可恢復正常。陰陵泉與足三里合用，能健脾（土）以制水。建里作為局部穴位，能和胃以改善食欲。中脘、氣海與足三里之組合則旨在健脾胃之氣。雖然部分症狀（食欲不振、大便溏瀉、舌淡苔白）可能提示脾氣虛，但此患者的急性症狀實為濕邪阻滯脾胃之氣所致。血壓、脈搏、全血球計數、紅血球數皆在正常範圍。《針灸證治》，Eastland出版社，1993年，血脈與經義篇，第7-10頁"
    },
