      ],
      "exp_en": "The Stomach muscle meridian does not connect with the Spleen muscle meridian. However, the latter does connect with the spine. This explains why points such as ST-36 and SP-3 can treat spinal problems. The Stomach muscle meridian only connects with the Gall Bladder, Large Intestine, and Bladder muscle meridians. The Stomach muscle meridian begins on the three middle toes, follows the anterior aspect of the leg, binds above the genitals, binds at the hip and connects with the spine, connects with the neck to join with the eye and in front of the ear. The Spleen muscle meridian spreads to the chest and then goes to adhere to the spine. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 128; The meridians of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 306, 297",
      "exp_hant": "胃經經筋並不與脾經經筋相連。然而，脾經經筋確實與脊椎相連，這說明了為何足三里（ST-36）與太白（SP-3）等穴位能治療脊椎問題。胃經經筋僅與膽經、大腸經與膀胱經的經筋相連。胃經經筋起於中間三趾，沿小腿前側上行，結於生殖器上方，結於髖部並與脊椎相連，再上行至頸部與眼睛及耳前相會。脾經經筋則散布於胸部，再附著於脊椎。《針灸大成手冊》，Deadman著，第2版，第128頁；《經絡學》(The Meridians of Acupuncture)，Maciocia著，2006年版，第306、297頁"
