      "exp_en": "These vessels originate between the two kidneys, go to the uterus, and then flow down to REN-1 (hui yin) from which the respective pathways of the vessels diverge. The bao luo is the uterus channel. REN-1 is the starting point for the ren mai. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 808; 2005 Edition, page 839",
      "exp_hant": "這些脈皆起於兩腎之間，行至子宮，再下行至會陰（REN-1），並由此處分別走出各自的循行路線。胞絡即子宮之脈絡。會陰是任脈的起始點。《中醫基礎學》，Maciocia著，2015年版，第808頁；2005年版，第839頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 225,
      "question_en": "Three months ago a 37 year-old male had a cerebral thrombosis that affected the left side of his brain. After the stroke he was paralyzed on the right side of his body. After physical therapy he was able to move his right side and could walk with a cane. However he had problems with his speech. He could respond when he was questioned but his answers did not make sense. When asked his name he would say \"Mary\". When asked how old he was he would say \"19\". When asked to count he would correctly count up to five but then skipped to 16 and then 20. His tongue was purple with a thick-white coating. His pulses were slippery and wiry. Which scalp acupuncture area(s) would you treat?",
      "question_hant": "三個月前，一名37歲男性發生腦血栓，影響大腦左側。中風後，他的身體右側出現癱瘓。經過物理治療後，他已能活動右側身體，並可拄拐杖行走。然而，他出現言語方面的問題。當被問及問題時他能作出回應，但回答內容卻不合邏輯。當被問及姓名時，他會回答「瑪麗」。當被問及年齡時，他會回答「19歲」。當被要求數數時，他能正確數到5，但接著會跳到16，然後又跳到20。舌質紫暗，苔厚白。脈滑而弦。您會治療哪個（些）頭皮針治療區？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Speech area I",
          "hant": "言語一區",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Speech area II",
          "hant": "言語二區",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Speech area II and the lower 1/5 of the Motor area",
          "hant": "言語二區與運動區下1/5",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Speech area III",
          "hant": "言語三區",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This type of aphasia is called Wernicke's aphasia. SPEECH AREA III overlies Wernicke's area in the brain. This type of aphasia is also called receptive aphasia, sensory aphasia, or posterior aphasia. In this type of aphasia the patient has difficulty understanding written and spoken language. It is an inability to understand written or spoken language due to disease of the auditory and visual word centers. Speech Area III is located on a horizontal line 1.5 cm superior to the ear apex and begins at the midpoint of the Vertigo and Hearing area and runs 4 cm posterior. The direction of needling can go posterior to anterior or anterior to posterior, needling the entire area. Treat this point bilaterally and rotate the needle 200 times per minute for 1-3 minutes, every 10 minutes for a total of 30-45 minutes. Or you can use electrical stimulation. It is helpful to have the patient talk during treatment. If during the treatment the patient experiences heat, cold, heaviness, distention, or electricity moving in the throat and tongue, then it is a good sign that the treatment will produce result. SPEECH AREA I treats motor aphasia. This type of aphasia is called motor aphasia, also called Broca's aphasia as it corresponds to Broca's area A in the brain which is the area that controls the muscles of tongue and mouth that form speech. In Broca's aphasia there is an inability to speak. The patient understands written and spoken words but has difficulty uttering the words. Speech area I overlaps the lower 2/5 of the Motor area. This area treats dysarthia, dysphonia, or motor aphasia after a stroke or brain injury to the area that control the muscles of speech. This area is needled bilaterally for motor aphasia, needling from the upper to the lower part and penetrating the entire line. SPEECH AREA II treats nominal aphasia in which the individual has word retrieval failures and cannot express the words they want to say. Nominal aphasia which is is a type of aphasia where an individual has word retrieval failures and cannot express the words they want to say. It is an inability to name objects, qualities, or conditions. Speech area II is located by finding the parietal eminence. It is a line parallel to the anterior-posterior line 2 cm posteriorly and runs 2 cm. Direction of needling can go posterior to anterior or anterior to posterior, needling the entire area. Chinese Scalp Acupuncture, Jason Hao, Lingzhi Hao, 2017, page 55, 59, 160",
      "exp_hant": "這種失語症稱為魏尼克氏失語症（Wernicke's aphasia）。言語三區對應大腦中的魏尼克區。這種失語症又稱為感覺性失語症、聽覺性失語症或後部失語症。此類失語症患者理解書面與口語語言有困難，是由於掌管聽覺與視覺文字中樞病變，導致無法理解書寫或口說語言。言語三區位於耳尖上方1.5公分的水平線上，起自暈聽區中點，向後延伸4公分。進針方向可由後向前或由前向後，針刺整個區域。此區應雙側治療，每分鐘捻轉200次，每次1-3分鐘，每10分鐘捻轉一次，總計治療30-45分鐘，亦可使用電刺激。治療期間讓患者說話有助於療效。若治療過程中患者感到咽喉與舌部有發熱、發冷、沈重、脹感或如電流竄動之感，則是療效良好的徵兆。言語一區治療運動性失語症。這類失語症稱為運動性失語症，又稱布洛卡氏失語症（Broca's aphasia），對應大腦中控制構成言語之舌與口部肌肉的布洛卡區。布洛卡氏失語症患者無法言語，雖能理解書寫與口說文字，但發音表達困難。言語一區與運動區下2/5重疊。此區治療中風或腦部損傷影響言語肌肉控制區後所致的構音障礙、發聲障礙或運動性失語症。治療運動性失語症時應雙側針刺此區，由上而下貫穿整條線。言語二區治療命名性失語症，患者出現詞語提取困難，無法說出想表達的詞語。命名性失語症是一種患者詞語提取失敗、無法表達所欲言詞的失語症，即無法為物品、性質或狀態命名。言語二區的定位方法為找出頂骨結節，取與前後正中線平行、其後方2公分處的一條線，長約2公分。進針方向可由後向前或由前向後，針刺整個區域。《中醫頭皮針》(Chinese Scalp Acupuncture)，Jason Hao、Lingzhi Hao著，2017年版，第55、59、160頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 226,
      "question_en": "Five years ago a 29 year-old female patient had hepatitis with jaundice. She also had nausea, poor appetite, abdominal distension, and pain in the right hypochondriac area. That is when she first developed occipital headaches which were continuous for one month. When the hepatitis resolved, all the symptoms were alleviated except for the headaches which then were on the right temporal area. These headaches were worse when she ate sweet and cheese and worsened with menstruation. The headaches were not affected by weather changes. The headaches had a sharp pain and were accompanied with nausea and vomiting. During the headaches she was also sensitive to noises. The duration of the headaches ranges from a couple of hours to a few days. Analgesics relieved the headaches but not all the time. During the past couple of months the migraines have become more severe. During the past seven days she has had a continuous migraine which analgesics did not relieve. She has abdominal distention, insomnia, and no appetite. Her menstrual cycle is irregular and is taking hormones to help regulate it. During the past year she has gained 33 pounds even though she eats little food. Bowel movements and urination are normal. The tongue body has a normal color with a white and slightly thick coating. The pulse is sunken and a little wiry. Blood Pressure is 128/74, Pulse 70, Respirations 18, Temperature 98.8 F. ESR is within normal limits. MRI of the brain with contrast shows deviation patchy meningeal enhancement ipsilateral to the migraine. She is treated with tai yang on the right side, GB-20 (feng chi), TB-5 (wai guan), REN-12 (zhong wan), SP-9 (yin ling quan), and ST-36 (zu san li). She was treated two times per week. After the first treatment her headaches were gone but returned mid-week but mild. She still had nausea. She was treated with the same prescription another three times after which her digestive symptoms improved but still had mild headaches for short periods. She complained of her sleep being unsound. What would you add to the prescription?",
      "question_hant": "五年前，一名29歲女性患者曾患有黃疸型肝炎，並伴有噁心、食慾不振、腹脹以及右脅肋疼痛。就在那時，她首次出現持續一個月的枕部頭痛。肝炎痊癒後，除頭痛外其餘症狀皆已緩解，而頭痛則轉移到右側顳部。這些頭痛在食用甜食與起司後會加重，並在月經期間惡化，但不受天氣變化影響。頭痛呈刺痛性質，伴隨噁心與嘔吐。發作時她對聲音也較為敏感。頭痛持續時間從數小時到數天不等。止痛藥可緩解頭痛，但並非每次都有效。在過去幾個月中，偏頭痛逐漸加重。過去七天她持續偏頭痛發作，止痛藥也無法緩解。她有腹脹、失眠與食慾不振。月經週期不規則，正在服用荷爾蒙藥物以調節月經。過去一年她體重增加了33磅，儘管進食量很少。大便與小便正常。舌體顏色正常，舌苔薄白略厚。脈沉略弦。血壓128/74，脈搏70，呼吸18，體溫98.8華氏度。ESR（紅血球沉降率）在正常範圍內。腦部顯影劑MRI顯示與偏頭痛同側有斑塊狀腦膜增強現象。她接受右側太陽穴、風池（GB-20）、外關（TB-5）、中脘（REN-12）、陰陵泉（SP-9）與足三里（ST-36）治療，每週治療兩次。第一次治療後頭痛消失，但週中又復發，程度較輕，仍有噁心。以相同處方再治療三次後，消化道症狀改善，但仍有短暫的輕微頭痛。她主訴睡眠不安穩。您會在處方中加入什麼？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
