        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "asthma, chronic diarrhea, and indigestion",
          "hant": "氣喘、慢性腹瀉與消化不良",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "abdominal pain, vomiting, and prolonged dysentery",
          "hant": "腹痛、嘔吐與久痢",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "impotence, Kidney yang deficiency, premature ejaculation",
          "hant": "陽痿、腎陽虛、早洩",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Salt has a cold temperature and enters the Stomach, Kidneys, and Small Intestine channels. Taken internally, salt clears heat, cools blood, and resolves toxins. Salt on moxa is selected to return the yang and stem counterflow or rebellious qi, treat acute abdominal pain, vomiting, diarrhea, and dysentery. Moxa on salt is most often use on the navel (REN-8) but can also be used on other points. Fill the navel with salt to the level of the surrounding skin. You can place a slice of ginger over the salt and then burn the moxa cones on top. If a ginger slice is not used then the heat can melt the salt and scald the skin. If you do not use ginger, remove the moxa when the patient says it is too hot. If the navel is not very deep, use dough made with flour and water (or use a noodle). Make a small ring around the navel with the dough or noodle. Then fill the ring with salt and place a slice of ginger on top. CAM, 3rd Edition, page 364; CAM, 4th Edition, page 440; Moxibustion: A Modern Clinical Handbook, Wilcox, 2018, page 81",
      "exp_hant": "鹽性寒，入胃、腎、小腸經。內服時，鹽能清熱、涼血、解毒。隔鹽灸的選用目的在於回陽、平息氣的逆亂，治療急性腹痛、嘔吐、腹瀉與痢疾。隔鹽灸最常施於神闕（REN-8），亦可用於其他穴位。將鹽填滿肚臍，與周圍皮膚齊平。可在鹽上放一片薑，再於薑片上放置艾炷施灸。若不使用薑片，熱度可能會使鹽融化並燙傷皮膚；若未使用薑片，應在患者感覺過熱時立即移除艾炷。若肚臍不夠深，可用麵粉加水製成的麵團（或麵條）圍成一圈放在肚臍周圍，再於圈內填滿鹽，並在鹽上放一片薑。CAM，第3版，第364頁；CAM，第4版，第440頁；《艾灸療法：現代臨床手冊》(Moxibustion: A Modern Clinical Handbook)，Wilcox著，2018年版，第81頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 239,
      "question_en": "An 8 year-old child has a fever, cough, body aches, headache, light sensitivity, lethargy, stiff neck, and a red rash. Which signs confirm an emergency situation?",
      "question_hant": "一名8歲兒童出現發燒、咳嗽、全身痠痛、頭痛、畏光、嗜睡、頸部僵硬與紅疹。哪些徵象可確認這是緊急狀況？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Spurling maneuver and blanching rash",
          "hant": "史柏林測試（Spurling maneuver）與可褪色皮疹",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Brudzinski sign and non-blanching rash",
          "hant": "布魯辛斯基氏徵象（Brudzinski sign）與不可褪色皮疹",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "light sensitivity and fever of 102F",
          "hant": "畏光與華氏102度發燒",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "fever of 102F",
          "hant": "華氏102度發燒",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The clinical picture points to meningitis and can be confirmed by Brudzinski sign and a non-blanching rash. Rashes can be divided into blanching and non-blanching. The group called blanching disappears when pressed. The group called non-blanching does not disappear when pressed. A non-blanching red rash is often a feature in meningitis. The Brudzinski neck sign is a clinical sign in which the forced flexion of the neck elicits a reflex flexion of the hips. In this sign the knees spontaneously move toward the torso when the neck of the head of the patient is moved forward toward the chest (flexion). This sign is elicited in patients with meningitis or subarachnoid haemorrhage. Spurling maneuver is an exam that helps diagnose neck pain by gently turning head of the patient and gently applying pressure to reproduce radiating, nerve-related neck pain. Meningitis is an inflammation of the meninges which are membranes surrounding the brain or the spinal cord. The inflammation is usually due to a bacteria (bacterial meningitis) or a virus (viral meningitis) but can arise from cancer, a drug reaction or an auto-immune disorder. Meningitis, especially bacterial meningitis, is potentially life-threatening. It can progress to neurologic problems, brain damage, and death. IMPORTANT: It is not possible to know which type of meningitis a patient might have by the clinical picture. The patient needs to have an urgent referral to make that determination via diagnostic tests, especially the required spinal tap test. BACTERIAL MENINGITIS: Classic symptoms of bacterial meningitis in children older than 1 year are fever, lethargy, a non-blanching rash, mental confusion, a headache, light sensitivity, neck stiffness, seizures. In the Brudzinski's sign the knees of the patient are automatically brought up toward the torso when the patient's neck is bent forward by the doctor. This is called the Brudzinski sign. The Brudzinski neck sign is a clinical sign in which the forced flexion of the neck elicits a reflex flexion of the hips. It is elicited in patients with meningitis and subarachnoid haemorrhage. Call 911 for transport. VIRAL MENINGITIS: Viral meningitis is less serious than bacterial meningitis. It frequently remains undiagnosed because its symptoms are similar to the common flu. Symptoms of viral meningitis are similar to the flu (fever, muscle aches, cough, headache but some might have one or more the symptoms of bacterial meningitis but in a very mild form such as stiff neck, headache, nausea, lethargy, sleepiness, light sensitivity, confusion, irritability. Patients of any age can get viral meningitis. Some individuals, however, have a higher risk (children under five, immunocompromised patients). Most patients with mild viral meningitis usually get better on their own within 7 to 10 days. Call 911 for transport if any type of meningitis is suspected. A doctor can determine the cause (bacterial or viral) and the best treatment. The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 172; www.webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "此臨床表現指向腦膜炎，可透過布魯辛斯基氏徵象與不可褪色皮疹加以確認。皮疹可分為可褪色與不可褪色兩類：可褪色皮疹在按壓時會消失，不可褪色皮疹則在按壓後不會消失。不可褪色的紅疹常是腦膜炎的特徵之一。布魯辛斯基氏頸部徵象是一種臨床徵象，指強迫頸部前屈時會誘發髖部的反射性屈曲，也就是當醫師將患者頭頸向胸部前屈時，患者的膝蓋會自發性地向軀幹靠近。此徵象常見於腦膜炎或蛛網膜下腔出血的患者。史柏林測試則是一種協助診斷頸部疼痛的檢查方式，透過輕輕轉動患者頭部並施加輕微壓力，以誘發放射性、與神經相關的頸部疼痛。腦膜炎是包覆腦部與脊髓之腦脊膜的發炎，通常由細菌（細菌性腦膜炎）或病毒（病毒性腦膜炎）引起，但也可能源於癌症、藥物反應或自體免疫疾病。腦膜炎——尤其是細菌性腦膜炎——具有潛在致命性，可能演變為神經系統問題、腦損傷甚至死亡。重要提醒：僅憑臨床表現無法判斷患者所患為何種腦膜炎，患者需緊急轉診，透過診斷檢查（尤其是必要的脊髓穿刺檢查）加以確認。細菌性腦膜炎：1歲以上兒童細菌性腦膜炎的典型症狀包括發燒、嗜睡、不可褪色皮疹、意識混亂、頭痛、畏光、頸部僵硬與抽搐。在布魯辛斯基氏徵象中，當醫師將患者頸部向前彎曲時，患者膝蓋會自動向軀幹靠攏，此即所謂布魯辛斯基氏徵象。布魯辛斯基氏頸部徵象是一種臨床徵象，指強迫頸部前屈會誘發髖部的反射性屈曲，常見於腦膜炎與蛛網膜下腔出血患者。應撥打911請求送醫。病毒性腦膜炎：病毒性腦膜炎的嚴重程度較細菌性腦膜炎輕，常因症狀與普通流感相似而未被診斷出來。病毒性腦膜炎的症狀類似流感（發燒、肌肉痠痛、咳嗽、頭痛），但部分患者可能會出現一項或多項輕微程度的細菌性腦膜炎症狀，如頸部僵硬、頭痛、噁心、嗜睡、想睡、畏光、意識混亂與易怒。任何年齡的患者皆可能罹患病毒性腦膜炎，但某些族群風險較高（五歲以下兒童、免疫功能低下患者）。大多數輕度病毒性腦膜炎患者通常可在7至10天內自行康復。若懷疑任何類型的腦膜炎，皆應撥打911安排送醫。醫師可判斷病因（細菌或病毒性）並給予最適當的治療。《輔助療法從業者紅旗轉診指南》(The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals)，Stephenson著，2013年版，第172頁；www.webmd.com"
    },
