      "exp_en": "The Spleen muscle channel follows the medial aspect of the leg, converges at the genitals, binds at the navel, binds at the ribs and spreads to the chest, and adheres to the spine. The Spleen muscle channel adhering to the spine explains the selection of SP-3 in the treatment of lumbar pain. The Spleen muscle channel connects with the Liver and Kidney muscle channels. The Liver muscle channel follows the medial aspect of the leg and connects with the genitals where it ends. The Liver luo-connecting channel also connects to the genitals. This shows the importance of the Liver channels in the treatment of genital problems. The Liver muscle channel connects with the Spleen muscle channel at the genitals. The Kidney muscle channel travels the medial aspect of the leg, binds at the genitals, ascends to the inner aspect of the spine, and binds at the occipital bone. The Kidney muscle channel connects with the Spleen and Bladder muscle channels. The Kidney muscle channel joins with the Bladder muscle channel at the occiput. The Kidney luo-connecting channel also connects at the nape of neck. This shows the importance of the Bladder and Kidney channels in treating the spine and back of neck. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 180, 332, 471; The Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 297-300",
      "exp_hant": "脾經之經筋循行於下肢內側，會聚於生殖器，結於臍部，結於肋部並散布於胸部，最後附著於脊椎。脾經之經筋附著於脊椎，說明了為何在治療腰痛時會選用太白（SP-3）。脾經之經筋與肝經、腎經之經筋相連。肝經之經筋循行於下肢內側，並連結至生殖器並終止於此。肝經之絡脈亦連結至生殖器，這顯示肝經在治療生殖器問題上的重要性。肝經之經筋於生殖器處與脾經之經筋相連。腎經之經筋循行於下肢內側，結於生殖器，沿脊柱內側上行，並結於枕骨。腎經之經筋與脾經及膀胱經之經筋相連，並於後枕部與膀胱經之經筋交會。腎經之絡脈亦連結於項部，這顯示膀胱經與腎經在治療脊椎與項背部問題上的重要性。《針灸大成手冊》，Deadman著，第2版，第180、332、471頁；《經絡學》，Maciocia著，2006年版，第297-300頁"
