    {
      "number": 291,
      "question_en": "A 55 year-old patient with a history of myocardial infarctions complains of chest pain and dizziness. What signs can indicate the early stage of a cardiogenic shock and require urgent referral and care?",
      "question_hant": "一名55歲患者有心肌梗塞病史，主訴胸痛與頭暈。下列何種徵象可能顯示心因性休克的早期階段，需緊急轉診與照護？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "resting pulse rate of 150",
          "hant": "靜息脈搏150次/分",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "resting respiratory rate of 12",
          "hant": "靜息呼吸速率每分鐘12次",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "resting pulse rate of 55",
          "hant": "靜息脈搏55次/分",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "resting respiratory rate of 5",
          "hant": "靜息呼吸速率每分鐘5次",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Within the context of a heart attack, an early stage of cardiogenic shock shows as a rapid (140 to 250 bpm) and strong pulse. This type of pulse rate is an indication of superventricular tachycardia or atrial fibrillation. This type of pulse is experienced by the patient as a pounding heart (palpitations). This is high priority red flag. A very weak and slow pulse can occur at a later stage of cardiogenic shock. It indicates that the heart is slowly ceasing to function as a result of pumping too hard. This is also high priority red flag. Cardiogenic shock is caused by the failure of the pumping action of the heart to circulate blood, either caused by heart muscle damage arising from a heart attack, heart valve problems, congestive heart failure, or irregular heart rhythm. Simply stated, cardiogenic shock is caused by the inadequate pumping of the heart due to heart disease or heart attack. Symptoms of cardiogenic shock Symptoms include: fainting, extremely low blood pressure, cold feet and hands, difficulty breathing, chest pain, pale skin, confusion, rapid breathing rate. The normal respiratory rate for an adult can be, according to different sources, 12 to 16 or 10 to 20 breaths per minute. In the initial stage of shock, there can be a rapid and respiratory rate as the body tries to compensate for the lack of blood flow to the body. There can also be a strong pulse but in the in the early stages but in the later stages of shock the pulse will be weak. For an adult, a resting pulse rate between 60 and 100 is considered normal. For an athlete a rate of 40 can be normal. A very slow pulse rate of 40 to 50 is a red flag for shock due to heart failure or arrhythmia. A severe heart attack that initiates the shock response can proceed to heart failure. That is, what started with a rapid heart rate in the early stages of shock, due to a heart attack, can progress to a very low heart rate when the heart attacks worsens into heart failure. Cardiogenic shock can occur very quickly following a heart attack (chest pressure, shoulder pain, pain along jawline, SOB, dizziness, nausea). Cardiogenic shock is the leading cause of death for patients with acute heart attack who reach the hospital alive. The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 48, 164",
      "exp_hant": "在心肌梗塞的情境下，心因性休克的早期階段會出現快而有力的脈搏（每分鐘140至250次）。此種脈搏顯示為室上性心搏過速或心房顫動。患者會將此感受為心悸（心跳砰砰作響）。這是高優先度的警訊徵象。心因性休克的較晚期階段則可能出現極為微弱而緩慢的脈搏，顯示心臟因長期過度用力搏動而逐漸衰竭，這同樣是高優先度的警訊徵象。心因性休克是由於心臟幫浦功能衰竭、無法有效循環血液所致，其成因可能是心肌梗塞造成的心肌損傷、心瓣膜問題、鬱血性心臟衰竭或心律不整。簡言之，心因性休克是因心臟疾病或心肌梗塞導致心臟幫浦功能不足所引起。心因性休克的症狀包括：暈厥、血壓極低、手腳冰冷、呼吸困難、胸痛、皮膚蒼白、意識混亂、呼吸急促。成人正常呼吸速率依不同文獻，介於每分鐘12至16次或10至20次之間。在休克初期，身體為代償血流不足，呼吸速率可能會加快；早期階段脈搏也可能仍然有力，但到休克後期脈搏則會轉弱。成人靜息脈搏在每分鐘60至100次之間屬正常範圍，運動員則可低至每分鐘40次仍屬正常。若靜息脈搏極慢，介於每分鐘40至50次，則是心臟衰竭或心律不整所致休克的警訊。嚴重心肌梗塞引發休克反應後可能進展為心臟衰竭，也就是說，休克早期因心肌梗塞而出現的心跳過速，隨著心肌梗塞惡化為心臟衰竭，可能轉變為心跳過緩。心因性休克可在心肌梗塞（胸悶、肩痛、下顎痛、呼吸急促、頭暈、噁心）發生後迅速出現。心因性休克是到院時仍存活的急性心肌梗塞患者中最主要的死亡原因。(出處：The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals，Stephenson，2013年，第48、164頁)"
    },
