      "exp_en": "Garlic is acrid and warm. It dissipates swelling, transforms nodules, draws out toxins, and stops pain. Moxa with garlic can be selected to treat abscesses, sores that have not ulcerated, scrofula, inflamed lymph nodes, toxic swellings, consumption, abdominal lumps and accumulations, and warts. Garlic with moxa is often used in skin conditions and can be used in an area that is developing inflammation to help draw out the \"evil\" pathogen. Cut a slice of garlic around 0.5 cm (0.19 inch) thick. Single-headed garlic (not many cloves) with purplish skin is preferred but this type of garlic is native to China and not common in the West. Punch tiny holes with an acupuncture needle or toothpick on the garlic slice. Place a moxa cone with a wide base on the garlic slice. Remove the moxa cone when the patient experiences the heat as too hot. One usually burns seven cones on the garlic. The skin under the garlic should become flushed and red. Since garlic is an irritating substance, a blister can form so let the patient know that this is a possibility and get their consent. CAM, 3rd Edition, page 364; CAM, 4th Edition, page 440; Moxibustion: A Modern Clinical Handbook, Wilcox, 2018, page 80",
      "exp_hant": "大蒜辛溫，能消腫、化結、拔毒、止痛。隔蒜灸可用於治療癰疽、瘡瘍未潰者、瘰癧、淋巴結腫大發炎、毒性腫塊、癆病、腹部積聚以及疣。隔蒜灸常用於皮膚病症，亦可用於正在發炎的部位以助「邪氣」外透。作法為切一片約0.5公分（0.19英吋）厚的蒜片，以獨頭（非多瓣）、外皮呈紫色的大蒜為佳，但此類大蒜原產於中國，西方並不常見。以鍼或牙籤在蒜片上刺出細孔，再將底部較寬的艾炷置於蒜片上，當患者感到過熱時即移除艾炷，通常每次灸七壯。蒜片下的皮膚應呈現潮紅。由於大蒜具刺激性，可能起水皰，應事先告知患者此一可能性並取得其同意。(出處：CAM，第3版，第364頁；CAM，第4版，第440頁；Moxibustion: A Modern Clinical Handbook，Wilcox，2018年，第80頁)"
