      "question_en": "A 65 year-old female patient has chronic edema which first started on the feet and then moved to the whole body. She has sallow complexion, cold limbs, back pain, fatigue, poor appetite, a pale tongue, and a deep-thready pulse. She is treated with SP-9 (yin ling quan) and REN-9 (shui fen). For this treatment she wants you to focus on her facial puffiness from the edema. Which point would you add to your prescription?",
