    {
      "number": 309,
      "question_en": "A 37 year-old male has a recent ear infection. He has ear pain, fever, and purulent discharge from the right ear. He has a history of otitis media. His temperature is 101.2 degrees F. The right ear has yellowish fluid. The mastoid bone is very tender to the touch. What action would you take with this patient?",
      "question_hant": "一名37歲男性最近患有耳部感染，出現耳痛、發燒及右耳化膿性分泌物。他有中耳炎病史，體溫為華氏101.2度。右耳有黃色分泌物，乳突骨壓痛明顯。您應對此患者採取下列何種行動？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "semi-urgent referral to primary care physician",
          "hant": "半緊急轉診至基層照護醫師",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "have a friend transport patient to emergency department (ED)",
          "hant": "請朋友將患者送往急診室",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "call 911 for emergency transport",
          "hant": "撥打911緊急救護車轉送",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "treat patient with GB-12, GB-20, and TB-17",
          "hant": "以完骨、風池及翳風穴為患者施治",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is ear pain, ear drainage, fever, severe mastoid tenderness. Acute mastoiditis is assumed present until proven otherwise. Acute mastoiditis is a serious bacterial infection, often a complication of otitis media. The referral should be semi-urgent to the PCP or urgent care center if no PCP is available or directly to an ENT physician. If not treated, an extension of the infection can cause osteomyelitis, abscess, meningitis, or facial nerve/labyrinth destruction resulting in hearing loss. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 108-109",
      "exp_hant": "此警訊徵象為耳痛、耳漏、發燒及乳突骨明顯壓痛。應假設為急性乳突炎，直至排除此可能性為止。急性乳突炎是一種嚴重的細菌感染，常為中耳炎的併發症。轉診應採半緊急方式，轉至基層照護醫師或（若無基層照護醫師可就診）緊急照護中心，或直接轉診至耳鼻喉科醫師。若未治療，感染擴散可能導致骨髓炎、膿瘍、腦膜炎，或顏面神經／內耳迷路受損而造成聽力喪失。(出處：An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals，2012年，Anzaldua，第108-109頁)"
    },
    {
      "number": 310,
      "question_en": "A 42 year-old female has been receiving treatment for anxiety for the past three months. Her anxiety started when she and her husband separated. Her symptoms have included palpitations, chest oppression, a slight feeling of lump in the throat, frequent sighing, shortness of breath, poor appetite, nausea, and a pale complexion. The tongue has been pale-purple on the sides. The pulse has been slightly overflowing on the left-front position. She received treatment two times per week with the prescription PC-6 (nei guan), HT-7 (shen men), REN-17 (shan zhong), REN-14 (ju que), and ST-40 (feng long). Her symptoms diminished about 60%. A month after her last treatment, she returned to report she is now going through the divorce proceedings. Her anxiety is now worse particularly in the evening. She has been waking up in the middle of the night with a sense of panic. The chest oppression has now become a sense of pressure on the chest. The tongue is unchanged but the pulse is now choppy. What treatment will you now give?",
      "question_hant": "一名42歲女性因焦慮已接受治療三個月，其焦慮始於與丈夫分居之時。症狀包括心悸、胸悶、咽喉有異物梗阻感、頻頻嘆氣、氣短、食欲不振、噁心及面色蒼白。舌兩側淡紫，脈象左寸略見洪象。每週治療兩次，處方為內關、神門、膻中、巨闕及豐隆，症狀改善約六成。末次治療一個月後，她回診表示現正進行離婚程序，焦慮加重，尤以傍晚為甚，並常於半夜驚醒感到恐慌。胸悶感已轉為胸口有壓迫感。舌象未變，但脈象轉為澀脈。您現在應給予下列何種治療？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
