        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "HT-5 (tong li), PC-6 (nei guan), REN-15 (jiu wei), LR-3 (tai chong), SP-6 (san yin jiao)",
          "hant": "通里、內關、鳩尾、太衝、三陰交",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "PC-5 (jian shi), ST-40 (feng long), REN-15 (jiu wei), REN-12 (zhong wan), HT-8 (shao fu)",
          "hant": "間使、豐隆、鳩尾、中脘、少府",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "HT-7 (shen men), GB-40 (qiu xu), BL-15 (xin shu), REN-14 (ju que), ST-36 (zu san li)",
          "hant": "神門、丘墟、心俞、巨闕、足三里",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "There is no TCM term for anxiety. Traditionally, it has been attributed to \"Fear and Palpitations\" or \"Panic Throbbing\", the latter referring to panic attacks. The original presentation of symptoms and signs indicate Heart Qi stasis. Chest distention, sighing, feeling of lump in throat all indicate qi stasis. The palpitations point to involvement of the Heart. Heart qi stasis involved the chest and can cause slight shortness of breath. The complexion is pale not because of Qi/Blood xu but because the qi stasis prevents the Blood ascending to the face. The poor appetite and nausea is due to the Heart qi not descending due to stasis and impacting Stomach function. The tongue indicates that the qi stasis is beginning to impact Blood. An overflowing pulse on the left front position is a key sign for this pattern. PC-6 opens the chest, moves qi,and calms Shen. HT-7 regulates Heart qi and calms Shen. REN-17 moves the qi in the chest. REN-14 regulates the Heart and subdues rebellious Stomach qi. ST-40 is selected not to transform Phlegm but to open the chest. The second clinical presentation indicates a worsening of the condition from Heart Qi Stasis to Heart Blood Stasis due to the stress from the divorce. Blood stasis is characterized by symptoms being worse at night and sleep when Blood circulation slows down. HT-5 moves Heart blood and calms the Shen. PC-6 moves Heart Blood, opens the chest and calms the Shen. Like all the other yin luo-connecting points, HT-5 and PC-6 have the special function of treating emotional and psychological disorders. REN-15, luo point for ren mai, calms the Shen and opens the chest. REN-15 has a strong calming action in severe anxiety, worry, or fears. LR-3 invigorates the Blood by moving qi. SP-6 invigorates Blood and calms Shen by nourishing the yin. The Rx with KI-3 is for anxiety due to Kidney and Heart not Communicating. The Rx with GB-40 is for anxiety due to Heart and Gall Bladder Xu. The Rx with HT-8 is for anxiety due to Phlegm-Heat harassing the Heart. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 402; Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 506, 1141, 1142",
      "exp_hant": "中醫並無「焦慮」此一病名，傳統上多歸屬於「驚悸」，若指恐慌發作則稱為「怔忡」。此案例最初的症狀與體徵顯示為心氣鬱滯。胸悶、嘆氣、咽喉異物感皆為氣滯之表現，心悸則指出病位在心。心氣鬱滯影響胸部，可致輕微氣短。面色蒼白並非因氣血兩虛，而是氣滯使血不能上榮於面所致。食欲不振與噁心，是因心氣鬱滯不降，進而影響胃之功能。舌象顯示氣滯已開始影響血分。左寸脈略見洪象，是此證型的關鍵指徵。內關開胸、行氣、安神；神門調理心氣、安神；膻中行胸中之氣；巨闕調心並降逆胃氣；豐隆之選用並非為化痰，而是為開胸。第二次就診的臨床表現顯示，因離婚壓力，病情已由心氣鬱滯加重為心血瘀阻。血瘀的特徵是症狀在夜間及血液循環減緩的睡眠時段加重。通里能行心血、安神；內關能行心血、開胸、安神。如同其他陰經絡穴一般，通里與內關皆具有治療情志病症的特殊功效。鳩尾為任脈之絡穴，能安神開胸，對嚴重焦慮、憂慮或恐懼有強力的鎮靜作用。太衝以行氣來活血，三陰交則以滋陰來活血安神。含太谿的處方適用於心腎不交所致的焦慮；含丘墟的處方適用於心膽氣虛所致的焦慮；含少府的處方則適用於痰熱擾心所致的焦慮。(出處：The Practice of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia，2008年，第402頁；Foundations of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia，2015年版，第506、1141、1142頁)"
    },
