    {
      "number": 313,
      "question_en": "According to the CNT Manual, which is the \"critical\" guideline that should always be followed when cleaning and disinfecting cups? The acupuncturist should first wash the cups with soap and water and then",
      "question_hant": "依據CNT手冊，清潔與消毒拔罐用具時應遵循的「關鍵」準則為何？鍼灸師應先以肥皂與清水清洗罐具，然後",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "with intermediate-level disinfectant if no blood is present in the cups",
          "hant": "若罐內無血跡則使用中效消毒劑",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "with a high or intermediate level disinfectant with or without blood in the cups",
          "hant": "無論罐內是否有血跡，皆使用高效或中效消毒劑",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "with a low-level disinfectant if no blood is present in the cups",
          "hant": "若罐內無血跡則使用低效消毒劑",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "with a high or intermediate level disinfectant only if blood is present in the cups",
          "hant": "僅在罐內有血跡時才使用高效或中效消毒劑",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The current controversy is how often the skin barrier is compromised with cupping, regardless of the cupping method used. Researchers have said that microscopic amounts of blood is regularly present with cupping even over intact skin. The acupuncturist needs to assess the patient's reaction to cupping. Of course, extruded blood or open blisters caused by cupping show a compromised skin barrier. But a visual inspection alone is insufficient to be able to detect microscopic amounts of blood that can be expressed via cupping. As such it is critical to wash all cups with soap and water followed by an intermediate to high-level medical disinfectant. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 38",
      "exp_hant": "目前的爭議在於，無論採用何種拔罐方式，皮膚屏障究竟多常受到破壞。研究者指出，即使皮膚表面完整，拔罐仍常會滲出微量血液。鍼灸師須評估患者對拔罐的反應。當然，若拔罐造成血液滲出或水皰破裂，即顯示皮膚屏障已受損；但單憑肉眼檢查，並不足以偵測拔罐可能擠出的微量血液。因此，所有罐具皆須先以肥皂與清水清洗，再以中效至高效的醫用消毒劑處理，此為關鍵準則。(出處：Clean Needle Technique，第7版，第38頁)"
    },
    {
      "number": 314,
      "question_en": "A 57 year-old male has BPH. Symptoms include dribbling urination, weak urinary stream, low back pain. He often feels chilly. The pulse is weak. The prescription includes BL-23 (shen shu), moxa REN-4 (guan yuan), DU-4 (ming men), moxa DU-20 (bai hui), and TB-4 (yang chi). Three weeks after the start of treatment he develops acute appendicitis. His medical doctor refers him to a surgeon for an appendectomy. After recovery the patient returns for acupuncture treatment. He now says that since the surgery he has dribbling urination, and distention and dull pain in the lower abdomen. There are purplish spots on the tongue. The pulse is rapid and hesitant. His medical doctor told him it was a temporary effect of the surgery. What treatment would you give?",
      "question_hant": "一名57歲男性患有良性攝護腺增生（BPH），症狀包括排尿滴瀝、尿線無力、腰痛，且常感畏寒，脈弱。處方為腎俞、灸關元、命門、灸百會，以及陽池。治療開始三週後，他罹患急性闌尾炎，其西醫轉介外科醫師施行闌尾切除手術。術後康復回診接受鍼灸治療，他表示自手術後出現排尿滴瀝，並有下腹脹滿及隱痛，舌上有紫斑，脈數而滯澀。其西醫告知這只是手術的暫時性影響。您應給予下列何種治療？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "BL-23 (shen shu), REN-4 (guan yuan), and KI-7 (fu liu), and SP-6 (san yin jiao)",
          "hant": "腎俞、關元、復溜及三陰交",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "REN-3 (zhong ji), SP-6 (san yin jiao), ST-28 (shui dao), KI-5 (shui quan)",
          "hant": "中極、三陰交、水道、水泉",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "BL-28 (pang guang shu), REN-3 (zhong ji), BL-39 (wei yang)",
          "hant": "膀胱俞、中極、委陽",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "TB-4 (yang chi), DU-4 (ming men), REN-4 (guan yuan), DU-20 (bai hui)",
          "hant": "陽池、命門、關元、百會",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Urinary retention or dribbling urination can be due Bladder Heat, Decline of Ming Men, or Qi damage to the channels. This patient originally presented with a decline of Kidney and of Ming Men fire. GV-4 and BL-23 reinforce Kidney yang. Moxa on REN-4 and DU-20 invigorates Kidney qi so that urination becomes free and smooth. A weak Kidney qi makes the Triple Burner fail in promoting the circulation of water. TB-4 is selected to invigorate the circulation of the water passages. After the patient returned three weeks later, the urinary symptoms were due to damage of the qi of the channels. Surgery can injure blood vessels and impede the function of the Bladder qi. REN-3 adjusts Bladder function and promotes urination. SP-6 promotes qi and blood circulation in the meridians and regulates urination. KI-5, the xi-cleft point, combined with ST-28 promotes urination and relieves distention and pain in the lower abdomen. CAM, 3rd Edition, page 438;CAM, 4th Edition, page 528",
      "exp_hant": "小便不利或滴瀝可能因膀胱熱、命門火衰，或經絡氣機受損所致。此患者最初表現為腎與命門火衰，命門與腎俞可補益腎陽，灸關元與百會能鼓舞腎氣，使排尿通暢。腎氣虛弱會使三焦無法正常運行水液，故選用陽池以促進水道運行。三週後患者回診，其排尿症狀則是因經絡氣機受損所致——手術可能傷及血脈，影響膀胱氣化功能。中極可調節膀胱功能、促進排尿；三陰交能促進經絡氣血運行、調節排尿；郄穴水泉配水道，能促進排尿並緩解下腹脹滿與疼痛。(出處：CAM，第3版，第438頁；CAM，第4版，第528頁)"
    },
