      "exp_en": "The red flag is facial pain over sinuses, fever, purulent discharge from nose continuously for 3 or more months or recurrently for > 6 months. Chronic bacterial sinusitis is assumed present until proven otherwise. For acupuncturist the key is to determine if the sinusitis is improving, independent of what therapy is being used. Patients which are worsening or the situation is becoming chronic should be referred before the infection spreads beyond the sinuses. Patients with weak immune systems (chronic prednisone, AIDS, etc) can quickly worsen with an ordinary infection. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 112-113",
      "exp_hant": "此警訊徵象為鼻竇部顏面疼痛、發燒，以及持續3個月以上或反覆發作超過6個月的鼻腔膿性分泌物。應假設為慢性細菌性鼻竇炎，直至排除此可能性為止。對鍼灸師而言，重點在於判斷鼻竇炎是否正在改善，而不論所使用的療法為何。病情惡化或逐漸轉為慢性者，應在感染擴散至鼻竇以外之前予以轉診。免疫力低下的患者（如長期使用類固醇、愛滋病患者等），即使是一般感染也可能迅速惡化。(出處：An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals，2012年，Anzaldua，第112-113頁)"
