      "exp_en": "This is the most complete answer. A mail carrier is not included in an ECP as it can be expected that they will not come in contact with the body fluids of patients. Acupuncturists with employees who pull needles, empty the trash, help with patient dressing/underessing should have an ECP. The ECP needs: 1) list the jobs where ALL employees have possible occupational exposure to body fluids. 2) list the jobs where SOME employees have possible occupational exposure to body fluids. 3) list the tasks and procedures where possible occupational exposure to body fluids can occur. The ECP needs to also have a schedule and the methods for putting these safety procedures into effect. Further, a copy of the ECP is to be made available to all employees. The ECP must be reviewed annually and, if necessary, be updated with new tasks, new jobs, and procedures. Training of employees must take place before they are exposed to hazards. All employees have to receive annual training regarding the OSHA blood borne pathogen procedures. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 207",
