    {
      "number": 339,
      "question_en": "A 8 year-old child with hip pain was brought to the acupuncture clinic by his mother. The pain started a month earlier while playing with friends. The pain was described as a dull ache behind the hip and lasts for an hour after the activity. The physical exam revealed a slight limp. There was as a slightly limited ROM in the left hip. The ROM test caused slight discomfort. The child says he is afraid of needles. The right knee and hip were normal. What would you do?",
      "question_hant": "一名8歲兒童因髖部疼痛由母親帶至鍼灸診所就診。疼痛始於一個月前與朋友玩耍時。疼痛描述為髖部後方隱隱作痛，活動後可持續一小時。理學檢查顯示輕微跛行，左髖關節活動度略受限，活動度測試時引起輕微不適。孩童表示害怕鍼刺。右膝及右髖均正常。您應該怎麼做？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "make a timely (a week or two) referral to primary care physician",
          "hant": "於適當時間內（一至兩週）轉診至基層照護醫師",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "treat the patient with 7-star needle and cupping",
          "hant": "以七星鍼及拔罐為患者治療",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "have mother drive the child to an ED (emergency department)",
          "hant": "請母親將孩童送往急診室",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "treat the patient with tui na",
          "hant": "以推拿為患者治療",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag no history of trauma and progressive hip pain on movement and decreased hip ROM. Avascular necrosis of the hip is assumed present until proven otherwise. Avascular hip necrosis is also called Perthes disease which is the death of a portion of the ball of the femur due to poor blood supply. Pain is the primary complaint in avascular necrosis. The pain usually starts hours after activity and lasts for one hour or two afterwards. Rest pain is present in 75% of cases. Night pain is present in 45% of cases. The peak incidence of Perthes disease is in children 4-10 years old with a median age of 6. There is another peak incidence period between 24-25 years old. The clue in this case was the hip pain plus the age. In this situation you may make a semi-urgent (same day or next day) or a timely referral. The ultimate consultant will be an orthopedic surgeon. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 119-120",
      "exp_hant": "此警訊徵象為無外傷史，卻有活動時漸進性加重的髖部疼痛及髖關節活動度下降。應假設為髖部缺血性壞死，直至排除此可能性為止。髖部缺血性壞死又稱為柏斯病（Perthes disease），是因血液供應不良導致股骨頭部分壞死的疾病。疼痛是缺血性壞死的主要主訴，通常於活動後數小時開始出現，並持續一至兩小時。75%的病例會有靜息時疼痛，45%的病例會有夜間疼痛。柏斯病的好發年齡為4至10歲兒童，中位數約6歲，另有一好發高峰期在24至25歲之間。本案例的線索在於髖部疼痛合併其年齡層。此情況下，可作半緊急（當日或隔日）或適當時間內的轉診，最終應轉介至骨科醫師會診。(出處：An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals，2012年，Anzaldua，第119-120頁)"
    },
    {
      "number": 340,
      "question_en": "According to the CNT manual, what is the recommended safe needling depth for the upper back, chest, and intercostal areas to avoid the possibility of a pneumothorax?",
      "question_hant": "依CNT手冊建議，為避免造成氣胸之可能，上背部、胸部及肋間部位建議的安全進針深度為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "20-30 mm",
          "hant": "20-30毫米",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "10-20 mm",
          "hant": "10-20毫米",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "30-40 mm",
          "hant": "30-40毫米",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "2-3 mm",
          "hant": "2-3毫米",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "According to the CNT manual, 10-20 mm is the recommendations. This is less than the face width of a US nickel. Shallow needling depth for the chest, back, and intercostal space is a critical recommendation to avoid the risk of pneumothorax. Using oblique needling in these areas is a strong recommendation. Because the apex of the lung extends 2-3 cm above the clavicular line, incorrect needling of GB-21 has produced pneumothorax. You can reduce the risk of pneumothorax when needling GB-21 by lifting the trapezius muscle with the opposite hand and needling across the muscle at GB-21, needling obliquely and not inferiorly toward the lung. It is a strong recommendation to limit vertically manipulating the needle on the back or chest. Avoiding an upward direction at REN-15 is also critical to avoid injuring the heart. It is strongly recommended not to cup over needles on the chest or on the abdomen to avoid compressing the tissue that can cause the needle to penetrate further into internal organs. Also, needling DU-22 is prohibited in infants. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 12",
      "exp_hant": "依CNT手冊建議，安全進針深度為10-20毫米，此深度小於一枚美金五分硬幣的直徑。胸部、背部及肋間部位採淺刺，是避免氣胸風險的關鍵建議，並強烈建議於這些部位採斜刺法。由於肺尖可高出鎖骨線上方2-3公分，若肩井（GB-21）進針不當，曾造成氣胸病例。降低肩井進針氣胸風險的方法，是以對側手提捏斜方肌，橫向穿越肌肉進針，並採斜刺而非朝肺部方向向下刺入。強烈建議限制在背部或胸部進行縱向提插行鍼。避免鳩尾（REN-15）朝上方向進針，對避免傷及心臟同樣至關重要。強烈建議勿於胸腹部留鍼處拔罐，以免壓迫組織使鍼進一步刺入內臟。此外，嬰兒禁刺囟會（DU-22）。(出處：Clean Needle Technique，第7版，第12頁)"
    },
    {
      "number": 341,
      "question_en": "A 43 year-old female reports having a \"bad cold\" from which she has not recovered. She feels cold with cold extremities, aversion to wind, and has spontaneous sweating. She has a cough and expectorates a little sputum. She denies having a sore throat, a fever, or thirst. She generally feels fatigued. Appetite, bowels, and urine are normal. Her history shows that she easily catches colds, has a tendency to have cold hands and feet, and likes to wear more clothes than others. The physical examination reveals a pale tongue with a white-moist coating. The pulse is sunken, thin, and without force. Blood pressure of 110/68, pulse rate of 74, temperature 99 F. Lab tests show a CBC a count of 4.2 and the WBC is 10,000. Hemoglobin is 12.1 and Hematocrit is 36. Negative throat Strep Culture and negative ASO Titer. The patient was treated with REN-6 (qi hai) with moxa, ST-36 (zu san li) with warm needle, TB-5 (wai guan), and BL-12 (feng men). After three treatments, she no longer has aversion to wind and spontaneous sweating. Which treatment would you now select?",
      "question_hant": "一名43歲女性主訴罹患「重感冒」尚未痊癒。她畏寒、四肢冰冷、惡風，並有自汗。有咳嗽並咳出少量痰液。她否認有喉嚨痛、發燒或口渴。整體感到疲倦，食欲、大小便皆正常。病史顯示她容易感冒，手腳易冷，且比一般人喜歡多穿衣物。理學檢查顯示舌淡苔白潤，脈沉細無力。血壓110/68，脈搏74次/分，體溫華氏99度。實驗室檢查CBC計數4.2，白血球10,000，血色素12.1，血比容36。喉部鏈球菌培養及ASO效價皆為陰性。患者接受灸氣海、溫鍼足三里、外關與風門治療。三次治療後，惡風與自汗已消失。您現在應選用下列何種治療？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
