    {
      "number": 356,
      "question_en": "Which burn degree has an absence of pain?",
      "question_hant": "哪一種燒傷程度沒有疼痛感？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "second degree burns",
          "hant": "二度燒傷",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "first and third degree burns",
          "hant": "一度與三度燒傷",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "first degree burns",
          "hant": "一度燒傷",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "third degree burns",
          "hant": "三度燒傷",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "First degree burns typically have a bright pink or red color on the skin, without any blistering. The pain can be intense because the first layer of skin is very sensitive. First degree burns can occur by staying out in the sun unprotected for too long or by touching a hot stove. While in first degree burns the skin stays mostly intact, in second degree burns there is a break in the first layer of skin in the form of blistering and even bubbling, with white fluid within the blisters. There is a greater pain involved with second degree burns, as two skin layers have been compromised. Third degree burns are the most severe as all layers of skin are likely to have been damaged, as well as muscles and tendons. The skin color is closer to a white hue as the injury gets deeper. In third degree burns the skin can have a thick-white leathery appearance. While first and second degree burns are painful, third degree burns are not painful because there is serious damage done to the nerves (pain receptors) You will also see the different degrees by different names: superficial, superficial partial thickness, deep partial thickness, full thickness.",
      "exp_hant": "一度燒傷的皮膚通常呈現亮粉紅色或紅色，不會出現水泡。由於表皮層極為敏感，疼痛感可能相當劇烈。一度燒傷常見於長時間未加防護曝曬於陽光下，或碰觸到滾燙的爐具。一度燒傷的皮膚大致仍保持完整，而二度燒傷則是表皮層出現破損，形成水泡甚至起泡，泡內含有白色液體。由於有兩層皮膚受損，二度燒傷的疼痛感更為強烈。三度燒傷最為嚴重，皮膚各層很可能都已受損，甚至波及肌肉與肌腱。傷勢越深，皮膚顏色越趨近於白色。三度燒傷的皮膚可能呈現厚實、發白、如皮革般的外觀。雖然一度與二度燒傷會伴隨疼痛，三度燒傷卻因神經（痛覺受器）已嚴重受損而不會疼痛。這些不同程度的燒傷也有其他名稱：淺層（表淺）、淺層部分皮層、深層部分皮層，以及全皮層燒傷。"
    },
