      ],
      "exp_en": "Liver Invading the Stomach. The treatment principle is to Subdue Rebellious Liver Qi and Strengthen the Stomach. LR-14 (qi men) harmonizes the Liver and Stomach. GB-34 (yang ling quan) smooths the flow of Liver qi especially in the hypochondrium. REN-13 (shang wan) subdues rebellious Stomach qi. ST-36 (zu san li) tonifies the Stomach. BL-21 (wei shu) tonifies the Stomach and is an important point to use in chronic conditions. REN-10 (xia wan), ST-21 (liang men), and ST-19 (bu rong) are other points that can be selected to descend the Stomach qi. ST-34 (liang qiu) can be selected to alleviate acute epigastric pain and discomfort. Reducing needle technique is used on points that treat the Liver and reinforcing needle technique is used on points that tonify the Stomach. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 562; 2005 Edition, page 532; 1989 Edition page 228",
      "exp_hant": "肝犯胃證。治療原則為平肝降逆、健運脾胃。期門調和肝胃；陽陵泉疏通肝氣，尤擅疏解脅肋部氣滯；上脘平降胃氣上逆；足三里補益脾胃；胃俞補益脾胃，是慢性病症中常用的要穴。此外，下脘、梁門、不容等穴亦可選用以降胃氣。梁丘可用於緩解急性胃脘疼痛不適。治肝之穴用瀉法，補脾胃之穴則用補法。《The Foundations of Chinese Medicine》，Maciocia，2015年版，第562頁；2005年版，第532頁；1989年版，第228頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 358,
      "question_en": "A 34 year-old male has a dry cough as the main complaint. The cough is without sputum. He has a dry throat, afternoon fever, malar flush, red tongue with a thin coating, and a thready-rapid pulse. You treat the patient with BL-13 (fei shu), LU-1 (zhong fu), LU-7 (lie que), and KI-6 (zhao hai). He returns to the third treatment with the same symptoms except now he adds that he has been suffering with nosebleeds. Which two points would you add to your prescription?",
      "question_hant": "一名34歲男性以乾咳為主訴，咳嗽無痰，伴有咽乾、午後發熱、顴紅、舌紅苔薄、脈細數。您以肺俞、中府、列缺、照海治療。第三次複診時，症狀相同，但患者另外提到近來有流鼻血的情形。您會在處方中加入哪兩個穴位？",
