      "exp_en": "Chronic diarrhea is associated with Spleen Deficiency or Kidney Deficiency. Acute diarrhea is associated with excess Cold-Dampness, Damp-Heat, or Food Retention. With the first clinical picture (diarrhea, weak pulse) you can do an initial diagnosis of Spleen Qi Deficiency. SP-3, a yuan-source point, REN-12, front-mu Stomach point, ST-36, Stomach he-sea point, and BL-20, back-shu point, are selected to invigorate the Spleen and strengthen the transformation-transportation function of the Spleen and Stomach to stop diarrhea. On the return visit, the clinical picture becomes clearer and points to a Kidney Deficiency (loose stools worse in the morning, pain below the navel that improves after BM, and increased borborygmus) along with a Spleen Deficiency. KI-3, yuan-source point, combined with the back-shu point BL-23 warms the Kidney yang and invigorates Kidney qi. DU-4 strengthens Kidney yang and the Gate of Fire. REN-4 nourishes the Kidneys, benefits essence, and warms and tonifies the Spleen. BL-20 and ST-36 tonify the Spleen and Stomach to stop diarrhea. The other prescriptions do not or insufficiently focus on the Kidneys. CAM, 3rd Edition, page 421; CAM, 4th Edition, page 513-515",
