      "exp_en": "This is the most complete answer. Hands should be washed after removing gloves. Hand washing should be done: 1) upon completion of required tasks and before leaving the office. 2) Immediately after removal of gloves or other personal protective equipment. 3) Upon contact or when there is visible contamination with blood or other potentially infectious material. 4) Before and after patient contact. 5) Before eating, drinking, smoking, applying cosmetics, or handling contact lenses. 6) Before and after using the bathroom. 7) Before any activities in which hand contact is made with mucous membranes, the eyes, or breaks in the skin (eg, cuts, abrasions, wounds). Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 62",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整的答案。脫除手套後也應洗手。洗手應於下列情況進行：1）完成所需工作後及離開診間前。2）脫除手套或其他個人防護裝備後立即。3）接觸到或可見有血液或其他潛在感染性物質污染時。4）接觸病患前後。5）進食、飲水、抽菸、化妝或配戴隱形眼鏡前。6）如廁前後。7）任何會使手接觸到黏膜、眼睛或皮膚破損處（如切傷、擦傷、傷口）的活動之前。《Acupuncture Risk Management》，CMS Press，Kailin，1997年，第62頁"
