    {
      "number": 373,
      "question_en": "A 25 year-old pregnant patient complains of morning sickness. She has nausea, vomiting, and frequent belching. She complains of eye distention and epigastric fullness. She is treated with ST-36 (zu san li), PC-6 (nei guan), REN-12 (zhong wan). She returns the following week and reports a reduction in the vomiting. However, all the other symptoms are still present. What point would you add to the prescription?",
