      ],
      "exp_en": "The clinical picture points to Kidney Yang Deficiency (back pain, tinnitus, feeling cold, frequent-pale urination), Spleen Deficiency (loose stools), Blood Deficiency (dry scalp, dandruff), and Wind-Heat (dry eczema). In terms of the location of the symptoms (nose, anus) the du mai is the applicable vessel to treat as well as the ren mai (eczema around navel). The pathway of the du mai travels to the anus and nose. Moreover, the du mai has an internal branch which follows a pathway similar to the ren mai which strengthens the wei qi system (allergic rhinitis). The du mai also strengthens the yang, the Kidneys, and the lower back. The opening (SI-3) and coupled (BL-62) points are selected for treatment. The Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 447",
      "exp_hant": "此臨床表現指向腎陽虛（腰痛、耳鳴、怕冷、頻尿且尿色清白）、脾虛（大便稀溏）、血虛（頭皮乾燥、頭皮屑），以及風熱（乾性濕疹）。就症狀所在部位（鼻、肛門）而言，督脈為適用經脈，任脈（臍周濕疹）亦相關。督脈的循行路線經過肛門與鼻部。此外，督脈有一內行分支，其路徑與任脈相似，能強化衛氣系統（過敏性鼻炎）。督脈也能強壯陽氣、補益腎臟及腰部。治療選用開穴（後谿）與相配穴（申脈）。《The Channels of Acupuncture》，Maciocia，2006年，第447頁"
    },
