        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "pain from surgical implants",
          "hant": "手術植入物所致疼痛",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Cervical spondylosis is generally asymptomatic, and when it does manifest itself, it is typically in the form of pain and stiffness in the neck. TDP lamp therapy is indicated for joint pain and stiffness. Bensky lists the indications for TDP lamp as low back pain, joint pain, tendonitis, neuralgia, soft tissue sprain, asthma, chronic bronchitis, frostbite, acute eczema, and chronic pharyngitis. The Merck Manual lists the indications for joint pain, back pain, fibrosisitis, muscle spasms, myositis, neuralgia, sprains, strains, whiplash, and tenosynovitis. Treatment in areas with surgical implants (metal, silicone, pacemakers) should be avoided. There is the risk that these materials can absorb and hold heat at a different rate than the living surrounding tissue and cause internal burns. Infants or persons who cannot communicate when the treatment is getting too hot should not be treated with a TDP lamp. Patients with neuropathy can have an inability to accurately experience temperature which can result in accidental burns. The Merck Manual has contraindications in the use of heat lamps for advanced heart disease, peripheral vascular disease, impaired skin sensation, and significant hepatic or renal insufficiency. The CNT Manual has contraindications for heat lamps on infants, children, incapacitated, sleeping, or unconscious patients. Bensky has contraindications in the use of heat lamps for acute TB, malignancies, cardiovascular insufficiency, hemorrhage, sensory impairment, and bleeding disorders. Treatment manuals for the TDP lamp can also list contraindications: Pregnancy, patients with high fever, otitis media, splenitis, eye diseases, varicose veins, open pulmonary tuberculosis, serious arteriosclerosis, and with bleeding tendencies. The TDP lamp should not be used on the head of patients with hypertension. When using on the head, protection of the eyes is required so they do not become dry. CNT Manual, 7th Edition, page 112; Acupuncture A Comprehensive Text, Bensky, 1981, page 436; Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 2753; Mineral Infrared Therapy, Tsu-Tsair Chi, 1993, page 37",
      "exp_hant": "頸椎病通常無明顯症狀，若出現症狀，多表現為頸部疼痛與僵硬。TDP神燈療法適用於治療關節疼痛與僵硬。Bensky列出TDP神燈的適應症包括腰痛、關節痛、肌腱炎、神經痛、軟組織扭傷、氣喘、慢性支氣管炎、凍瘡、急性濕疹及慢性咽炎。《Merck Manual》列出的適應症則包括關節痛、背痛、纖維組織炎、肌肉痙攣、肌炎、神經痛、扭傷、拉傷、頸部揮鞭傷及腱鞘炎。應避免對有手術植入物（金屬、矽膠、心律調節器）的部位進行治療，因這些材料吸收與釋放熱能的速率可能與周圍活組織不同，有造成內部灼傷的風險。無法在治療過熱時表達不適的嬰兒或人士，不應使用TDP神燈治療。神經病變患者可能無法準確感知溫度，因而有意外燙傷的風險。《Merck Manual》列出的熱燈禁忌症包括重度心臟病、周邊血管疾病、皮膚感覺障礙，以及嚴重肝腎功能不全。CNT手冊則列出嬰兒、兒童、失能、睡眠中或意識不清患者的熱燈使用禁忌。Bensky則列出急性肺結核、惡性腫瘤、心血管功能不全、出血、感覺障礙及出血性疾病作為熱燈使用的禁忌。TDP神燈治療手冊亦可能列出下列禁忌症：懷孕、高燒患者、中耳炎、脾臟發炎、眼疾、靜脈曲張、開放性肺結核、嚴重動脈硬化，以及有出血傾向者。高血壓患者不應於頭部使用TDP神燈。若於頭部使用，須保護眼睛以避免乾澀。CNT手冊，第7版，第112頁；《Acupuncture A Comprehensive Text》，Bensky，1981年，第436頁；《Merck Manual》，第18版，第2753頁；《Mineral Infrared Therapy》，Tsu-Tsair Chi，1993年，第37頁"
    },
