      "exp_en": "A medical emergency is an event that threatens the patient in such a manner that immediate medical care is needed to prevent death or serious impairment of health. A medical emergency includes severe pain, bad injury, a serious illness, or a medical condition that is quickly getting much worse. Questions to help decide whether 911 should be called include: 1) Is the condition life or limb threatening, 2) Could the condition worsen quickly on the way to the hospital, 3) If the victim is moved, will it cause further injury, 4) Does the victim need skills or equipment that paramedics carry right away, 5) Would distance or traffic cause a delay in getting the person to the hospital. If the answer is yes to any these questions, call 911. If you are unsure call and get assistance. The trained dispatcher will help advise you. Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 115",
