      "exp_en": "From a TCM point of view, fibromyalgia is associated primarily with Dampness (though Cold and Wind can be involved), entering the body and chronically lodging itself in the muscle channels and in the luo-connecting vessels located in the superficial energetic wei-qi layer between the skin and muscles. The Dampness pathogen can be associated with patterns of Qi Stasis, Spleen Qi/Yang Deficiency, Liver-Kidney Yin Xu, Liver Blood Xu, or Blood Stasis. The initial clinical picture of the patient indicates an acute attack of Dampness worsening her pre-existing condition. As the manifestation (biao) is strong, the focus of the treatment should be on resolving and transforming Dampness. REN-9, SP-9, and KI-7 resolve Dampness. Additional points that can be selected include REN-12 and BL-22. LI-10 and ST-36 are selected to invigorate yang ming channels to help eliminate Dampness and are an effective combination to reduce muscle aches and fatigue in the limbs. This Rx is the base Rx for resolving Dampness, regardless of the underlying pattern. After the initial cycle of treatment, her pain attenuated and the thick-sticky tongue coating was resolved. Now one can see the underlying pattern of qi and blood stasis (fixed boring pain, pain worse at night, dark complexion, dark menstrual blood). The fact that the blood is stagnant indicates a deeper progression of the Dampness pathogen impeding the deep luo-connecting channels at the blood level. GB-34 and LR-3 move qi and eliminate qi stasis. BL-17 and SP-10 invigorate and move the Blood. SP-4 could also be selected as it moves qi, Blood, or stuck Dampness. The Rx with BL-20 would be selected when the underlying pattern is Dampness, Qi stasis, and a weak Spleen. The Rx with LR-8 would be added when the underlying pattern is Dampness and Liver Blood Xu. The Rx with DU-20 would be added when the emphasis is Dampness clouding the Mind. Additionally, you can select local, adjacent, and distal points that target the main area of pain. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 1097-1105, 1115, 1119",
      "exp_hant": "從中醫角度而言，纖維肌痛症主要與濕邪有關（雖然寒與風也可能牽涉其中），濕邪侵入人體後，長期滯留於肌肉經絡及位於皮肉之間、屬於衛氣淺層的絡脈之中。濕邪可能兼夾氣滯、脾氣（陽）虛、肝腎陰虛、肝血虛，或血瘀等證型。此患者初期的臨床表現顯示為急性濕邪發作，加重了原本的病情。由於標證（表現症狀）明顯，治療重點應放在化濕、袪濕上。水分、陰陵泉、復溜能袪濕，亦可加選中脘與三焦俞。手三里與足三里則能振奮陽明經以助袪濕，兩者合用可有效減輕四肢痠痛與疲勞，此方為化濕的基本處方，不論其潛在證型為何皆可使用。經過初期治療後，患者疼痛減輕，舌苔厚膩已消退，此時可見其潛在證型為氣血瘀滯（固定不移的刺痛、夜間疼痛加重、面色晦暗、經血暗黑）。血瘀的出現顯示濕邪已進一步深入，阻滯了血分層次的深層絡脈。陽陵泉與太衝能行氣、袪除氣滯；膈俞與血海則能活血化瘀。公孫亦可選用，因其能行氣、行血、袪除滯濕。若潛在證型為濕邪、氣滯兼脾虛，則選用含脾俞之處方；若潛在證型為濕邪兼肝血虛，則加入含曲泉之處方；若重點為濕邪蒙蔽心神，則加入含百會之處方。此外，亦可依主要疼痛部位選取局部、鄰近及遠端穴位。《The Practice of Chinese Medicine》，Maciocia，2008年，第1097-1105、1115、1119頁"
