      "exp_en": "It is the extraordinary meridians which either act as a reservoir of qi to provide qi to the primary channels or to absorb an excess of qi in the primary channels. The yang divergent channels connect the corresponding fu organ, complementary zang organ, and corresponding primary channel. Most yin divergent channels connect to their corresponding zang organ and primary channel and complementary divergent channel. The divergent channels connect body areas which the primary channels do not cover (eg. gall bladder, stomach, and bladder divergent all connect with the Heart. The bladder divergent connects to the anal area whereas the Bladder primary does not, etc). The divergent channels bring qi and blood to the head. The head connects all of the yang primary channels. Only the deep internal pathways of the Heart and Liver primary channels connect to the head. The yin divergent channels, through their connection to the yang divergent channels and yang primary channels, have a way to bring qi and blood to the head. For example, the Lung primary channel does not go to the head. However, LU-7 can treat nose problems because the connection of the Lung primary channel to the head is through the association between the Lung divergent channel and the Large Intestine primary channel. The divergent channels explain why certain primary channel points do what they do (eg PC-6 treating head and neck problems). The divergent channels do not have their own points or pathology but primary channel points make use of the divergent channel pathways to affect areas of the body not covered by the primary channels. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 16",
      "exp_hant": "扮演氣血蓄積之所、能為正經提供氣或吸收正經多餘之氣的，其實是奇經。陽經之經別連結相應的腑、互為表裡的臟，以及相應的正經。大多數陰經之經別則連結其相應的臟、正經，以及互為表裡的經別。經別能連結正經未能涵蓋的身體部位（例如：膽、胃、膀胱的經別皆與心相連；膀胱經別連結肛門部位，而膀胱正經則無此連結，等等）。經別能將氣血帶至頭部。頭部連結所有陽經正經，僅有心與肝正經的深層內行路線與頭部相連。陰經之經別透過與陽經之經別及陽經正經的聯繫，得以將氣血帶至頭部。例如，肺正經並不上達頭部，但列缺卻能治療鼻部問題，這是因為肺經之經別與大腸正經之間的聯繫，使肺經得以連結頭部。經別解釋了某些正經穴位為何具有特定療效（例如內關能治療頭頸部問題）。經別本身沒有專屬的穴位或病候，而是正經的穴位運用經別的循行路徑，來影響正經未能涵蓋的身體部位。A Manual of Acupuncture，Deadman，第2版，第16頁"
