      "exp_en": "LI-3 expels wind-heat, clears heat and benefits the throat and teeth, and dispels fullness and treats diarrhea. Very few points of the three yang channels of the hand are indicated in the treatment of their respective organ. For example, the Small Intestine points have no indications in treating the intestines. The lower he-sea points (ST-37, ST-39, BL-39) are preferred to the treatment of the organs. However, for the Large Intestine channel the point LI-3 is indicated to treat diarrhea and borborygmus. Shu-stream points are indicated for heaviness of the body and joint pain. LI-3 can treat problems with the fingers, especially the index and middle fingers. LI-3 is often combined with SI-3 to treat the fingers. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 34, 103",
      "exp_hant": "三間能袪風熱、清熱、利咽喉與牙齒，並能消脹滿、治療腹瀉。手三陽經中，很少有穴位能主治其相應臟腑，例如小腸經的穴位並無治療腸道的主治項目；下合穴（上巨虛、下巨虛、委陽）反而更常用於臟腑病症的治療。然而，大腸經的三間卻能主治腹瀉與腸鳴。輸穴主治身重與關節疼痛。三間能治療手指問題，尤其是食指與中指。三間常與後谿配合用以治療手指問題。A Manual of Acupuncture，Deadman，第2版，第34、103頁"
