      ],
      "exp_en": "Diabetes can arise from Heat exhausting Body Fluids and injuring the yin or from a Deficiency of Kidney yang. This disorder is classified as wasting in the Upper, Middle, and Lower burner wasting which are related to the Lung, Spleen, and Kidneys respectively. The Upper Burner wasting is characterized by great thirst, the Middle Burner by great hunger, and the Lower Burner by frequent urination. The original points selected treat and drain Heat from the Upper Burner (BL-13), the Middle Burner (ST-36, BL-20), and the Lower Burner (BL-23, KI-3). As the thirst (Upper Burner) is still an issue, the focus of the added points are to Clear Lung Heat (LU-10) and nourish the Blood generate Body Fluids (BL-17). If the patient complained that hunger was the unresolved symptom, then the back-shu point (BL-21) and the front-mu point (REN-12) for the Stomach would be selected to further focus the treatment on regulating the middle jiao. Were the unresolved symptom be in the Lower Burner (frequent urination) then KI-7 (benefits Kidneys and regulates Water Passages) and REN-4 (tonifies and nourishes Kidneys and benefits Essence) would be selected. The extra point wei guan xia shu (Pancreas shu) is 1.5 cun lateral to lower border of T8 regulates the pancreas to treat diabetes. Extra point zi gong is selected to regulate menstruation. Acupuncture A Comprehensive Text, Bensky, 1981, page 605",
      "exp_hant": "糖尿病可能源於熱邪耗傷津液、損傷陰分，或源於腎陽虛。此病依上、中、下三消分類，分別對應肺、脾、腎。上消以口渴甚為特徵，中消以易饑為特徵，下消則以頻尿為特徵。原處方所選穴位分別清瀉上焦（肺俞）、中焦（足三里、脾俞）及下焦（腎俞、太谿）之熱。由於口渴（上消）仍為未解決的症狀，新加入的穴位重點在於清肺熱（魚際）及養血生津（膈俞）。若患者主訴未解決的症狀為易饑，則應選用胃之背俞穴（胃俞）與募穴（中脘），以進一步著重調理中焦。若未解決的症狀屬下焦（頻尿），則應選用復溜（益腎、調理水道）及關元（補益滋養腎臟、益精）。經外奇穴胃管下俞（胰俞）位於第八胸椎下緣旁開1.5寸，能調理胰臟以治療糖尿病。經外奇穴子宮則用於調理月經。《Acupuncture A Comprehensive Text》，Bensky，1981年，第605頁"
