      "exp_en": "PCP refers to primary care physician. ED refers to emergency department. The red flag is vaginal bleeding years after last menses. Uterine cancer is assumed present until proven otherwise. Vaginal bleeding in post-menopausal women is an early symptom of uterine cancer. When pre-menopausal women have uterine cancer there is often a heavier than normal menstrual bleeding or bleeding between menses or abnormal discharges. Pre-menopausal women with these symptoms should also be referred if the problem does not resolve itself with acupuncture/herbs within 3-6 months. At later stages, uterine cancer has additional symptoms such as heaviness in the pelvis or painful sexual intercourse. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 36-37",
      "exp_hant": "PCP指基層照護醫師（primary care physician）。ED指急診室（emergency department）。此案例的警訊徵象是停經多年後出現的陰道出血，在未證實排除之前應假定為子宮癌。停經後婦女的陰道出血是子宮癌的早期症狀。停經前婦女若罹患子宮癌，常會出現經量較平常增多、經期間出血或異常分泌物等情形。停經前婦女若有這些症狀，且問題在接受針灸／中藥治療3至6個月後仍未緩解，也應予以轉介。子宮癌到了較晚期，還會出現骨盆沉重感或性交疼痛等其他症狀。(出處：An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals，Anzaldua，2012年，第36-37頁)"
