        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Within 36 hours",
          "hant": "36小時內",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Within 24 hours",
          "hant": "24小時內",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "It should be done during or immediately after treatment. Medical records are legal documents, and are subject to the laws of the country/state in which they are produced. Medical notes should be comprehensive enough to allow another medical professional to reconstruct the consultations with the patient. Updates in the medical records document clinical changes, new information, etc.. These often take the form of a SOAP note. They are kept in chronological order and document the sequence of events leading to the current state of health. Health care providers may be required to give an explanation under the Data Protection Act (1998) if the information contained in the records is not intelligible.",
      "exp_hant": "病歷應在治療當下或治療後立即完成。病歷屬於法律文件，須遵守製作所在國家／州的相關法規。病歷記載應力求完整，使其他醫療專業人員也能藉此重建與病人之間的問診過程。病歷的更新用以記錄臨床變化、新資訊等，通常以SOAP病歷格式呈現。病歷須依時間順序記載，呈現導致目前健康狀態的事件經過。若病歷中的資訊難以理解，醫療提供者可能須依《1998年資料保護法》（Data Protection Act）之規定提出說明。"
    },
    {
      "number": 429,
      "question_en": "A 46 year-old female reports that two years ago she noticed difficulty writing. This developed as a fine hand-tremors, right arm stiffness, and trembling in her right leg. She went to see a neurologist who diagnosed her with Parkinson's disease. On taking her health history she reports that she has had hair loss, blurred vision, and occasional night blindness. Upon inspection, her tongue was pale and a little blue-purple on the sides, deviated, and swollen. The pulse was weak-choppy. She was given two herbal formulas, ba zhen tang combined with tian ma gou teng yin. The acupuncture treatment consisted of selecting a prescription from the following points: LR-3 (tai chong), GB-20 (feng chi), DU-19 (hou ding), REN-4 (guan yuan), TB-5 (wai guan), LI-4 (he gu), ST-36 (zu san li), SP-6 (san yin jiao), KI-3 (tai xi), LR-8 (qu quan), and BL-17 (ge shu). She received the preceding point prescription over a two year period. She then took a one month break and returned for another consultation. She reported that her tremors were gone and that she had a general sense of well-being. She did say that her right arm stiffness was still present. The pulse felt stronger but a little wiry. The only change in the tongue was that it was no longer deviated. She wanted to continue to receive treatment to help improve her health. She was told to continue taking the herbal formulas. What acupuncture treatment would you select to address the root of any unresolved TCM disharmony?",
      "question_hant": "一位46歲女性主訴兩年前開始出現書寫困難。之後演變為手部細微顫抖、右臂僵硬，以及右腿震顫。她就診於神經科醫師，被診斷為帕金森氏症。詢問病史時，她提到有掉髮、視力模糊，偶爾夜盲的情形。理學檢查時，舌質淡且舌邊略帶青紫色，舌體歪斜且腫脹。脈象為弱澀脈。她被給予兩種中藥方劑：八珍湯合天麻鉤藤飲。針灸治療則從以下穴位中選穴組方：太衝、風池、後頂、關元、外關、合谷、足三里、三陰交、太谿、曲泉，以及膈俞。她在兩年期間持續接受上述處方治療。之後她停診一個月，再回診諮詢。她表示震顫已經消失，整體感覺良好，但仍提到右臂僵硬依舊存在。脈象較先前有力，但略帶弦象。舌象唯一的變化是舌頭不再歪斜。她希望繼續接受治療以改善健康。她被告知應持續服用中藥方劑。針對尚未解決的中醫證候之根本，你會選擇什麼針灸治療？",
