      "exp_en": "The Small Intestine channel connects with DU-14 from which it goes to the supraclavicular fossa. An internal branch of the Small Intestine starts at ST-12 (supraclavicular fossa), connects with REN-17, REN-13, REN-12, descends to enter the Heart, Stomach, and Small Intestine organ, and moves down the leg to end at the Lower He-Sea point for the Small Intestine organ (ST-39). There is another branch that ascends from ST-12 to cross the neck, cheek, to the outer canthus meeting with GB-1 (foot shao yang), then travels posteriorly intersecting with GB-11 and TB-20, and then goes towards the ear and enters the ear at SI-19. This branch also connects to the inner canthus at BL-1 (foot tai yang). Thus the Small Intestine channel connects with both the inner and outer canthus which explains the eye symptoms treated by Small Intestine points. That the Small Intestine channel entering the ear also helps to explain the selection of Small Intestine points to treat ear disorders. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion, 2010 Edition, page 75; A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, second edition, page 227",
      "exp_hant": "小腸經與大椎相聯繫，再由大椎行至缺盆。小腸經的一條內行支脈起於缺盆（相當於缺盆穴），聯絡膻中、上脘、中脘，向下入心、胃及小腸腑，再沿下肢下行，止於小腸的下合穴（下巨虛）。另有一條支脈由缺盆上行，經頸部、面頰至目外眥，與足少陽經的瞳子髎相會，再向後行，與頭竅陰及角孫相交，然後走向耳部，入於聽宮。此支脈亦聯絡至足太陽經的睛明穴（內眥）。因此小腸經與內、外眥皆有聯繫，這也說明了小腸經穴位可用於治療眼部病症的原因。小腸經入耳，也說明了選用小腸經穴位治療耳疾的道理。(出處：Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion，2010年版，第75頁；A Manual of Acupuncture，Deadman，第2版，第227頁)"
    },
    {
