    {
      "number": 437,
      "question_en": "A 10 year-old child has the flu. Symptoms include fever with fear of cold, headache, sore throat. He is treated with LI-4 (he gu), LI-11 (qu chi), and BL-12 (feng men). His mother calls two days later. She reports that her child's fever is worse at night and that he complains of a dry mouth but does not want to drink. She also says that he is restless and can't sleep at night. You make a house call. Upon inspection, the tongue is red without coating. What treatment would you give?",
      "question_hant": "一位10歲兒童罹患流感，症狀包括發熱惡寒、頭痛、喉嚨痛。曾以合谷、曲池、風門治療。兩天後，其母親來電表示孩子夜間發熱加劇，主訴口乾卻不想喝水，並且煩躁不安、夜不能寐。你前往出診，檢查時發現舌紅無苔。此時你會給予什麼治療？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "PC-8 (lao gong), HT-9 (shao chong), KI-6 (zhao hai)",
          "hant": "勞宮、少衝、照海",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "KI-2 (ran gu), ST-44 (nei ting), LR-2 (xing jian), BL-15 (xin shu)",
          "hant": "然谷、內庭、行間、心俞",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "HT-7 (shen men), LI-11 (qu chi), DU-14 (da zhui), PC-7 (da ling)",
          "hant": "神門、曲池、大椎、大陵",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "DU-14 (da zhui), BL-40 (wei zhong), LI-11 (qu chi), LI-4 (he gu)",
          "hant": "大椎、委中、曲池、合谷",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The first set of symptoms presented point to a wind-heat invasion. The combination of LI-4 and LI-11 release the exterior and clear heat. BL-12 expels exterior wind. The treatment did not expel the external pathogenic factor. Instead the symptoms that the mother said point to the pathogenic factor going deeper into the body and lodging itself in the nutritive qi or ying level. The treatment principle here is to Clear Nutritive Qi Heat and Promote Fluids. PC-8, a ying-spring and fire point, clears heat from the nutritive level and cools the blood. HT-9, a jing-well and wood point, clears heat and calms the Shen. KI-6, the confluent point for the Yin Motility Vessel, nourishes yin, promotes body fluids, and calms the Shen. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2005, page 770, 775; 2005 Edition, page 726, 731",
      "exp_hant": "最初出現的一組症狀顯示為風熱外襲。合谷配曲池能解表清熱，風門則能袪除外風。然而該治療並未將外邪驅除，反而依母親所述的症狀來看，顯示病邪已深入體內，鬱結於營分。此時的治療原則應為清營分熱、生津養液。勞宮為滎穴、屬火，能清營分之熱、涼血；少衝為井穴、屬木，能清熱、安神；照海為陰蹻脈的通穴，能滋陰生津、安神。(出處：Foundations of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia，2005年，第770、775頁；2005年版，第726、731頁)"
    },
    {
      "number": 438,
      "question_en": "A 44 year-old female has a one week history of dizziness. She could not identify what started it. There is no swirling or spinning sensation with the dizziness but she occasionally has tinnitus. She reports having nausea but not vomiting. She complains of poor appetite and slight epigastric and abdominal pain. She says that she dislikes drinking water and avoids cold foods. Urination and stool are normal. The tongue is pale-flabby with small purple dots and thin-white-moist coating in the middle and back. The pulse is slippery. Blood Pressure is 170/90, Pulse is 82, Respirations 20. Electrocardiogram is within normal limits. MRI of the brain is within normal limits. She was treated with ST-8 (tou wei), GB-20 (feng chi), ST-25 (tian shu), and ST-40 (feng long). After three treatments she reported that her dizziness and nausea improved but still had problems with her poor appetite and epigastric distention. There were no changes in the pulse and tongue which still had purple dots. How would you modify the prescription?",
      "question_hant": "一位44歲女性頭暈已一週，無法指出誘發原因。頭暈並無天旋地轉的感覺，但偶有耳鳴。她表示有噁心感但無嘔吐，並主訴食慾不振、上腹及腹部輕微疼痛。她說不喜歡喝水，也會避免食用冰冷食物。大小便正常。舌質淡胖，有細小紫點，舌中及舌根處有薄白潤苔。脈滑。血壓170/90，脈搏82次，呼吸20次。心電圖正常。腦部核磁共振正常。她曾接受頭維、風池、天樞、豐隆治療。三次治療後，她表示頭暈與噁心已有改善，但食慾不振與上腹脹滿的問題依然存在。脈象與舌象皆無變化，舌上仍有紫點。你會如何調整處方？",
      "image": null,
