      "exp_en": "Luo-connecting point. BL-58 (feiyang) has the traditional indications of 1) harmonizing excess in the upper part of the body (excess yang rising) with deficiency in the lower part of the body (deficiency in the kidneys) and 2) expelling wind from the Bladder channel (chills, fever, no sweating, neck/occiput pain, nasal congestion). However, in modern clinical practice BL-58 (feiyang) is most often used for leg and lumbar disorders, especially sciatic pain. As the Bladder divergent channel circles the anus, BL-58 (feiyang) can be used to treat hemorrhoids. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 316",
      "exp_hant": "此為絡穴。飛揚的傳統主治包括：一、調和上實（陽氣上亢）與下虛（腎虛）；二、袪除膀胱經之風（惡寒發熱、無汗、頸項及後頭部疼痛、鼻塞）。然而在現代臨床上，飛揚最常用於治療腿部及腰部病證，尤其是坐骨神經痛。由於膀胱經別環繞肛門，飛揚亦可用於治療痔瘡。(出處：A Manual of Acupuncture，Deadman，第2版，第316頁)"
