      ],
      "exp_en": "The diagnosis is Heart Fire Transmitted to Small Intestine. The treatment principle is to Clear Heart Fire, Calm the Mind, Clear Bladder Heat, Resolve Dampness. HT-8 and SI-2 clear Heart Fire and Heat in the Small Intestine. HT-8 also calms the Shen. SP-9 drains Damp-Heat and opens up the water passages. REN-3 clears Bladder Heat and also opens up the water passages. BL-63 clears Bladder Heat, lessens the urge, and stops pain. The red tongue tip with red points, the full-rapid pulse at the front left position, and the depression from the loss of the mother indicate an excess Fire condition affecting the Heart. The Fire from the Heart has been transmitted to its coupled organ, the Small Intestine. The Fire then infuses the Bladder (burning, scanty, hot urination). The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 850; 1994 Edition, page 505",
      "exp_hant": "此為心火下移小腸之證。治療原則為清心瀉火、安神、清膀胱之熱、化濕。少府與前谷能清心火及小腸之熱，少府亦能安神。陰陵泉能瀉濕熱、通利水道。中極能清膀胱之熱，同樣能通利水道。金門能清膀胱之熱、緩解尿急並止痛。舌尖紅有紅點、左寸脈實而數，加上因喪母而情緒低落，皆顯示心火偏盛之實證。心火下傳至其相表裡之腑——小腸，繼而下注膀胱，導致小便灼熱、量少、色深。(出處：The Practice of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia，2008年，第850頁；1994年版，第505頁)"
    },
