          "hant": "針對可能發生的緊急狀況訂定書面應變流程；備妥可能發生緊急狀況所需的物資；標示診所內急救設備的所在位置",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "written protocols for possible emergencies; history of vendor purchases of emergency equipment; maintain supplies for possible emergencies",
          "hant": "針對可能發生的緊急狀況訂定書面應變流程；緊急設備廠商採購紀錄；備妥可能發生緊急狀況所需的物資",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "written protocols for possible emergencies; maintain supplies for possible emergencies",
          "hant": "針對可能發生的緊急狀況訂定書面應變流程；備妥可能發生緊急狀況所需的物資",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Vendor purchases need not be catalogued. The plan needs to have a written response protocol for possible emergencies, need to identify and maintain the necessary equipment and supplies for possible emergencies, and clearly indicate in your office the location of first aid equipment. The most common types of emergencies in primary care offices include asthma complications, psychiatric-related issues, seizures, anaphylaxis, and cardiac arrest. Keep all supplies in one easily accessible location. Evaluate your patient population and the type of emergencies that may be encountered which will help to decide what equipment, supplies and medications to have readily available. Basic emergency supplies might include ambu-bags and masks, oxygen tank, a pulse oximeter, blood pressure cuffs of all sizes, latex gloves, alcohol swabs, and protective eye gear. In selecting supplies, the skills and training that the staff has should be considered. Equipment and supplies must be able to be safely used within the scope of practice of the staff member. A written protocol for each type of emergencies will ensure that staff has an understanding of their respective roles during an emergency event. The plan, ideally, should list the responsibilities to each staff member. Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 112-113",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整且準確的答案。廠商採購紀錄並不需要建檔。應變計畫必須針對可能發生的緊急狀況制定書面應變流程，需辨識並備妥處理緊急狀況所需的必要設備與物資，並在診所內清楚標示急救設備的所在位置。基層診所最常見的緊急狀況包括氣喘併發症、精神科相關問題、癲癇發作、過敏性休克，以及心跳停止。所有物資應集中放置在一個容易取得的地點。評估你的病人族群及可能遇到的緊急狀況類型，有助於決定應隨時備妥哪些設備、物資與藥物。基本的緊急物資可能包括甦醒球與面罩、氧氣筒、血氧監測儀、各種尺寸的血壓計壓脈帶、乳膠手套、酒精棉片，以及防護眼罩。選擇物資時，應考量工作人員所具備的技能與訓練，設備與物資的使用也必須在工作人員的執業範圍內方能安全操作。針對每一類緊急狀況制定書面流程，能確保工作人員了解各自在緊急事件中的職責。理想上，此計畫應列出每位工作人員的個別職責。(出處：Acupuncture Risk Management，CMS Press，Kailin，1997年，第112-113頁)"
    },
