        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "LI-11 (quchi), ST-44 (neiting), LI-4 (hegu), left side ST-28 (shuidao), left side ST-29 (guilai)",
          "hant": "曲池、內庭、合谷、左側水道、左側歸來",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The prescription for the original diagnosis was based on Liver qi stagnation. The difficult to pass stools, resentment, wiry pulse, and headaches were seen as due to the Liver qi failing to flow smoothly. Combining GB-34 with REN-6 moves Liver qi in the lower abdomen. LR-3 moves stagnant qi and pacifies the Liver. TB-6 regulates the Three Burners and moves qi. What was overlooked in the original analysis were the dry stools and the bloodshot eyes and pounding headache after drinking. In constipation only due to Liver qi stasis, the stools are difficult to pass but are not dry. Only when there is heat will the stools become dry. This is a case that involves Liver qi stasis transforming into heat (wiry pulse, redness on sides of tongue) and bordering on Liver Fire. The etiology in this case involves emotional stress and consumption of alcohol (hot qi). The emotional stress (resentment) stagnates the Liver qi. When chronic the qi stasis transforms into heat. The bouts of alcohol binges aggravate the heat and ignites it into an acute Liver Fire episode (pounding headaches, bloodshot eyes, dark urine). The prescription needs to address not only the Liver qi stasis but also the excess heat. LI-4 clears Large Intestine heat. TB-6 clears heat, opens the Triple Burner, and promotes bowel movement. LR-2 moves Liver qi and drains Liver Fire. SP-6 smooths Liver qi and moistens the intestines. ST-28 clears intestinal heat and promotes bowel movement. For constipation, only needling ST-28 on the left side is sufficient to affect the descending colon. Left side ST-28 can be combined with left side ST-29 for a stronger effect. The prescription with BL-25 is similar to the original prescription which does not address the Liver heat. The prescription with SP-15 focuses on constipation due to Liver Blood deficiency. The prescription with LI-11 focuses on constipation due to yang ming heat. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 535, 543; Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2nd Edition, page 823-826",
      "exp_hant": "最初診斷所開立的處方，是根據肝氣鬱結而定。排便困難、憤懣不平、脈弦及頭痛，皆被視為肝氣疏泄不暢所致。陽陵泉配氣海能行下腹部之肝氣，太衝能行氣解鬱、平肝，支溝能調理三焦、行氣。然而最初的分析忽略了糞便乾燥、雙眼佈滿血絲，以及飲酒後劇烈頭痛等表現。若便秘僅由肝氣鬱滯所致，糞便雖排出困難，但不至於乾燥；唯有兼夾熱象時，糞便才會變乾。此案例牽涉肝氣鬱結化熱（脈弦、舌邊紅），已近乎肝火之勢。其病因涉及情緒壓力與飲酒（酒為熱性之品）。情緒壓力（憤懣不平）使肝氣鬱結，日久氣鬱化熱；反覆縱飲則助長熱勢，進而引動急性肝火發作（劇烈頭痛、雙眼血絲、尿色深黃）。因此處方須同時處理肝氣鬱結與實熱兩方面。合谷能清大腸之熱。支溝能清熱、宣通三焦、通利大便。行間能行肝氣、瀉肝火。三陰交能疏肝氣、潤腸道。水道能清腸中之熱、通利大便。就便秘而言，僅針刺左側水道即足以影響降結腸；左側水道亦可配合左側歸來以加強療效。以大腸俞為主的處方與原方相似，並未處理肝熱；以大橫為主的處方著重於肝血虛所致的便秘；以曲池為主的處方則著重於陽明熱盛所致的便秘。(出處：Foundations of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia，2015年，第535、543頁；Practice of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia，第2版，第823-826頁)"
    },
