      "exp_en": "Neurodermatitis is also known as lichen simplex chronicus. Neurodermatitis is a skin disorder that starts with an itchy patch of skin. Scratching the skin makes neurodermatitis even itchier. This leads to a itch-scratch cycle which can make the skin leathery and thick. Neurodermatitis typically manifests on the the neck, wrists, forearms, legs or anal region. The cause of neurodermatitis is unknown. In some patients neurodermatitis is associated with chronic skin conditions such as eczema, psoriasis, or chronic dry skin. Plum blossom needle can also give good results with hypertension, headaches, dysmeorrhea, intercostal neuralgia, neurasthenia, GI disorders, and other local skin diseases. When tapping the plum blossom hammer the usual sequence is from above to below and medial to lateral. Acupuncture: A Comprehensive Text, Bensky, 1981, page 418",
      "exp_hant": "神經性皮膚炎又稱為慢性單純性苔蘚。這是一種皮膚疾病，起初表現為一小片搔癢的皮膚。搔抓會使搔癢感加劇，形成越抓越癢、越癢越抓的惡性循環，久而久之皮膚會變得粗厚如皮革。神經性皮膚炎常見於頸部、手腕、前臂、腿部或肛門周圍。其成因尚不明確，部分病人的神經性皮膚炎與濕疹、乾癬，或慢性皮膚乾燥等慢性皮膚病有關。梅花針對高血壓、頭痛、痛經、肋間神經痛、神經衰弱、腸胃疾患，以及其他局部皮膚病也有良好療效。以梅花針叩擊時，通常依循由上而下、由內而外的順序進行。(出處：Acupuncture: A Comprehensive Text，Bensky，1981年，第418頁)"
    },
