    {
      "number": 486,
      "question_en": "Eleven months ago, an 81 year-old male patient had a stroke caused by cerebral thrombosis. His right leg and arm were paralyzed. His tongue had a purplish tinge with a normal coating. The pulse was fine-wiry on both sides. Which scalp acupuncture areas would you treat?",
      "question_hant": "11個月前，一位81歲男性病人因腦血栓而中風，右側手臂與腿部癱瘓。舌質略帶紫色，苔象正常。雙側脈象皆為細弦脈。你會選擇治療哪些頭皮針區域？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "treat the upper 1/5 and middle 2/5 of both the Motor and Sensory Areas on the left side",
