          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "treat the middle 2/5 and lower 2/5 of both the Motor and Sensory Areas on the left side",
          "hant": "治療左側運動區與感覺區的中2/5及下2/5",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "treat the upper 1/5 and middle 2/5 of both the Motor and Sensory Areas on the right side",
          "hant": "治療右側運動區與感覺區的上1/5及中2/5",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The diagnosis is Qi and Blood Stasis in the Channels. The Motor Area is divided into fifths by three regions. There is the Upper 1/5 region, the middle 2/5 region, and the lower 2/5 region. These upper 1/5 of the Motor Area treats contralateral movement disorders of the lower limbs, trunk, spinal cord, and neck. The middle 2/5 area treats contralateral movement disorders of the upper limb. The lower 2/5 of the Motor Area treats bilateral movement disorders of the face and head and also treats dysphasia due caused by a stroke or brain damage. Needling is done from the upper are downward, penetrating the entire section. The Sensory Area is also divided into fifth by three regions. There is the Upper 1/5 region, the middle 2/5 region, and the lower 2/5 region. These areas affect the contralateral side of the body. The upper 1/5 of the Sensory Area treats abnormal sensations and pain in the lower limbs, trunk, back, chest, and neck. The middle 2/5 treats the upper limbs. The lower 2/5 treats face and head disorders such as migraines, trigeminal neuralgia, headache, and TMJ. Needling is done from the upper are downward, penetrating the entire section. For treatment, insert the needles and twirl them for 200 times per minute every 10 minutes. If it is difficult to do needle rotation, electrical stimulation can be used on only two points per session. In treating paralysis after a stroke, needle the appropriate Motor and Sensory areas using contralateral needling to the affected area. As the acupuncturist manipulates the needles, the patient moves the affected limb actively and passively. The patient can exercise the affected limb with or without assistance. During treatment if the patient feels heat, cold, tingling, heaviness, numbness, distention or the sensation of flowing water or electrical sensation in the limb, then that indicates a positive response. The patient can be expected to improve. Initially treatments are given 2-3 times per week until there is a major improvement, then once per week, then every two weeks. A treatment course consists of ten treatments. Scalp acupuncture provides the fastest response to the treatment of paralysis. To make a full recovery scalp acupuncture can be combined with body acupuncture, moxa, massage, and physical therapy. Chinese Scalp Acupuncture, Jason Hao, Lingzhi Hao, 2017, page 47, 59, 51, 86-89",
      "exp_hant": "此為經絡氣血瘀阻之證。運動區分為三個區段，共五等分：上1/5區、中2/5區，以及下2/5區。運動區的上1/5治療對側下肢、軀幹、脊髓及頸部的運動障礙；中2/5治療對側上肢的運動障礙；下2/5則治療雙側顏面與頭部的運動障礙，並能治療中風或腦損傷所致的語言障礙。針刺方式為由上往下透刺整個區段。感覺區同樣分為三個區段、共五等分：上1/5區、中2/5區，以及下2/5區，這些區域皆影響身體對側。感覺區的上1/5治療下肢、軀幹、背部、胸部及頸部的異常感覺與疼痛；中2/5治療上肢；下2/5則治療顏面與頭部病症，如偏頭痛、三叉神經痛、頭痛及顳頜關節疾患。針刺方式同樣為由上往下透刺整個區段。治療時，進針後每10分鐘捻轉200次；若捻轉手法操作不易，每次治療可於其中兩個穴位施以電針刺激。治療中風後的癱瘓時，應在患側對側的相應運動區與感覺區進行針刺。在施術者運針的同時，病人應主動並被動地活動患肢，可在有無他人協助的情況下活動患肢。治療過程中，若病人患肢感到發熱、發冷、麻刺感、沉重感、麻木感、脹感，或有如水流或電流般的感覺，皆代表反應良好，可預期病情將有所改善。初期治療每週2至3次，直到病情有明顯改善後改為每週一次，再改為每兩週一次。十次治療為一個療程。頭皮針對治療癱瘓的反應速度最快。若欲達到完全康復，頭皮針可與體針、灸法、按摩及物理治療合併使用。(出處：Chinese Scalp Acupuncture，郝重耀、郝令莉，2017年，第47、59、51、86-89頁)"
    },
