      "exp_en": "Liver Fire Blazing Upwards. LR-2 (xing jian) is the main point of the formula as it drains Liver Fire. GB-20 (feng chi) drains Liver Fire and descends the yang (important point to use with eye symptoms or headaches from Liver Fire). GB-13 (ben shen) subdues the hyperactive Liver yang and calms the mind. LI-11 (qu chi) clears Heat. SP-6 (san yin jiao) nourishes the yin thereby assisting in draining Liver Fire. If there is a headache tai yang can be selected to clear Liver Fire and alleviate temporal headaches. LR-3 (tai chong) and LR-1 (da dun) can be also selected to drain Liver Fire. LR-1 (da dun) also subdues hyperactive Liver yang. The local points GB-9 (tian chong), GB-8 (shuai gu), GB-6 (xuanli) and GB-1 (tong zi liao) can be selected as local points to calm the ascending Liver Fire that is causing headaches. Reducing needle technique is used. No moxa. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 542; 2005 Edition, page 513; 1989 Edition page 220",
      "exp_hant": "此為肝火上炎之證。行間為方中主穴，能瀉肝火。風池能瀉肝火、降逆陽氣（治療肝火所致眼疾或頭痛的重要穴位）。本神能平抑亢盛之肝陽、寧心安神。曲池能清熱。三陰交能滋陰，有助於瀉肝火。若兼有頭痛，可選用太陽穴以清肝火、緩解顳側頭痛。太衝與大敦亦可用於瀉肝火，大敦並能平抑亢盛之肝陽。天衝、率谷、懸釐及瞳子髎等局部穴位，可用於平息上炎所致的肝火性頭痛。針法用瀉法，不用灸法。(出處：The Foundations of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia，2015年，第542頁；2005年版，第513頁；1989年版，第220頁)"
