    {
      "number": 492,
      "question_en": "A 30 year-old male patient has had hiccups for the past ten days. He presented with difficulty breathing, frequent hiccups throughout the day but worse after meals. He also had a sense of fullness in the abdomen, acid reflux, and contracting pain in the chest and hypochondrium. The pulse was wiry and the tongue had a thin-white coating. He was treated with REN-17 (shanzhong), BL-17 (geshu), REN-12 (zhongwan), PC-6 (neiguan), and ST-36 (zusanli). He set up an appointment for the following week but because of stress at work it was postponed. He returns two weeks later. He now reports distending pain in the upper abdomen that is worse after meals. Chest constriction, acid reflux and frequent belching are still present but slightly less intense. His bowel movements and urination were previously normal but now the bowel movements are two times per day with odorous loose stools and the urination is dark yellow. The tongue is slightly red and with a sticky-yellow coating. The pulse is wiry-rolling. The new prescription is PC-6 (neiguan), LR-3 (taichong), ST-36 (zusanli), REN-12 (zhongwan), and SP-6 (sanyinjiao}. Which other point would you add to the new prescription?",
      "question_hant": "一名30歲男性病患打嗝已持續十天，呼吸不順，整日頻繁打嗝、餐後尤甚，並伴有腹部脹滿感、泛酸及胸脅部拘急疼痛。脈弦，舌苔薄白。曾以 REN-17 (shanzhong) 膻中、BL-17 (geshu) 膈俞、REN-12 (zhongwan) 中脘、PC-6 (neiguan) 內關及 ST-36 (zusanli) 足三里治療。他原本預約下週複診，但因工作壓力而延後，兩週後才回診。此時主訴上腹部脹痛，餐後加重；胸悶、泛酸及頻繁噯氣仍在但程度略減。原本大便及小便正常，現則變為一日兩次、大便臭穢質稀，小便深黃。舌略紅，苔黃膩，脈弦滑。新處方為 PC-6 (neiguan) 內關、LR-3 (taichong) 太衝、ST-36 (zusanli) 足三里、REN-12 (zhongwan) 中脘及 SP-6 (sanyinjiao) 三陰交。此新處方還應再加入下列哪一個穴位？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "DU-9 (zhiyang)",
          "hant": "至陽",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "DU-8 (jinsuo)",
          "hant": "筋縮",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "DU-12 (shenzhu)",
          "hant": "身柱",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "extra point huanmen",
          "hant": "患門",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The original clinical presentation points to Liver qi stasis (hypochondrium distention, wiry pulse) attacking the Stomach (acid reflux, belching, abdominal fullness). REN-17 and BL-17 were chosen to comforts the chest, relax the diaphragm, and smooth the qi. REN-12 and ST-36 harmonize the Stomach and descend the qi. PC-6 regulates-smooths the Liver qi, descends rebellious Stomach qi, and opens the chest. When he returned the energetic configuration changed to Liver qi stasis transforming to heat (slightly red tongue, wiry pulse). The Liver qi stasis disrupted the downward flow of Stomach (acid reflux, belching, epigastric pain). The Liver heat disrupted the Spleen function of transforming fluids resulting in damp-heat (dark urine, smelly loose stools, rolling pulse, sticky-yellow coating). The treatment principle is to smooth and clear Liver qi, descend Stomach qi, and transform Spleen damp-heat. PC-6 moves Liver qi through the relationship between the Liver and Pericardium channels within Terminal Yin. PC-6 assists REN-12 and ST-36 in regulating Earth and assists Wood in smoothing qi. LR-3 moves Liver qi. When Liver qi transforms to heat, the focus of the treatment is to smooth and clear Liver qi which is the source of the heat rather than directly clearing heat. ST-36 harmonizes the Stomach, fortifies Spleen, and resolves dampness. REN-12 harmonizes the middle burner and descends rebellion, regulates qi, and alleviates pain. ST-36 and REN-12 reinforce each other to descend the qi and harmonize the middler burner. SP-6 tonifes the Spleen, resolves dampness and heat, harmonizes the Liver, and regulates urination. DU-9 is located at the level of BL-17, the diaphragm shu point. The diaphragm separates the upper and middle jiao. DU-9 acts on the middle jiao by draining dampness or damp-heat as well as tonifying the Spleen and Stomach. DU-9 acts on the upper jiao by unbinding the chest and diaphragm. DU-9 is a major point in the treatment of jaundice. DU-8 is called sinew contraction and pacifies wind to relieves spasms. DU-12 clears Lung and Heart heat. Extra point huanmen is located 1.5 cun lateral to the spinous process of the 5th thoracic vertebra. Its action is to nourish yin, clear heat, and tonify qi. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 536, 611; A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 541; Case Studies from the Medical Records, Zhu Bing, 2011, page 50, 56",
      "exp_hant": "原本的臨床表現顯示肝氣鬱結（脅肋脹滿、脈弦）橫逆犯胃（泛酸、噯氣、腹脹）。選用 REN-17 (shanzhong) 膻中與 BL-17 (geshu) 膈俞以寬胸、鬆解橫膈、順氣；REN-12 (zhongwan) 中脘與 ST-36 (zusanli) 足三里和胃降氣；PC-6 (neiguan) 內關則疏調肝氣、降逆和胃、寬胸理氣。病患複診時，證型已轉變為肝鬱化熱（舌略紅、脈弦），肝氣鬱結擾亂胃氣下降（泛酸、噯氣、胃脘痛），肝熱又影響脾之運化水濕功能，形成濕熱（小便深黃、大便臭穢質稀、脈滑、苔黃膩）。此時治則為疏肝清熱、降胃氣、化脾濕熱。PC-6 (neiguan) 內關透過肝與心包同屬厥陰的關係以行肝氣，並協助 REN-12 (zhongwan) 中脘與 ST-36 (zusanli) 足三里調理脾胃（土），輔助肝（木）疏泄。LR-3 (taichong) 太衝行肝氣；當肝氣化熱時，治療重點應在疏肝清肝以治其熱之源，而非直接清熱。ST-36 (zusanli) 足三里和胃健脾化濕；REN-12 (zhongwan) 中脘和中降逆、理氣止痛，兩者相輔以降氣和中；SP-6 (sanyinjiao) 三陰交健脾化濕熱、調肝、利尿。DU-9 (zhiyang) 至陽與膈俞（BL-17）同一水平，橫膈分隔上焦與中焦，至陽作用於中焦可袪濕或化濕熱並健脾胃，作用於上焦則可寬胸利膈，是治療黃疸的要穴。DU-8 (jinsuo) 筋縮能息風解痙。DU-12 (shenzhu) 身柱能清肺熱與心熱。經外奇穴患門位於第五胸椎棘突旁開1.5寸，功能為滋陰清熱、補氣。參考資料：《The Foundations of Chinese Medicine》，Maciocia，2015年，第536、611頁；《A Manual of Acupuncture》，Deadman，第2版，第541頁；《Case Studies from the Medical Records》，朱兵，2011年，第50、56頁。"
    },
    {
      "number": 493,
      "question_en": "A 50 year-old patient had a stroke last year which affected the left side of her brain. She was paralyzed on the right side and could not speak. She received both physical and speech therapy. The aphasia improved gradually. Sometimes she has difficulty naming objects but also could not speak in long sentences. Her paralysis completely recovered but still had a problem with her speech. Her tongue was purple and thin with a white coating. The pulses were fine and wiry. Which scalp acupuncture area(s) would you treat?",
      "question_hant": "一名50歲病患去年中風，影響左側大腦，導致右側偏癱且無法言語，曾接受物理治療與語言治療，失語症狀逐漸改善。她有時難以說出物品名稱，也無法說出較長的句子。偏癱已完全恢復，但語言問題仍然存在。舌質紫且瘦薄，苔白，脈細弦。此時應治療下列哪個（些）頭皮針區？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Speech area I",
          "hant": "語言一區",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Speech area III",
          "hant": "語言三區",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Speech areas I and III",
          "hant": "語言一區與三區",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Speech area II",
          "hant": "語言二區",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The TCM diagnosis is qi stasis and blood stasis obstructing the orifices. The type of aphasia she has is called nominal aphasia (also called anomic aphasia). Nominal is a type of aphasia where an individual has word retrieval failures and cannot express the words they want to say. It is an inability to name objects, qualities, or conditions. SPEECH AREA II is located by finding the parietal eminence. It is a line parallel to the anterior-posterior line 2 cm posteriorly and runs 2 cm. Direction of needling can go posterior to anterior or anterior to posterior, needling the entire area. Treat this point bilaterally and rotate the needle 200 times per minute for 1-3 minutes, every 10 minutes for a total of 30-45 minutes. Or you can use electrical stimulation. It is helpful to have the patient talk during treatment. If during the treatment the patient experiences heat, cold, heaviness, distention, or electricity moving in the throat and tongue, then it is a good sign that the treatment will produce result. SPEECH AREA I treats motor aphasia is also called Broca's aphasia as it corresponds to Broca's area in the brain which is the area that controls muscles of tongue and mouth that form speech. Broca's aphasia an inability to speak. The patient understands written and spoken words but has difficulty uttering the words. Speech area I overlaps the lower 2/5 of the Motor area. This area treats dysarthia, dysphonia, or motor aphasia after a stroke or brain injury to the area that control the muscles of speech. This area is needled bilaterally for motor aphasia, needling from the upper to the lower part and penetrating the entire line. SPEECH AREA III overlies Wernicke's area in the brain. Wernicke's aphasia (also knowns as receptive aphasia, sensory aphasia, or posterior aphasia) is a type of aphasia in which the patient has difficulty understanding written and spoken language. It is an inability to understand written or spoken language due to disease of the auditory and visual word centers. It is like a word blindness. Speech Area III is located on a horizontal line 1.5 cm superior to the ear apex and begins at the midpoint of the Vertigo and Hearing area and runs 4 cm posterior. The direction of needling can go posterior to anterior or anterior to posterior, needling the entire area. Chinese Scalp Acupuncture, Jason Hao, Lingzhi Hao, 2017, page 55, 59, 163",
      "exp_hant": "中醫診斷為氣滯血瘀、阻閉清竅。此病患的失語類型稱為命名性失語（又稱健忘性失語），表現為詞語提取困難、無法說出想表達的字詞，即無法說出物品、性質或狀態的名稱。語言二區的定位方法為先找到頂結節，取一條與前後正中線平行、其後方2公分處的線，長2公分。進針方向可由後向前或由前向後，貫穿整個區域。雙側同時治療，每分鐘捻轉約200次，每次持續1至3分鐘，每隔10分鐘捻轉一次，總療程30至45分鐘，亦可改用電針。治療時讓病患說話有助療效；若治療過程中病患感到咽喉與舌部出現發熱、發涼、沉重、脹感或如觸電般的感覺，則是療效良好的徵兆。語言一區用於治療運動性失語，又稱布洛卡失語症，對應大腦布洛卡區，即控制舌與口部言語肌肉的區域。布洛卡失語症患者無法言語，但仍能理解書面與口語文字，僅是發音表達困難。語言一區與運動區下2/5重疊，用於治療中風或腦部言語肌肉控制區受損後的構音障礙、發聲障礙或運動性失語。此區雙側同時針刺治療運動性失語，由上而下貫穿整條線。語言三區則對應大腦的韋尼克區。韋尼克失語症（又稱感覺性失語、接受性失語或後失語）患者難以理解書面與口語語言，即因聽覺與視覺語詞中樞病變而無法理解文字或言語，如同「文字失明」。語言三區位於耳尖上方1.5公分的水平線上，起於暈聽區中點，向後延伸4公分。進針方向可由後向前或由前向後，貫穿整個區域。參考資料：《Chinese Scalp Acupuncture》，郝重耀（Jason Hao）、郝玲芝（Lingzhi Hao），2017年，第55、59、163頁。"
    },
    {
