      ],
      "exp_en": "The Extraordinary Vessels all derive directly or indirectly from the Kidneys. The ren mai, du mai, and chong mai directly start in the lower jiao in the space between the Kidneys (the lower dan tian). Both the Uterus and Room of Sperm reside in the lower dan tian. These three (ren, du, and chong) then flow to REN-1 from where each take a different pathway with the ren mai ascending the abdominal midline, the du mai ascending the posterior midline, and the chong mai ascending along side the Kidney channel in the abdomen. The ren, du, and chong mai are considered three branches of the same vessel and are seen as the source from which the other five Extraordinary Vessels originate. For example, when the qi of chong mai reaches KI-6, BL-62, and GB-26 then the yin and yang qiao mai and the dai mai arise. Since the Extraordinary Vessels directly or indirectly originate in the Kidneys they all have a connection to Kidney Essence which they all circulate (particularly the ren, du, and chong mai). The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 869, 876, 878",
      "exp_hant": "奇經八脈皆直接或間接源於腎。任脈、督脈與衝脈直接起於下焦、兩腎之間（下丹田），子宮與精室皆位於下丹田。此三脈（任、督、衝）皆流注至 REN-1 (huiyin) 會陰，再各自循行不同路徑：任脈上行於腹部正中線，督脈上行於背部正中線，衝脈則沿腎經於腹部上行。任、督、衝三脈被視為同一脈的三個分支，也是其餘五條奇經的源頭。例如，當衝脈之氣行至 KI-6 (zhaohai) 照海、BL-62 (shenmai) 申脈與 GB-26 (dai mai) 帶脈時，即分別衍生出陰蹻脈、陽蹻脈與帶脈。由於奇經八脈皆直接或間接源於腎，故皆與腎精有所聯繫並循行輸布腎精（尤以任、督、衝三脈為甚）。參考資料：《The Foundations of Chinese Medicine》，Maciocia，2015年，第869、876、878頁。"
