      ],
      "exp_en": "The Triple Burner luo-connecting channel separates from the Triple Burner primary channel at TB-5 (wai guan), ascends the posterior part of the arm to the shoulder, and converges with the Pericardium primary channel in the chest. Wai guan is translated as outer gate, in contrast to PC-6 (nei guan) inner gate. The Triple Burner channel together with the Gall Bladder channel is part of the shao yang division which is a hinge between tai yang (greater yang) and yang ming (bright yang). What this means is that the shao yang channels can have an influence on both tai yang and bright yang. TB-5 (wai guan) can harmonize the yang, subdue Liver yang, and expel external and internal wind. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 388",
      "exp_hant": "三焦經之絡脈於 TB-5 (wai guan) 外關處由三焦正經分出，沿手臂後側上行至肩部，並在胸部與心包正經匯合。外關意為「外側之關」，與 PC-6 (nei guan) 內關的「內側之關」相對應。三焦經與膽經同屬少陽，是太陽與陽明之間的樞紐，這代表少陽經能同時影響太陽與陽明。TB-5 (wai guan) 外關能調和陽氣、平抑肝陽、袪除內外之風。參考資料：《A Manual of Acupuncture》，Deadman，第2版，第388頁。"
    },
