      "exp_en": "Bensky writes that this point is located on the posterior, superior part of the antitragus. CAM describes the location as at the posterior, superior corner of the lateral aspect of the antitragus. CAM writes that the occiput point is used for sedation and analgesia. It eases the mind and removes wind. It is indicated for dizziness, insomnia, and headache, etc. Bensky lists this point for neuropsychiatric disorders and disorders due to meningeal irritation such as convulsions, locked jaw, stiffness on the nape of the neck and psychosis. It can also prevent sea sickness. It treats skin diseases, eye disorders, inflammation,pain, and shock. CAM, 3rd Edition, pages 520; CAM, 4th Edition, page 426; Bensky, 1981, page 484",
      "exp_hant": "Bensky 記載此穴位於對耳屏的後上部；CAM 則描述其位置在對耳屏外側面的後上角。CAM 記載「枕」穴具有鎮靜止痛之效，能安神袪風，主治眩暈、失眠、頭痛等症。Bensky 則將此穴列為治療神經精神疾患及腦膜刺激徵候（如抽搐、牙關緊閉、頸項強直、精神疾病）之用穴，亦可預防暈船，並治療皮膚病、眼疾、發炎、疼痛與休克。參考資料：CAM，第3版，第520頁；CAM，第4版，第426頁；Bensky，1981年，第484頁。"
    },
