    {
      "number": 505,
      "question_en": "What should the practitioner wear when removing cups that have blood in them?",
      "question_hant": "移除含血的罐具時，執業者應配戴下列何種防護裝備？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "gloves",
          "hant": "手套",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "gloves and eye protection",
          "hant": "手套與護目裝備",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "lab coat and gloves",
          "hant": "實驗衣與手套",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "two sets of gloves",
          "hant": "兩層手套",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "When wet cupping is used, follow standard precautions, maintain a clean field, and follow hand sanitation. When a cup contains blood, the vacuum from the cup should be slowly released. The acupuncturist should wear gloves and protective eyewear when the cup is being removed as there is the possibility that the blood can splash or aerosolize onto the hands, eyes, and to other objects in the treatment room. Clean the site of skin puncture and discard the gauze, cotton swab, or paper towel used to collect the blood in the biohazard trash. If single-use cups were used, they should also be put in the biohazard trash. If the cups are reusable, they must be cleaned with soap and water and must be disinfected with a high-level disinfectant for medical devices or sterilized in an autoclave. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 36",
      "exp_hant": "施行刺絡拔罐（濕罐）時，應遵循標準防護措施，維持治療區域清潔並確實執行手部衛生。當罐內有血液時，應緩慢釋放罐內負壓。移除罐具時，執業者應配戴手套與護目裝備，因為血液可能噴濺或形成氣霧，接觸到手部、眼睛或治療室內其他物品。清潔穿刺部位後，將用於吸血的紗布、棉球或紙巾丟棄於生物危害廢棄物容器中。若使用一次性罐具，亦應丟棄於生物危害廢棄物容器；若為可重複使用的罐具，則須以肥皂水清洗後，再以醫療器材高效消毒劑消毒或以高壓滅菌釜滅菌。參考資料：《Clean Needle Technique》，第7版，第36頁。"
    },
    {
      "number": 506,
      "question_en": "In using an electrical point location device which body points are usually selected for setting the sensitivity level of the device?",
      "question_hant": "使用電子測穴儀時，通常選用身體上的哪個穴位來設定儀器的靈敏度？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "KI-1 or DU-20",
          "hant": "湧泉或百會",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "REN-4 or taiyang",
          "hant": "關元或太陽",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "SP-6 or KI-3",
          "hant": "三陰交或太谿",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "yintang or LI-4",
          "hant": "印堂或合谷",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "For the ear the reference points are Point Zero or shenmen. Point location devices detect areas of low skin resistance to help locate the acupuncture point. If the sensitivity level of the location device is set too low (less current) it will pick less points. If set too high (more current) it will detect too many points. Also, if it is set too high then the device will start to act as a treatment. Electrical skin resistance can help monitor treatment progress, confirm diagnosis, as well as for point location. The point location function of the device is subject to error as it is dependent on the skin condition which varies (moist, dryness) in different areas and the ability of the practitioner to apply consistent pressure on different areas. Skin resistance is also low over superficial veins or bony prominences. Electroacupuncture A Practical Manual and Resource, Mayor, 2007, page 331",
      "exp_hant": "耳穴的參考點則為零點（Point Zero）或神門穴。測穴儀是透過偵測皮膚電阻較低的區域來協助定位穴位。若儀器靈敏度設定過低（電流較小），偵測到的穴位會較少；若設定過高（電流較大），則會偵測到過多穴位，甚至可能使儀器本身產生治療作用。皮膚電阻可用於監測療效進展、輔助診斷及穴位定位；然而由於皮膚狀況（潮濕或乾燥程度）因部位而異，且執業者施加壓力的一致性也會有所影響，故此定位功能仍有誤差可能。淺表靜脈或骨性隆起處的皮膚電阻通常也較低。參考資料：《Electroacupuncture: A Practical Manual and Resource》，Mayor，2007年，第331頁。"
    },
