        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Phlegm-Damp. ST-36 (zu san li) and REN-12 (zhong wan) strengthen the Spleen and Stomach to resolve Dampness and Phlegm and regulate the middle jiao. PC-6 (nei guan) can be added to strengthen the effect of descending rebellious Stomach qi. GB-20 (feng chi) and LR-3 (tai chong) extinguish Wind. TB-17 (yi feng) and SI-19 (ting gong) restore qi circulation in channels around the ear. In TCM, aural vertigo can be due to Damp-Phlegm blocking the middle burner and suppressing the cleansing yang (qi of breathing which rises to the head to maintain clarity in the senses). It can also be due to Kidney yin depletion causing Liver yang to ascend in the form of wind. Acupuncture a Comprehensive Text, Bensky, 1981, in section starting on page 684",
      "exp_hant": "此為痰濕證。ST-36 (zu san li) 足三里與 REN-12 (zhong wan) 中脘能健脾和胃、化痰袪濕、調理中焦；亦可加入 PC-6 (nei guan) 內關以加強降逆和胃之效。GB-20 (feng chi) 風池與 LR-3 (tai chong) 太衝息風；TB-17 (yi feng) 翳風與 SI-19 (ting gong) 聽宮則能疏通耳周經氣。中醫理論認為，耳源性眩暈可因痰濕阻遏中焦、抑遏清陽（上升頭部以維持感官清明之氣）所致，亦可因腎陰虧虛導致肝陽上亢化風而引起。參考資料：《Acupuncture: A Comprehensive Text》，Bensky，1981年，第684頁起之章節。"
    },
