      "exp_en": "A broken needle under the skin or just a little bit out of the skin surface can be due to a poor quality needle, an eroded base of the needle, a strong muscle spasm, a sudden movement by the patient or from forcefully withdrawing a stuck needle. To prevent the needle from going deeper, the patient needs to stay calm and still. If the broken part protrudes from the skin, remove it with forceps. If the broken needle is at the same level of the skin, press around the tissue until the broken end is exposed, and remove with forceps. If the needle is completely under the skin, it should be surgically removed. tcmtests.com, January 2014",
      "exp_hant": "斷針可能露出皮膚外一小部分，也可能完全埋於皮下，其成因可能是針具品質不佳、針柄鏽蝕、肌肉強烈痙攣、病患突然移動，或強行拔出滯針所致。為避免斷針繼續深入，病患應保持鎮定並靜止不動。若斷端露出皮膚外，可直接以鑷子夾出；若斷端與皮膚表面齊平，則應按壓周圍組織直到斷端露出後再以鑷子夾出；若斷針完全埋於皮下，則應以外科手術方式取出。參考資料：tcmtests.com，2014年1月。"
