      "exp_en": "This is the most complete answer. The Small Intestine and Gall Bladder meridians do not go to the lips. A branch of the Liver meridian descends from the eye through the cheek and encircles the inner surface of the lips. A branch of the Large Intestine meridian goes from the gums to ST-4, curves around the upper lip and crosses to the opposite side at DU-26. A branch of the Stomach meridian circles around the lips and meets with REN-24. The interior portion of the Ren Mai winds around the mouth, connecting to DU-28 and terminates below ST-1. Deadman, 2nd Edition, pages 96, 125, 470, 495; the Chong Mai runs along both sides of the abdomen, goes up to the throat and curves around the lips",
