      "exp_en": "Yin shu-stream points treat disorders of zang. They are the main channel points that are used to tonify and harmonize their respective zang. LU-9 tonifies Lung qi and yin. SP-3 tonifies Spleen qi and yang. HT-7 tonifies and nourishes the Heart qi, Blood, yin, and yang. KI-3 tonifies Kidney yin, qi, and yang. PC-7 has a strong effect on calming the Shen when affected by Heat. LR-3 treats any Liver pattern whether due to deficiency or excess. In contrast, the yang shu-stream points are selected not to treat organ patterns but to treat channel patterns. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2001, page 34",
      "exp_hant": "正確答案為俞穴。陰經俞穴主治五臟病證，是各經用以補益、調和其相應臟腑的主要穴位。LU-9（太淵）補肺氣肺陰；SP-3（太白）補脾氣脾陽；HT-7（神門）補養心氣、心血、心陰、心陽；KI-3（太谿）補腎陰、腎氣、腎陽；PC-7（大陵）對熱擾心神有顯著鎮靜安神之效；LR-3（太衝）無論肝之虛實皆可治療。相對而言，陽經俞穴並非用以治療臟腑病證，而是用以治療經絡病證。參考資料：《A Manual of Acupuncture》，Deadman，2001年版，第34頁。"
