    {
      "number": 595,
      "question_en": "How does the \"Great Compendium of Acupuncture\" advise the needling of the points associated with the Extraordinary Vessels?",
      "question_hant": "《針灸大成》建議如何針刺奇經八脈相關的穴位？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "needle the Opening point on one side and the Associated point on the other side",
          "hant": "一側先刺開穴，另一側刺配穴",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "needle the Opening point and Associated point unilaterally",
          "hant": "開穴與配穴皆刺同一側",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "only needle the Opening point bilaterally",
          "hant": "僅雙側刺開穴",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "first needle the Opening point and then needle the Associated point",
          "hant": "先刺開穴，再刺配穴",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "All of these are valid techniques for needling the Opening and Associated points of the Extraordinary Vessels. The Great Compendium of Acupuncture recommends first needling the Opening point and then needling the Associated point. This is called the \"guest-host\" technique in which the Opening point (host) of the vessel is first needled and then followed by needling the Associated point (guest). Maciocia recommends first needling the Opening point on one side and the Associated point on the opposite side. Further, he assigns needling the Opening point on the left side and the Associated point on the right side for men. It is vice versa for women. Needling the Opening and Associated points unilaterally is selected to treat unilateral disorders such as one sided back pain, one sided headache, bi-syndrome, or the after effect of a Wind-Stroke. The needles are usually removed in the reverse order than they were inserted. The Opening and Associated points are selected when there is a need to influence the areas targeted by an Extraordinary Vessel or to absorb and regulate an excess such as stagnant qi or blood. For example, a patient has an acute itchy nose from an attack of wind-heat and also has an itchy anus due to damp-heat. Each disorder can be treated separately via pattern diagnosis (expel wind-heat, drain damp and clear heat). However, both disorders can be treated via the Governing Vessel's area of influence on the nose and anus without having to consider the cause (wind-heat, damp-heat) of each pattern. This is done by first needling SI-3 and then needling BL-62. These two points treat the whole area under the direct influence of the Governing Vessel (du mai). Individual points on the Extraordinary Vessels only influence the local area and DO NOT influence the totality of the areas of the vessel. Only the Opening and Closing points do that. However, individual points on the vessel can be combined with the Opening and Associated points to direct the energy of that Vessel to that area. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 880-881",
      "exp_hant": "正確答案為先刺開穴，再刺配穴。以上皆為針刺奇經開穴與配穴的可行方法。《針灸大成》建議先針開穴，再針配穴，此即所謂「主客」法，先刺該經之「主」（開穴），再刺其「客」（配穴）。馬萬里（Maciocia）建議一側先刺開穴、對側刺配穴，並進一步指出男性應左側刺開穴、右側刺配穴，女性則相反。單側同刺開穴與配穴則用於治療單側病證，如單側腰痛、單側頭痛、痺證，或中風後遺症。出針時通常依相反於進針的順序拔出。選用開穴與配穴，是為了影響某條奇經所主之區域，或吸納並調節如氣滯、血瘀等過盛之邪。例如，一名患者因外感風熱急性鼻癢，同時因濕熱肛門搔癢，兩種病證可分別依證型論治（袪風熱、化濕清熱）。然而，此二證亦可藉督脈所主之鼻與肛門區域，不必考量各自病因（風熱、濕熱），一併治療，作法是先針SI-3（後谿），再針BL-62（申脈）。此二穴能治療督脈直接主司之全部區域。奇經個別穴位僅能影響局部，並不能影響整條經脈所主之全部區域，唯有開穴與閉穴（即配穴）方能如此。然而，奇經上的個別穴位仍可與開穴、配穴合用，以引導該經之氣至該區域。參考資料：《Foundations of Chinese Medicine》，Maciocia，2015年版，第880-881頁。"
    },
    {
      "number": 596,
      "question_en": "What is accurate about the Du Mai?",
      "question_hant": "關於督脈，下列敘述何者正確？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
