          "key": "D",
          "en": "the Du Mai has three internal branches",
          "hant": "督脈有三條內行支",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The Du Mai has three internal branches. A branch of the du mai goes to the Kidney. A branch of Du Mai goes from BL-12 (feng men) to the Kidneys. An internal branch enters the brain at DU-16 (feng fu). The du mai only connects with the Kidneys and Heart organs. The du mai or Governing Vessel has an external pathway with three internal branches. The primary pathway, which is what is shown in illustrations, starts in the lower abdomen, emerges at the perineum, goes to DU-1 and ascends to nape of neck (DU-16) where a branch it enters the brain and goes to DU-20. The external branch at DU-16 goes ascends to the top of the head, descends to terminate at DU-28. One internal branch starts in the lower abdomen, goes to genitals and perineum, circles the anus, ascends the spinal column to enter the Kidneys. The second internal branch starts at the lower abdomen, circles the genitals, ascends the midline to the navel, passes through the Heart, circles the mouth, and ascends below the middle of the eyes. The third branch starts at BL-1, follows the Bladder channel bilaterally, then converges at the vertex to enter the brain, emerges at DU-16 where it bifurcates and goes bilaterally to BL-12 and further descends to enter the Kidneys. Through the internal branches one can see how moxa on DU-14 can be selected to tonify both Heart and Kidney yang, and strengthen will power (Kidneys) and the Mind (Heart). One can see how DU-20 can be selected to treat the brain and lift depression because of a branch that goes from DU-20 to DU-16. REN-1 and REN-24 are categorized as meeting points of Du Mai and Ren Mai. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 529",
      "exp_hant": "正確答案為督脈有三條內行支。督脈有一分支通向腎。督脈有一分支自BL-12 (feng men) 風門通向腎。有一內行支於DU-16 (feng fu) 風府處入腦。督脈僅與腎、心兩臟相連。督脈（即Governing Vessel）具有一條外行主幹路徑及三條內行分支。圖示中常見的主要路徑起於小腹，出於會陰，行至DU-1（長強），沿脊柱上行至項後（DU-16），於此處分出一支入腦並上達DU-20（百會）。DU-16處的外行支則繼續上行至頭頂，再下行止於DU-28（齦交）。第一條內行支起於小腹，行於生殖器與會陰，環繞肛門，沿脊柱上行入腎。第二條內行支起於小腹，環繞生殖器，沿正中線上行至臍，貫心，環口，上行至兩目中間下方。第三條內行支起於BL-1（睛明），沿膀胱經雙側下行，於頭頂會合入腦，於DU-16處分為兩支，分別通向雙側BL-12（風門），再下行入腎。由這些內行支可理解為何DU-14（大椎）施灸能同補心陽與腎陽，並強志（腎）安神（心）。也可理解DU-20（百會）為何能治腦病、提振情緒低落，因其有一分支通向DU-16。REN-1（會陰）與REN-24（承漿）則歸類為督脈與任脈的交會穴。參考資料：《A Manual of Acupuncture》，Deadman 第2版，第529頁。"
    },
