      "exp_en": "A clean field is an area where sterile acupuncture needles and other clean or sterile tools can be prepared and maintained to reduce the possibility of contamination. The clean field should be clean, dry and on a flat surface. The treatment table is not a suitable location for the clean field. A treatment table increases the risk of the patient accidentally knocking over the clean field. The surface of the clean field needs to be cleaned with a low-level disinfectant NOT after each patient but at least once daily. A clean field can consist of paper towel, table paper, a clean metal tray with a paper barrier or a metal tray cleaned with a disinfectant between each patient use. It is strongly recommended to keep sterile items (needles) in the center of the field and clean items (cotton balls) near the edges. In setting up a clean field, hand sanitation guidelines need to be followed. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 70, 71, 74",
      "exp_hant": "正確答案為每位患者皆須重新建立清潔區，並將未拆封的棉片放置於清潔區。清潔區是準備並維持無菌針具及其他清潔或無菌器械的區域，以降低污染的可能性。清潔區應保持乾淨、乾燥，並置於平坦表面。治療床並不適合作為清潔區，因治療床會增加患者不慎碰倒清潔區的風險。清潔區表面並非每位患者使用後皆須以低效消毒劑清潔，而是至少每日清潔一次。清潔區可由紙巾、治療床紙、附紙質隔層的清潔金屬托盤，或每次患者使用間以消毒劑清潔的金屬托盤構成。強烈建議將無菌物品（針具）置於清潔區中央，清潔物品（棉球）置於邊緣。設置清潔區時，仍須遵循洗手衛生規範。參考資料：《Clean Needle Technique》第7版，第70、71、74頁。"
