      "exp_en": "Any health care worker who can be anticipated to have contact with blood during their job performance are considered to have occupational exposure and to be at risk of being infected with HBV. OSHA recommends: \"The vaccination must be offered after the worker is trained and within 10 days of initial assignment to a job where there is occupational exposure, unless the worker has previously received the vaccine series, antibody testing has revealed that the worker is immune, or the vaccine is contraindicated for medical reasons. The employer must obtain a written opinion from the licensed health care professional within 15 days of the completion of the evaluation for vaccination. This written opinion is limited to whether hepatitis B vaccination is indicated for the worker and if the worker has received the vaccination.\". Acupuncture Risk Management, Kailin, page 68",
      "exp_hant": "正確答案為10天。任何在職務執行過程中可能接觸血液的醫療從業人員，皆被視為具有職業暴露風險，可能感染B型肝炎病毒（HBV）。OSHA建議：「疫苗應於員工完成訓練後、且於首次被指派至具有職業暴露風險之職務起10天內提供，除非該員工已完成疫苗接種、抗體檢測顯示已具免疫力，或因醫療因素不適合接種。雇主須於評估完成後15天內，取得合格醫療專業人員之書面意見，該意見僅限於說明該員工是否適合接種B型肝炎疫苗，以及是否已完成接種。」參考資料：《Acupuncture Risk Management》，Kailin，第68頁。"
