          "hant": "第一類醫療器材",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "There is no Class IV category. The FDA sometimes classifies devices which are uregulated as either unclassified or as Class III. The FDA website search for medical devices gives no result for cupping. Class I Devices are evaluated at the lowest level of risk of all medical devices and are required to comply with the lowest level of regulatory control. Examples of Class I devices are elastic bandages, dental floss and enemas. Class II devices are simple devices, though they are more complicated than Class I devices. They are considered to be at slightly higher risk than Class I devices and require more stringent controls to provide assurance of their safety and effectiveness. Examples of Class II devices are condoms, pregnancy testing kits and powered wheelchairs. Class III devices are generally considered to be the most complex devices. They are considered to be at the highest risk and require more stringent controls to provide assurance of their safety and effectiveness. Examples of Class III devices are implantable pacemakers and breast implants.",
      "exp_hant": "正確答案為未分類醫療器材。並無所謂「第四類」的分類。FDA有時會將未受規範的器材歸類為未分類或第三類。在FDA網站上搜尋醫療器材資料庫，並無拔罐的相關結果。第一類醫療器材是所有醫療器材中風險最低者，僅須遵循最低程度的法規管制，例如彈性繃帶、牙線與灌腸器。第二類醫療器材較為簡單，但較第一類複雜，風險略高於第一類，須有更嚴格的管制以確保其安全性與有效性，例如保險套、驗孕試劑與電動輪椅。第三類醫療器材通常屬於最複雜的器材，風險最高，須有最嚴格的管制以確保其安全性與有效性，例如植入式心律調節器與乳房植入物。"
    },
    {
      "number": 628,
      "question_en": "A 57 year-old male patient has had chest pain since this morning. The sharp pain is on the center of the chest and worsens on inhale. Body temperature is 99.8 F. Pulse rate is 95 beats per minute. During heart auscultation, a grating sound can be heard. Which aspect of the clinical picture most indicate a red flag referral?",
      "question_hant": "一名57歲男性患者自今晨起出現胸痛，疼痛呈銳痛，位於胸部正中央，吸氣時加劇。體溫為華氏99.8度，脈搏每分鐘95下。心臟聽診可聞及摩擦音。臨床表現中，哪一項最能提示需要進行紅旗轉診？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "chest pain, heart sound, body temp",
          "hant": "胸痛、心音、體溫",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "chest pain worse inhaling",
          "hant": "吸氣時胸痛加劇",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "heart sound, pulse rate",
          "hant": "心音、脈搏",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "body temp, pulse rate, patient age",
          "hant": "體溫、脈搏、患者年齡",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the best overall answer. Pericarditis, is inflammation of any of the three layers of the pericardium. The inner visceral layer (visceral pericardium) envelopes the entire heart. The middle fluid layer prevents friction between the visceral layer and the parietal layer. The fibrous parietal layer is the outer layer. Pericarditis can be caused by an infection, tumor, post heart surgery or heart attack. The main symptoms are chest pain, fever, and increase heart rate. The chest pain is sharp, on the center of the chest, worse on inhaling, and worse on leaning forward or lying down. The fever is low-grade (slightly above normal of 98.6 F). The heart rate is less than 100 bpm. During heart auscultation acute pericarditis can be associated with the sound called friction rub. This sounds like a rub, scratching or grating sound similar to leather rubbing against leather. If pericarditis is suspected the patient should be referred for further assessment. The patient can have uncomplicated pericarditis with sharp central chest pain, elevated heart rate, low grade fever, pain while inhaling, and a friction rub heart sound. The patient can also present these signs and symptoms associated with other disorders such as a) heart failure with breathlessness and edema, 2) arrhythmia, 3) heart attack or unstable angina. Pericarditis associated with the preceding disorders is a more complicated situation and requires a more urgent referral. The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 36; wwww.webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "正確答案為胸痛、心音、體溫，此為整體最佳答案。心包炎是心包膜三層組織中任一層發炎的病症。內層的臟層心包包覆整個心臟；中間的液體層可防止臟層與壁層之間的摩擦；外層則為纖維性的壁層心包。心包炎可能由感染、腫瘤、心臟手術後或心肌梗塞引起。主要症狀為胸痛、發熱與心跳加快。此胸痛呈銳痛，位於胸部正中央，吸氣時加劇，前傾或平躺時亦會加劇。發熱通常為低度發熱（略高於正常體溫華氏98.6度）。心跳速率通常低於每分鐘100下。急性心包炎於心臟聽診時可聞及「摩擦音」，聲音類似皮革相互摩擦的刮擦聲。若懷疑心包炎，應將患者轉診作進一步評估。單純性心包炎可表現為胸部正中央銳痛、心跳加快、低度發熱、吸氣時疼痛加劇，以及摩擦音。然而，這些徵象與症狀也可能與其他疾病並存，例如：1）伴隨呼吸困難與水腫的心衰竭；2）心律不整；3）心肌梗塞或不穩定型心絞痛。若心包炎合併上述疾病，情況將更為複雜，需要更緊急的轉診。參考資料：《The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals》，Stephenson，2013年版，第36頁；wwww.webmd.com。"
    },
