    {
      "number": 633,
      "question_en": "What is the general size of an enlarged lymph node, without obvious causes, is suggestive of lymphoma and should be referred?",
      "question_hant": "在沒有明顯病因的情況下，腫大淋巴結達到多大時，應懷疑為淋巴瘤並轉診？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "greater than 2 cm",
          "hant": "大於2公分",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "greater than 3 cm",
          "hant": "大於3公分",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "greater than 1.5 cm",
          "hant": "大於1.5公分",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "greater than 2.5 cm",
          "hant": "大於2.5公分",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "When there is an infection it is unusual for a lymph node to be grossly enlarged. Two cm is almost 8/10 of an inch. Enlarged lymph nodes of this size caused by cancer can be firm and painless. This is characteristic of lymphoma which is cancer of the lymphatic system (Hodgkin disease, non-Hodgkin lymphomas). The constellation of unexplained fever, unexplained weight loss, itching (Hodgkin itch), and lymph node enlargement are suggestive of lymphoma. The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 49",
      "exp_hant": "若是感染引起，淋巴結通常不會明顯腫大。2公分大約等於0.8英吋。由癌症引起的這種大小的腫大淋巴結，可能質地堅硬且無痛，這正是淋巴瘤（淋巴系統癌症，包括何杰金氏病與非何杰金氏淋巴瘤）的特徵。原因不明的發燒、不明原因的體重減輕、搔癢（何杰金氏搔癢）與淋巴結腫大同時出現，即提示淋巴瘤的可能。The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals，Stephenson著，2013年，第49頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 634,
      "question_en": "A 57 year-old female patient has a four day history of a swollen and painful left leg. The patient recently had a total hip arthroplasty due to severe arthritis. She is currently on estrogen-only replacement therapy (HRT) for perimenopausal symptoms. Her BMI is 24. Physical examination shows an edematous left leg below the knee with mild erythema. The right leg appears normal. Homans' sign is positive. The Thomas test is positive. Which of the following answers contain the strongest aspect of the clinical picture that warrants a referral?",
      "question_hant": "一名57歲女性病人，左腿腫脹疼痛已四天。病人近期因嚴重關節炎接受了全髖關節置換術，目前正因更年期症狀使用單純雌激素補充療法（HRT）。她的身體質量指數（BMI）為24。理學檢查顯示左腿膝蓋以下水腫，伴輕微紅斑；右腿外觀正常。霍曼氏徵象（Homans' sign）呈陽性，湯瑪士測試（Thomas test）呈陽性。下列何者包含最能顯示需要轉診的臨床表現重點？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "hip arthroplasty, HRT, Homan's sign, edema and erythema",
          "hant": "髖關節置換術、HRT、霍曼氏徵象、水腫與紅斑",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "postive Homan's sign, BMI 24, perimenopause with HRT",
          "hant": "霍曼氏徵象陽性、BMI 24、更年期併用HRT",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "BMI 24, hip arthroplasty, HRT, Homan's sign, Thomas Test",
          "hant": "BMI 24、髖關節置換術、HRT、霍曼氏徵象、湯瑪士測試",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Homan's sign, Thomas Test, edema and erythema",
          "hant": "霍曼氏徵象、湯瑪士測試、水腫與紅斑",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the best and strongest answer. This patient likely has a deep vein thrombosis (DVT). The BMI is not a factor in this patient. Normal BMI is 18.5 to 24.9. The Thomas test is done with the patient supine with full hip flexion. If the opposite hip lifts off the table, there is likely a fixed flexion deformity. This test is not relevant. This patient has DVT should be referred. DVT classically presents itself as unilateral, swollen, and a painful lower extremity. In the Homan's Sign the foot is dorsiflexed (bend toward shin). If it causes pain it is positive. This sign is often unreliable for DVT. The Virchow's triad refers to the types of conditions that can predispose a patient to the formation of an abnormal thrombus (blood clot). Virchow's triad can be remembered with the acronym SHE. These are Stasis (S), Hypercoagulability (H), and Epithelial Injury (E). S STASIS: The most common conditions that can cause blood flow stasis are surgery (hip or knee), prolonged immobilization, long travel, varicose veins atrial fibrillation, or obesity (normal BMI is 18.5 to 24.9). In these conditions, the blood can pool or stagnate, increasing the risk of platelet coagulation. H HYPERCOAGULABILITY: This means an increased (hyper) risk of coagulation. The most common conditions for hypercoagulability risk are surgery (hip or knee), hormone replacement therapy, birth control pills, pregnancy, or obesity (normal BMI is 18.5 to 24.9). E EPITHELIAL INJURY: The endothelial is the cell layer of cells that lines veins. Damage to this layer can be from a direct or indirect cause stimulates platelets and the coagulation process. Damage to this layer can be due to IV drug abuse, trauma, or surgery (hip or knee). In patients who have a total hip or knee replacement surgery there is venous stasis (S) due to perioperative immobilization, hypercoagulability (H) due to postoperative fibrinolytic shutdown, and epithelial injury (E) caused by the surgery. DVT can lead to blood clots traveling to the lungs (pulmonary embolism). There can be a sudden onset of non-infectuous pleurisy (central chest pain worse with breathing, bloody sputum), breathessness, cyanosis. This would be high-priority emergency referral. The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 176, 43",
      "exp_hant": "這是最佳且最有力的答案。此病人很可能罹患深部靜脈血栓（DVT）。BMI在此病例中並非相關因子，正常BMI範圍為18.5至24.9。湯瑪士測試是讓病人仰臥並將髖關節完全屈曲，若對側髖部因此離開檢查台，則可能表示存在固定性屈曲畸形，此測試與本案無關。此病人的DVT應予轉診。DVT的典型表現為單側下肢腫脹疼痛。霍曼氏徵象是將足部背屈（朝向脛骨方向彎曲），若引發疼痛即為陽性，但此徵象對診斷DVT常不可靠。魏爾嘯三角（Virchow's triad）指的是容易誘發異常血栓形成的幾類狀況，可用字母縮寫SHE來記憶，分別為：血流淤滯（Stasis, S）、高凝血狀態（Hypercoagulability, H）與內皮損傷（Epithelial Injury, E）。S血流淤滯：最常見造成血流淤滯的情況包括手術（髖部或膝部）、長時間制動、長途旅行、靜脈曲張、心房顫動，或肥胖（正常BMI為18.5至24.9）。在這些情況下，血液可能滯留或淤積，增加血小板凝集的風險。H高凝血狀態：指凝血風險增加。最常見造成高凝血狀態風險的情況包括手術（髖部或膝部）、荷爾蒙補充療法、口服避孕藥、懷孕，或肥胖（正常BMI為18.5至24.9）。E內皮損傷：內皮是襯於靜脈內壁的細胞層，直接或間接的原因造成此層受損時會刺激血小板與凝血過程。造成此層損傷的原因可能包括靜脈注射藥物濫用、外傷，或手術（髖部或膝部）。接受全髖或全膝關節置換手術的病人，會因手術期間制動而出現靜脈血流淤滯（S）、因術後纖維蛋白溶解功能受抑而出現高凝血狀態（H），並因手術本身造成內皮損傷（E）。DVT可能導致血栓移行至肺部（肺栓塞），可能突然出現非感染性胸膜炎（呼吸時加劇的中央胸痛、帶血痰）、呼吸困難、發紺，此時應列為高優先等級的緊急轉診。The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals，Stephenson著，2013年，第176、43頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 635,
      "question_en": "A 50 year-old female wanted acupuncture treatment for anxiety, fatigue, and shortness of breath. She was treated by her primary care physician with asthma inhalers but her condition was not helped. She was told that her SOB was due to her anxiety. She had a five-pound weight gain over the past two months. She complained of a sensation of smothering when she laid flat in bed at night. During the physical examination she had mild SOB while at rest. BP was 140/90. The lungs were clear. She denied any chest pain. She had 1+ bilateral pitting ankle edema. Which action would you take?",
      "question_hant": "一名50歲女性希望接受針灸治療其焦慮、疲勞與呼吸困難。她的主治醫師曾以氣喘吸入劑治療，但病情未見改善，並告知她呼吸困難是焦慮所致。過去兩個月體重增加了五磅。她主訴夜間平躺時會有窒息感。理學檢查顯示她在靜止時有輕度呼吸困難，血壓為140/90，肺部聽診清晰，否認胸痛，雙側踝部呈現1+可凹陷性水腫。你會採取下列何種行動？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "timely (within one week) referral to primary care physician",
          "hant": "適時轉診（一週內）至主治醫師",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "semi-urgent (same or next day) referral to primary care physician",
          "hant": "半緊急轉診（當天或隔天）至主治醫師",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "call 911 for emergency assist",
          "hant": "撥打911尋求緊急協助",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "have a family member drive patient to ED",
          "hant": "請家屬開車送病人至急診室",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is bilateral, pitting ankle swelling with SOB. Congestive heart failure (CHF) is assumed present until proven otherwise. Early signs of CHF include fatigue, edema of the ankles, SOB, and breathing difficulties while lying flat. The referral depends on the severity of the condition. Patients with slight pitting edema and mild SOB should have a semi-urgent referral to their primary care physician. Patients with moderate SOB and edema should be sent to the nearest ED for a quick transport by a friend or family member. If the CHF patient has chest pain, severe SOB, or cyanosis then 911 should be called. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 175-176",
      "exp_hant": "警訊徵象為雙側可凹陷性踝部水腫合併呼吸困難。在排除其他可能性之前，應假設病人罹患鬱血性心臟衰竭（CHF）。CHF的早期徵象包括疲勞、踝部水腫、呼吸困難，以及平躺時呼吸不順。轉診的急迫程度取決於病情嚴重度：輕度可凹陷性水腫合併輕度呼吸困難的病人，應半緊急轉診至主治醫師；中度呼吸困難合併水腫的病人，應請親友迅速送往最近的急診室；若CHF病人出現胸痛、嚴重呼吸困難或發紺，則應撥打911。An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals，Anzaldua著，2012年，第175-176頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 636,
      "question_en": "A 66 year-old female patient reports dizziness and shortness of breath while supine on the treatment table. The pulse rate is very rapid. A continuous pulse rate of _____ beats per minute not returning to a normal rate after _____ minutes is ________ referral.",
      "question_hant": "一名66歲女性病人在治療床上平躺時，主訴頭暈與呼吸困難，脈搏非常快速。持續脈搏率達每分鐘_____下，且經過_____分鐘後仍未恢復正常，屬於________轉診。",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "200, 2, an urgent",
          "hant": "200，2，緊急",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "250, 3, an urgent",
          "hant": "250，3，緊急",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "150, 5, a high-priority",
          "hant": "150，5，高優先等級",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "175, 7, a high-priority",
          "hant": "175，7，高優先等級",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The normal pulse rate for an adult is between 60 and 100 beats per minutes. Pulse rates this rapid are usually due to supraventricular tachycardia (SVT) or atrial fibrillation. Supraventricular refers to the lower two chambers of the heart. Supraventricular tachycardia (SVT) is a rapid heart rate, 100 beats or more per minute but usually in the range of 140 to 250. The general range of SVT typically falls between 100-220 bpm. On the other hand, the he upper limit of SVT can reach 200-220 bpm. Continued episodes of tachycardia can progress to acute heart failure. The severity of the symptoms and signs will determine whether the referral is a high-priority same day referral or an urgent emergency referral. If an attack of tachycardia and associated symptoms (SOB, dizziness) do not subside within five minutes, an emergency referral should made. If the tachycardia subsides within a few minutes, it is a high-priority same day referral. The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 35",
      "exp_hant": "成人正常脈搏率介於每分鐘60至100下之間。如此快速的脈搏通常是由陣發性室上性心搏過速（SVT）或心房顫動所引起。室上性是指心臟下方兩個心室。室上性心搏過速（SVT）是一種快速心律，每分鐘100下以上，但通常介於140至250之間。SVT的一般範圍多落在每分鐘100至220下；另一方面，SVT的上限則可達每分鐘200至220下。持續發作的心搏過速可能進展為急性心臟衰竭。轉診的急迫程度須依症狀與徵象的嚴重度而定，可能是當天高優先等級轉診，或緊急轉診。若心搏過速發作及其相關症狀（呼吸困難、頭暈）在五分鐘內未緩解，應立即緊急轉診；若心搏過速在數分鐘內緩解，則屬當天高優先等級轉診。The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals，Stephenson著，2013年，第35頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 637,
      "question_en": "A 50 year-old female has sharp chest pain whenever she takes a deep breath. She had a history of both her ankles swelling and mild heart failure. Physical exam, shows a pulse of 90 bpm and regular. Blood pressure is 140/85. Respiration is 15/minute. The patient is 5 feet 2 inches tall and weighs 170 pounds. Pitting edema was observed in her ankles, with the right ankle 4 cm larger than the left. She also has SOB in the office. What would you now do?",
      "question_hant": "一名50歲女性每當深呼吸時便出現尖銳胸痛。她過去曾有雙側踝部腫脹與輕度心臟衰竭病史。理學檢查顯示脈搏90下/分且規則，血壓140/85，呼吸速率每分鐘15下。病人身高5呎2吋，體重170磅。踝部可見可凹陷性水腫，右踝比左踝大4公分。她在診間也出現呼吸困難。此時你會怎麼做？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "refer to cardiologist within the next week",
          "hant": "一週內轉診至心臟科醫師",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "call 911 for transport to emergency department (ED)",
          "hant": "撥打911送往急診室（ED）",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "have family member transport to emergency department (ED)",
          "hant": "請家屬送往急診室（ED）",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "next day referral to primary care physician",
          "hant": "隔天轉診至主治醫師",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is sharp chest pain and SOB with unilateral or bilateral asymmetric ankle swelling. A pulmonary embolus (PE) is assumed present until proven otherwise. This is an emergency event requiring 911 emergency transport. Patients with PE appear acutely ill with fast breathing, fast pulse, symptoms of poor oxygenation such as cyanosis, pleuritic chest pain, and SOB. It is important to measure the circumference of the ankles to detect significant differences between the two ankles. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 105-106",
      "exp_hant": "警訊徵象為尖銳胸痛合併呼吸困難，且踝部呈單側或雙側不對稱腫脹。在排除其他可能性之前，應假設病人罹患肺栓塞（PE），此為需撥打911緊急送醫的急症。PE病人通常呈現急性病容，呼吸急促、脈搏加快，並出現缺氧徵象如發紺、胸膜性胸痛與呼吸困難。測量雙側踝部周徑以偵測是否有顯著差異是重要的評估項目。An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals，Anzaldua著，2012年，第105-106頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 638,
      "question_en": "Employers are required to make available to employees with occupational bloodborne pathogen exposure risk a series of three HBV vaccinations, at no cost to employees. The vaccinations must be made available within how many working days of initial assignment?",
      "question_hant": "雇主必須為有職業性血液媒介病原體暴露風險的員工，免費提供一系列三劑B型肝炎（HBV）疫苗接種。此疫苗必須在員工到職後幾個工作天內提供？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "30 days",
          "hant": "30天",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "15 days",
          "hant": "15天",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "45 days",
          "hant": "45天",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "10 days",
          "hant": "10天",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "HBV can be transmitted via blood contact, sexual contact, sharing of needles, needle sticks, and through mother-child through pregnancy. Any worker who can reasonably anticipate contact with blood during performance of their job is considered to have occupational exposure and be at risk of being infected. Workers infected with HBV face a risk for liver ailments which can be fatal. The vaccination must be offered after the worker is trained and within 10 days of initial assignment to a job where there is occupational exposure, unless the worker has previously received the vaccine series, antibody testing has revealed that the worker is immune, or the vaccine is contra-indicated for medical reasons. The employer must obtain a written opinion from the licensed healthcare professional within 15 days of the completion of the evaluation for vaccination. This written opinion is limited to whether hepatitis B vaccination is indicated for the worker and if the worker has received the vaccination. Employers must ensure that workers who decline vaccination sign a declination form. Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 68",
      "exp_hant": "B型肝炎（HBV）可經由血液接觸、性接觸、共用針具、針扎傷，以及母子垂直傳染（懷孕期間）傳播。任何在執行工作時可合理預期會接觸血液的員工，皆被視為具有職業暴露風險並可能受到感染。感染HBV的員工面臨肝臟疾病的風險，嚴重時可能致命。疫苗必須在員工完成訓練後，且於首次被指派從事具有職業暴露風險的工作之10天內提供，除非該員工先前已完成疫苗接種系列、抗體檢測顯示已具免疫力，或因醫療原因不宜接種。雇主必須在完成疫苗接種評估後15天內，取得具執照醫事人員出具的書面意見，該書面意見僅限於說明該員工是否適合接種B型肝炎疫苗，以及是否已完成接種。雇主必須確保拒絕接種的員工簽署拒絕聲明書。Acupuncture Risk Management，CMS Press出版，Kailin著，1997年，第68頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 639,
      "question_en": "Severe pneumothorax is an emergency medical situation. A patient with severe pneumothorax can have severe breathlessness and",
      "question_hant": "嚴重氣胸是一種緊急醫療狀況。嚴重氣胸的病人可能出現嚴重呼吸困難，並且",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "chest pain worse when slowly exhaling",
          "hant": "緩慢吐氣時胸痛加劇",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "absence of chest pain while breathing",
          "hant": "呼吸時無胸痛",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "chest pain worse with shallow inhaling and exhaling",
          "hant": "淺呼吸（吸氣與吐氣）時胸痛加劇",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "chest pain worse with deep inhaling",
          "hant": "深吸氣時胸痛加劇",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Normal respiratory rate in a an adult is 10 to 20 breaths per minute (one inhalation exhalation). Moderate breathlessness is more than 30 breaths per minute (bpm). Severe breathlessness is more than 60 bpm. This is an urgent referral. A severe pneumothorax can result in the lung suddenly collapsing. A pneumothorax is defined as a collection of air outside the lung but within the pleural cavity. It occurs when air accumulates between the parietal and visceral pleurae inside the chest. The air accumulation can apply pressure on the lung and make it collapse. The degree of collapse determines the clinical presentation of pneumothorax. A pneumothorax can be caused by penetrating chest injury, certain medical procedures, or arising due to damage from underlying lung disorder. It can occur without any obvious reason. When a lung collapses the chest pain is a sharp, stabbing chest pain which worsens on breathing or with deep inspiration. This pain is called pleuritic pain because it originates from the nerve endings of the pleura which is the inner lining of the rib wall. Pleuratic pain comes from irritation of nerve endings in the pleura (inner lining of the rib wall). Lung tissue itself does not have pain-sensing nerve endings. Pneumothorax usually involves inserting a needle or tube between the rib to remove excess air. If the pneumothorax is small it can heal by itself. The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 165, 166",
      "exp_hant": "成人正常呼吸速率為每分鐘10至20次（一次吸氣加一次吐氣）。中度呼吸困難為每分鐘超過30次，嚴重呼吸困難則為每分鐘超過60次，此時應緊急轉診。嚴重氣胸可能導致肺臟突然塌陷。氣胸是指空氣積聚於肺臟外、胸膜腔內的狀態，發生於空氣積聚在胸腔內的壁層與臟層胸膜之間。積聚的空氣會對肺臟施加壓力，使其塌陷，塌陷的程度決定了氣胸的臨床表現。氣胸可由穿刺性胸部外傷、某些醫療處置，或因潛在肺部疾病造成的損傷所引起，也可能沒有明顯原因而發生。當肺臟塌陷時，胸痛表現為尖銳、刺痛感，並於呼吸或深吸氣時加劇。這種疼痛稱為胸膜性疼痛，因為它源自胸膜（肋骨壁內襯）的神經末梢受到刺激；肺組織本身並無痛覺神經末梢。氣胸的處置通常需要在肋骨間置入針具或引流管以排出多餘空氣；若氣胸範圍小，則可能自行癒合。The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals，Stephenson著，2013年，第165、166頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 640,
      "question_en": "You are trained in CPR. One of your patients has no pulse and is not breathing. You do CPR. The patient becomes conscious. As a result of the CPR, the patient has two fractured ribs. Which statement reflects the practitioner liability and malpractice?",
      "question_hant": "你受過心肺復甦術（CPR）訓練。你的一位病人失去脈搏且沒有呼吸，你為他施行CPR，病人恢復意識，但因CPR而造成兩根肋骨骨折。下列何者正確反映執業者的責任與醫療過失問題？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Fractured ribs are an acknowledged risk and difficult to conclusively attribute to malpractice",
          "hant": "肋骨骨折是公認的風險，難以明確歸咎於醫療過失",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "The practitioner is liable for the fractured ribs because the practitioner applied sub-standard CPR",
          "hant": "執業者須為肋骨骨折負責，因為其CPR操作未達標準",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Practitioner liability is dependent on whether CPR certification is up to date",
          "hant": "執業者的責任取決於其CPR證照是否為最新有效",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "The practioner is not liable because Good Samaritan laws apply",
          "hant": "執業者不須負責，因為適用好撒瑪利亞人法",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Studies show that a significant portion of the people who receive CPR may end up with broken ribs or other bones as a result. Broken ribs are to be expected when doing CPR and the general worry of causing a break should not deter people from helping someone who is in cardiac arrest. All states carry Good Samaritan Laws which act as a legal shield for those individuals who take the risk to save lives. Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 115",
      "exp_hant": "研究顯示，相當比例接受CPR的人最終會發生肋骨或其他骨頭骨折。施行CPR時發生肋骨骨折是可預期的結果，一般對造成骨折的擔憂不應阻礙人們對心臟停止的病人施以援手。所有州皆訂有好撒瑪利亞人法，為冒險搶救生命的人提供法律上的保護。Acupuncture Risk Management，CMS Press出版，Kailin著，1997年，第115頁"
