    {
      "number": 642,
      "question_en": "A 61 year-old male patient has an aplastic anemia diagnosis from his primary care physician. He reports that his tiredness, dizziness and shortness of breath have gradually worsened during the past month. Facial complexion is very pale, almost white. Review of systems is positive for frequent colds and recurring urinary tract infections. The physical exam reveals pinhead-sized bruising on the forearms. Which aspect of the clinical picture indicates a worsening of the aplastic anemia requiring a referral for further evaluation?",
      "question_hant": "一名61歲男性病人，經主治醫師診斷為再生不良性貧血。他主訴過去一個月疲倦、頭暈與呼吸困難逐漸加重，面色蒼白甚至近乎慘白。系統回顧顯示他經常感冒且反覆泌尿道感染。理學檢查發現前臂有針頭大小的瘀點。下列臨床表現中，哪一項顯示再生不良性貧血正在惡化、需要轉診做進一步評估？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "age, complexion, frequent urinary tract infections and frequent colds",
          "hant": "年齡、面色、頻繁泌尿道感染與頻繁感冒",
