      ],
      "exp_en": "This is cauda equina syndrome. In some cases, severe back pain can be a sign of cauda equina syndrome. This is a medical emergency which usually requires urgent surgical treatment. In cauda equina syndrome there is compression on the spinal nerve roots. Fast treatment is needed to prevent lasting damage leading to incontinence and maybe leg paralysis. The most common causes of the nerve root compression are: 1) a severe ruptured disk in the lumbar area which is the most common cause. 2) spinal stenosis. 3) spinal tumor. 4) spinal infection, bleeding, or fracture. 5) trauma. Symptoms include: severe low back pain. Pain, numbness, or weakness in one or both legs. Altered sensations in the legs, buttocks, inner thighs, backs of the legs, or feet. Difficulty feeling anything in the areas of the body that would sit in a saddle (saddle anesthesia). Recent problem with bladder or bowel function. Sudden sexual dysfunction.",
      "exp_hant": "這是馬尾症候群。某些情況下，嚴重背痛可能是馬尾症候群的徵兆，這是一種通常需要緊急手術治療的醫療急症。馬尾症候群是脊神經根受到壓迫所致，須儘快治療以避免造成永久性損傷，導致失禁甚至腿部癱瘓。造成神經根壓迫最常見的原因包括：1）腰椎椎間盤嚴重破裂，這是最常見的原因；2）脊椎狹窄；3）脊椎腫瘤；4）脊椎感染、出血或骨折；5）外傷。其症狀包括：嚴重下背痛；單側或雙側腿部疼痛、麻木或無力；腿部、臀部、大腿內側、腿後側或足部感覺異常；鞍區（坐於馬鞍時接觸的部位）感覺遲鈍或喪失（鞍區麻木）；近期出現膀胱或腸道功能問題；以及突發性性功能障礙。"
    },
    {
      "number": 646,
      "question_en": "You are treating a patient with a bloodletting technique. During the treatment the patient becomes dizzy and weak. The pulse has become rapid, floating, and weak. Which points can the practitioner moxa?",
      "question_hant": "你正在為一位病人施行放血療法，治療過程中病人出現頭暈與虛弱，脈象轉為快、浮而弱。此時施術者可以艾灸哪些穴位？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "DU-14, REN-8",
          "hant": "大椎、神闕",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "DU-14, DU-26, DU-20, or ST-36",
          "hant": "大椎、水溝、百會，或足三里",
