      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. In this situation the practitioner can repeatedly moxa DU-14 with a small amount of heat, salt moxa REN-8, or repeatedly thread size moxa on DU-20 or ST-36. Moxa on DU-26 is not selected. The symptoms and pulse are an indication of high-dosage bloodletting for the patient and too much blood was expressed. Before you treat a patient with bloodletting try to judge the appropriate dosage (number of points, how much blood is expressed). According to their condition (relatively healthy, replete, vacuous). If unsure treat the patient with a minimal number of points and with a low-dosage. For very weak patients that express dark-viscous at the beginning, do not wait for the blood to become lighter and more fluid before stopping the procedure as doing so would be considered too high of a dosage of stimulation. If the patient is relatively healthy or has an overall repletion, you can keep expressing the dark blood until it becomes lighter. Be sure in either case to monitor the pulse for ill effects of the treatment. Japanese Acupuncture, 1998, Birch and Ida, page 241",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整且最正確的答案。在此情況下，施術者可以小劑量的熱度反覆艾灸大椎，以隔鹽灸法灸神闕，或以線香大小的艾炷反覆灸百會或足三里；水溝則不予選用。此病人出現的症狀與脈象顯示放血劑量過高、擠出的血量過多。在為病人施行放血療法之前，應先依其體質狀況（相對健康、實證或虛證）判斷適當的劑量（穴位數目與擠血量）。若不確定，宜以最少的穴位數與最低劑量施術。對於體質非常虛弱、一開始擠出的血呈暗紫黏稠狀的病人，不應等到血色變淡、質地變稀才停止操作，否則刺激劑量會過高。若病人相對健康或整體屬實證，則可持續擠出暗色血液直到顏色變淡為止。無論哪種情況，都應密切監測脈象，以留意治療所造成的不良反應。Japanese Acupuncture，Birch與Ida著，1998年，第241頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 647,
      "question_en": "Nociceptors are found in skin, skeletal and cardiac muscles as well as heart vessels. Noxious events are conducted from these nociceptor fibers to",
      "question_hant": "傷害感受器（Nociceptors）存在於皮膚、骨骼肌與心肌，以及心臟血管中。傷害性事件由這些傷害感受器纖維傳導至",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "purkinje fibers of the spinal cord",
          "hant": "脊髓的浦金氏纖維",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "A-delta fibers",
          "hant": "A-δ纖維",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "unmyelinated C-fibers",
          "hant": "無髓鞘C纖維",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "dorsal horn of the spinal cord",
          "hant": "脊髓背角",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "E",
          "en": "internuncial neurons of the spinal cord",
          "hant": "脊髓的中介神經元",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Nociceptors, often called \"pain receptors,\" are free nerve endings located in the the skin, muscles, joints, bones, and internal organs. They play a pivotal role in how a person feels and reacts to pain. The dorsal horn of the spinal cord receives the noxious events through the nociceptor fibers and synapses, predominantly on interneurons instead of projection neurons. Interneurons synapse again in an inhibitory manner or may excite projection neurons for further transmission of the afferent sensory signals toward higher cortical areas. Interneurons, also known as association neurons, are neurons that are found exclusively in the central nervous system (CNS). That is, they are found in the brain and spinal cord and not in the peripheral segments of the nervous system. Projection neurons are neurons whose axons extend from the cell body within the central nervous system (CNS) to one or more distant regions of the CNS. Neuro-Acupuncture; Z.H. Cho, E.K. Wong, J. Fallon; 2001, Q-puncture, page 115",
      "exp_hant": "傷害感受器常被稱為「痛覺受器」，是位於皮膚、肌肉、關節、骨骼與內臟中的游離神經末梢，在人體感受與反應疼痛的過程中扮演關鍵角色。脊髓背角經由傷害感受器纖維接收傷害性事件並形成突觸，主要與中介神經元而非投射神經元形成連結。中介神經元可再以抑制方式形成突觸，或興奮投射神經元，以將傳入的感覺訊號進一步傳向較高層次的皮質區域。中介神經元又稱聯絡神經元，僅存在於中樞神經系統（CNS）中，也就是說，僅存在於腦與脊髓，而不存在於周邊神經系統。投射神經元則是指其軸突自中樞神經系統內的細胞本體延伸至CNS內一個或多個較遠區域的神經元。Neuro-Acupuncture；Z.H. Cho、E.K. Wong、J. Fallon著；2001年，Q-puncture出版，第115頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 648,
      "question_en": "Which electro-acupuncture frequency mainly affects motor neurons?",
      "question_hant": "哪一種電針頻率主要影響運動神經元？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
