          "hant": "一息七至",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "twelve beats per respiration",
          "hant": "一息十二至",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "nine beats per respiration",
          "hant": "一息九至",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "According to Li Zhi-chen it is enough to check for \"strong, weak, retarded and quick pulses\" in an infant. A strong pulse indicates Excess, a weak one indicates Deficiency, a quick pulse indicates invasion of pathogenic factors (Evil Qi). A retarded pulse is normal for an infant. Li Zhi-chen notes that infant pulses are normally faster than those of adults. In an infant, the normal pulse rate between the ages three to five is seven beats per each respiration. Nine beats indicates Heat. Four or five beats indicates Cold. Li Zhi-chen advises taking the pulse with only one finger. Other practitioners have advised one finger for a young infant, two fingers on an older baby and three fingers held together for a child. Turtle Tail and Other Tender Mercies: Traditional Chinese Pediatrics, Blue Poppy Press, Bob Flaws, 1985, page 17",
      "exp_hant": "根據李峙辰的說法，為嬰幼兒把脈時，只需辨別「有力、無力、遲、數」即可。有力之脈屬實，無力之脈屬虛，數脈顯示邪氣入侵，遲脈則為嬰兒的正常脈象。李峙辰指出，嬰兒的脈象通常較成人快。三至五歲兒童的正常脈率為一息七至；一息九至為熱象，一息四至或五至則為寒象。李峙辰建議為嬰兒把脈時僅用一指；亦有其他醫家建議對年幼嬰兒用一指、稍大嬰兒用二指、對兒童則併用三指診脈。Turtle Tail and Other Tender Mercies: Traditional Chinese Pediatrics，Blue Poppy Press出版，Bob Flaws著，1985年，第17頁"
    },
