      "exp_en": "In Japanese treatment it is not the number of cones (3, 5, or 7) that is important but how many times the actual heat is felt by the patient. As such, the recommendation is that the patient should feel the moxa heat 3, 5, or 7 times. That means if a moxa cone is used and the patient does not feel the heat from it, then that cone is not counted. As the moxa cones are small and thin, on some points it might take the application of dozens of cones before the patient actually feels the heat 3, 5, or 7 times. Japanese Acupuncture, 1998, Birch and Ida, page 118",
      "exp_hant": "在日式治療中，重要的並非艾炷的壯數（3、5或7壯），而是病人實際感受到熱感的次數。因此建議應讓病人感受到艾灸熱感3、5或7次，也就是說，若施灸一壯而病人並未感受到熱感，該壯則不予計算。由於艾炷體積小而細，在某些穴位上，可能需要施灸數十壯，病人才會實際感受到3、5或7次熱感。Japanese Acupuncture，Birch與Ida著，1998年，第118頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 651,
      "question_en": "A 37 year-old male patient has an acute high fever of 104 F. He feels hot, the complexion is flushed, is thirsty, and is very agitated. The tongue is red. The pulse is rapid and full. The patient has a history of hypertension. He inherited thalassemia from his mother. What treatment should be selected?",
      "question_hant": "一名37歲男性病人突發急性高燒，體溫達華氏104度，自覺燥熱，面色潮紅，口渴，情緒十分躁動不安，舌紅，脈快而有力。病人有高血壓病史，並自母親遺傳了地中海貧血。應選擇下列何種治療？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "bleeding tip of ear",
          "hant": "耳尖放血",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "body acupuncture only",
          "hant": "僅施以體針",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "bleeding PC-9 (zhong chong)",
          "hant": "中衝放血",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "body acupuncture and bleeding tip of ear",
          "hant": "體針併耳尖放血",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Thalassemias are inherited blood disorders with decreased hemoglobin, which is the iron-containing oxygen-transport in red blood cells. Symptoms may include mild to severe anemia. Any type of anemia such as thalassemia is contraindicated with blood letting. Blood letting is contraindicated in pregnancy, vascular tumors, patients with weak constitution, and hypotension. If bloodletting is indicated for a patient it should be stopped when the face of the patient becomes pale, the pulse becomes faint, the patient gets cold limbs, or the patient starts sweating. Releasing a few drops of blood at specific points can improve the localized qi and blood flow, which helps treating conditions like toxic heat accumulation, swelling, pain, blood stasis, qi stagnation, hyperactive organs, restless mind, and head orifices blockages. Blood letting therapy is indicated for acute, heat, excess and painful syndromes. It is often used to relieve high fever, throat soreness due to heat, stubborn joint pain, mastitis, female breast pain, muscle sprain, as well as localized swelling and numbness. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 48; Acupuncture A Comprehensive Text, Bensky, 1981, page 429",
      "exp_hant": "地中海貧血是一種遺傳性血液疾病，患者血紅素（紅血球中負責攜帶氧氣的含鐵蛋白）偏低，症狀可從輕度到重度貧血不等。任何類型的貧血（包括地中海貧血）皆為放血療法的禁忌。放血療法亦禁用於孕婦、血管性腫瘤患者、體質虛弱者及低血壓患者。若病人適合施行放血，一旦出現面色蒼白、脈象轉弱、四肢冰冷或開始出汗，即應立即停止操作。在特定穴位釋出少量血液，可改善局部氣血運行，有助於治療毒熱蘊結、腫脹、疼痛、血瘀、氣滯、臟腑亢盛、心神不寧，以及頭部竅道阻塞等病症。放血療法適用於急證、熱證、實證與痛證，常用於緩解高熱、熱性咽喉腫痛、頑固性關節疼痛、乳腺炎、婦女乳房疼痛、肌肉扭傷，以及局部腫脹與麻木。Clean Needle Technique，第7版，第48頁；Acupuncture A Comprehensive Text，Bensky著，1981年，第429頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 652,
      "question_en": "When applying tape over the intradermal needle it is important to",
      "question_hant": "在皮內針上貼膠布時，重要的是應該",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "stretch the skin",
          "hant": "將皮膚拉展",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "cover only the needle body",
          "hant": "僅覆蓋針身",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "pucker the skin",
          "hant": "使皮膚皺起",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "cover only the needle handle",
          "hant": "僅覆蓋針柄",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Normally two pieces of tape are used. The first piece of tape is smaller and is placed under the handle. The second piece of tape is placed over the whole needle and the first piece of tape. When applying the second piece of tape, the skin should be stretched so as to prevent it from loosening when the patient stretches the skin when performing day to day activities. Sometimes a third piece of tape is used, like the 2nd piece, to ensure a secure placement. The book recommends 1/2 inch MICROPORE tape. Japanese Acupuncture, 1998, Birch and Ida, page 151, 152",
      "exp_hant": "通常會使用兩片膠布：第一片較小，貼於針柄下方；第二片則覆蓋整根針及第一片膠布。貼第二片膠布時，應將皮膚拉展開來，以避免病人日常活動使皮膚伸展時膠布鬆脫。有時會如第二片一樣再貼上第三片膠布，以確保固定牢靠。書中建議使用1/2英吋的MICROPORE膠布。Japanese Acupuncture，Birch與Ida著，1998年，第151-152頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 653,
      "question_en": "Nociceptors are high threshold mechanoreceptors that are activated by intense mechanical stimulation including tissue damage, and which is usually innervated by",
      "question_hant": "傷害感受器是一種高閾值機械受器，會被強烈的機械性刺激（包括組織損傷）所活化，通常由下列何者所支配？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "A-delta fiber",
          "hant": "A-δ纖維",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "C-fibers",
          "hant": "C纖維",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "substance P",
          "hant": "P物質",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "B-fibers",
          "hant": "B纖維",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "E",
          "en": "D-fibers",
          "hant": "D纖維",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A-delta fiber is a thin, myelinated fiber that is generally responsible for the brief, or fast, pin-prick type of pain rather than slow and chronic pain. Nerve fibers are classified according to the size and speed of conduction and whether they are mylenated or unmyelinated. The impulse in a myelinated nerve fiber travels faster than an impulse in an unmyelinated nerve fiber. C-fibers are unmylenated. Mylenated A-fibers are the fastest the thickest, the myelinated B-fibers are the next in terms of speed and thickness, and the unmyelinated C-fibers are the slowest and thinnest. Substance P (SP) is protein that transmits pain signals from the sensory nerves to the central nervous system. SP is secreted by nerves and inflammatory cells such as macrophages, lymphocytes, and dendritic cells and has a proinflammatory effect in diseases of the respiratory, gastrointestinal, and musculoskeletal systems. Neuro-Acupuncture; Z.H. Cho, E.K. Wong, J. Fallon; 2001, Q-puncture, page 115",
      "exp_hant": "A-δ纖維是一種細而有髓鞘的神經纖維，主要負責短暫、快速的針刺樣疼痛，而非緩慢的慢性疼痛。神經纖維依其粗細與傳導速度，以及是否具有髓鞘來分類。有髓鞘神經纖維的傳導速度快於無髓鞘神經纖維，C纖維即為無髓鞘纖維。有髓鞘的A纖維傳導最快、最粗；有髓鞘的B纖維次之；無髓鞘的C纖維則傳導最慢、最細。P物質（Substance P，SP）是一種將痛覺訊號自感覺神經傳向中樞神經系統的蛋白質，由神經細胞及巨噬細胞、淋巴球、樹突細胞等發炎細胞分泌，在呼吸系統、腸胃系統與肌肉骨骼系統疾病中具有促發炎作用。Neuro-Acupuncture；Z.H. Cho、E.K. Wong、J. Fallon著；2001年，Q-puncture出版，第115頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 654,
      "question_en": "How were motor points (MPs) discovered and identified?",
      "question_hant": "運動點（Motor Points, MPs）是如何被發現與確認的？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "by trial and error and observing their therapeutic effect on muscle dysfunction",
          "hant": "透過反覆嘗試並觀察其對肌肉功能障礙的療效",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "cadaver dissection",
          "hant": "屍體解剖",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "cadaver dissection and cutaneous electrical stimulation",
          "hant": "屍體解剖與皮膚電刺激",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "cutaneous electrical stimulation by their proximity to acupuncture points",
          "hant": "依其與穴位的相近程度以皮膚電刺激測定",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A pen electrode has been used to identify and map the location of MPs. A small electrical current was applied to different locations on the skin where the motor point was suspected through evoking a muscle twitch. The point that used the least amount of electrical stimulation was considered as the MP of that muscle. This superficial skin area corresponds to the location which is over the motor entry point (MEP) where an electrical pulse evokes a muscle twitch with the least amount of current. The MEP is where the motor nerve pierces the muscle belly. Surface electrode testing is not useful or reliable for locating muscle motor points that are located in the deeper muscle layers. For example, the MPs for the hip external rotator muscles are too deep to be tested on the surface of the skin via a pen electrode. Research has also been done to identify MPs via cadaver dissection by locating the motor nerve entry points (MEP) into the muscle. For muscles with deeply located MPs, the research based on cadaver dissection is used to locate and identify the MPs. Research on cadavers can also help to confirm the MPs located via the pen electrode stimulation method. Sports Medicine Acupuncture, Callison, 2020, page 1033",
      "exp_hant": "研究者曾使用筆型電極來確認並繪製運動點的位置：在懷疑為運動點的皮膚各處施以微小電流，藉由引發肌肉抽動來測試，所需電刺激量最小的點即被視為該肌肉的運動點。此表淺皮膚區域對應的位置正是運動神經進入點（MEP）之上——在此以最小電流即可引發肌肉抽動，MEP即為運動神經穿入肌腹之處。對於位於較深肌肉層的運動點，體表電極測試並不實用也不可靠，例如髖部外旋肌群的運動點過深，無法以筆型電極在體表測得。也有研究透過屍體解剖，藉由定位肌肉內的運動神經進入點（MEP）來確認運動點；對於運動點位置較深的肌肉，即以屍體解剖研究來定位與確認。屍體研究也能協助驗證以筆型電極刺激法所測得的運動點。Sports Medicine Acupuncture，Callison著，2020年，第1033頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 655,
      "question_en": "Which of the following is true regarding using gua sha in the treatment of trigger points?",
      "question_hant": "關於使用刮痧治療激痛點，下列敘述何者正確？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "gua sha helps in resolving the knots associated with trigger points",
          "hant": "刮痧有助於化解與激痛點相關的結節",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "gua sha is a both a primary and adjunct method of resolving trigger points",
          "hant": "刮痧既是化解激痛點的主要方法，也是輔助方法",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "gua sha affects the deep qi and blood stasis of the trigger points",
          "hant": "刮痧可作用於激痛點深層的氣血瘀滯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "gua sha is mainly an adjunct method in the treatment of trigger points",
          "hant": "刮痧主要是治療激痛點的輔助方法",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Trigger points are knots associated with taut muscle bands caused by qi and blood stasis located in deep layers of the muscle tissue. Gua sha is more of a superficial method to release external pathogenic factors and blockage of channels. The sha syndrome is caused by an exposure to external pathogenic factors (wind, cold, damp, heat) and blockage of channels. When the strength of the external pathogens exceed the strength of the wei qi, the pathogens enter the body and stagnate the qi and blood of the channels. The external invasion manifests as chill, fever and blockage as pain, rigidity, or numbness. The term sha applies to both a syndrome associated with a pathogenic factor retained in the body and its rash-like expression on the surface of the body. The skin reaction is associated with the retained external pathogenic factor which stagnate the qi and blood in the meridians. The sha rash consists of raised bumps that can be red, blue, purple, or black that appear after the application of the gua sha or the skin scraping technique. As such gua sha is an adjunct and not a primary modality in resolving trigger points. Gua sha can help with the muscle adhesions and congestion that can be part of the trigger point complex. However, gua sha will not deactivate trigger points, though it may provide temporary relief. . Gua Sha, Nielsen, 2009, page 44",
      "exp_hant": "激痛點是位於肌肉組織深層、因氣血瘀滯而形成的緊繃肌束結節。刮痧則是較表淺的方法，用以疏解外邪並疏通經絡阻滯。「痧」證是因外邪（風、寒、濕、熱）侵襲並阻滯經絡所致：當外邪的力量超過衛氣時，邪氣便侵入人體，使經絡氣血鬱滯。外邪入侵表現為惡寒發熱，阻滯則表現為疼痛、僵硬或麻木。「痧」一詞既指體內留滯病邪所形成的證候，也指其顯現於體表的類皮疹反應；此皮膚反應與經絡中氣血因留滯病邪而鬱滯有關。痧疹是刮痧或刮痧手法施術後皮膚出現的隆起斑點，可呈紅色、青色、紫色或黑色。因此，刮痧對於化解激痛點而言是輔助方法，而非主要療法。刮痧有助於處理可能屬於激痛點複合體一部分的肌肉沾黏與鬱滯，但刮痧並不能使激痛點失活，僅能提供暫時性的緩解。Gua Sha，Nielsen著，2009年，第44頁"
    },
