        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A motor point is a zone of muscle innervation. This can be viewed in three ways. 1) The zone of innervation is where the motor nerve pierces the muscle belly. This is known as motor nerve entry point (MEP). 2) The zone of innervation is the terminal end of motor nerve which is located at the motor-end plate of the motor nerve. This is also known as the intramuscular motor point (IMP). Motor points have the greatest concentration of motor-end plates in the muscle. Both the MEP and IMP innervate the muscle. 3) The zone of innervation is a cutaneous point with the lowest resistance to electrical conductivity for the entire muscle. When this cutaneous point is electrically stimulated the muscle contracts more strongly than any other areas of the skin over the muscle. Definitions one and two is where the nerve connects directly to the muscle. Definition three is a skin area that electrically influences the muscle to contract. This superficial skin area corresponds to the location which is over the MEP, where an electrical pulse evokes a muscle twitch with the least amount of current. Sports Medicine Acupuncture, Callison, 2020, page 1033",
      "exp_hant": "運動點是肌肉神經支配的區域，可從三個角度理解：1）神經支配區是指運動神經穿入肌腹之處，稱為運動神經進入點（MEP）；2）神經支配區是指運動神經的末端，位於運動神經的運動終板，也稱為肌肉內運動點（IMP），運動點是整塊肌肉中運動終板密度最高之處，MEP與IMP皆能支配該肌肉；3）神經支配區是指整塊肌肉中電阻最低、導電性最佳的皮膚點，當此皮膚點受到電刺激時，肌肉的收縮力會比該肌肉上方其他皮膚區域更強。第一與第二種定義是指神經直接與肌肉相連之處；第三種定義則是指以電性方式影響肌肉收縮的皮膚區域，此表淺皮膚區域對應的位置正是MEP之上——在此以最小電流即可引發肌肉抽動。Sports Medicine Acupuncture，Callison著，2020年，第1033頁"
