    {
      "number": 669,
      "question_en": "A 15 year-old male has a sudden onset of strong abdominal pain which improves with warmth and worsens with cold. He has loose stools, no thirst, and clear urine. The limbs are cold. The tongue has a thin-white coating and the pulse is deep-tight-slow. The prescription is REN-12 (zhong wan), ST-36 (zu san li), SP-4 (gong sun), and salt moxa on REN-8 (shen que). After several treatments the intensity of the abdominal pain abates and now feels intermittent and dull. The pain still improves with warmth and worsens with cold but also worsens with hunger and fatigue. He has an aversion to cold. The pulse is deep-thready. The tongue has a thin and white coating. What prescription would you choose next?",
      "question_hant": "一名15歲男性突然出現劇烈腹痛，得溫則減、遇寒加重，大便溏薄，口不渴，小便清長，四肢冰冷。舌苔薄白，脈沉緊而遲。處方為中脘、足三里、公孫，並隔鹽灸神闕。經過數次治療後，腹痛強度減輕，變為時發時止的隱痛，仍然得溫則減、遇寒加重，但也在飢餓與疲勞時加重，並有畏寒現象。脈沉細，舌苔薄白。接下來你會選擇哪一個處方？",
