      "number": 675,
      "question_en": "A 33 year-old male has the flu. He has high fever, thirst, cough, thin yellow sputum, and sweating. The treatment prescribed was LU-5 (chi ze), LU-10 (yu ji), DU-14 (da zhui), and BL-13 (fei shu). A few days after the first treatment, he calls saying that his fever has worsened after working in hot and humid weather. He comes in for another visit. He states that his symptoms have now changed. His only symptom is fever which is continuous, improves after sweating, and then increases again. He has loose stools. The tongue has a sticky yellow coating and the pulse is soggy. What prescription would you now choose?",
