    },
    {
      "number": 738,
      "question_en": "Which point Spreads Liver qi; Subdues Liver yang and extinguishes wind; Nourishes Liver blood and Liver yin; Regulates menstruation and the lower jiao, and Clears the head and eyes?",
      "question_hant": "下列何穴能疏肝理氣、平肝熄風、養肝血滋肝陰、調經理下焦，並清利頭目？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "LR-3 (taichong)",
          "hant": "太衝",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "GB-43 (xiaxi)",
          "hant": "俠谿",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "LR-6 (zhongdu)",
          "hant": "中都",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "LR-4 (zhongfeng)",
          "hant": "中封",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Shu-stream, yuan-source, and Earth point. LR-3 (taichong) can treat both excess and deficiency patterns of the Liver organ and channel. Any Liver pattern can be accompanied with stagnant Liver qi with distention and pain in any part of the body (head, eyes, throat, chest, breasts, Heart, costal area, epigastrium, abdomen). LR-3 (taichong) is an essential point in promoting the free flow of Liver qi whether the stagnant Liver qi is caused by repressed emotions, damp-heat, or failure of Liver yin to nourish the Liver. LR-3 (taichong) is an important point in subduing an hyperactive Liver yang and pacifying Liver wind (from excess heat or deficient Liver blood/yin). LR-3 (taichong) promotes the generation of Liver blood and yin. It treats all xu Liver patterns and nourishes the areas of body which the Liver dominates (eyes, uterus, sinews). As such LR-3 (taichong) can treat both the root (blood and yin xu) and the manifestation (eyes, uterus, costal area, etc). As the Liver opens into the eyes, LR-3 (taichong) can treat blurred/failing vision due to xu (Liver yin/blood xu) or red/swollen/painful/congested/twitching eyes due to shi (Liver fire/wind). As the Liver channel has an internal pathway to the vertex of the head, LR-3 (taichong) can treat dizziness and vertex headaches from deficiency or excess. As the Liver stores blood and is connected to the ren mai, LR-3 (taichong) helps regulate the uterus (amenorrhea, irregular menstruation, uterine bleeding). The spreading function of the Liver helps regulate the qi of the Bladder and genitals. As such LR-3 (taichong) can be used to treat excess conditions (retention of urine, difficult urination, retraction of testicles, genital pain) and deficient conditions (enuresis, frequent urination, incontinence). LR-3 (taichong) can be used to treat both constipation (stagnant qi or stagnant heat) or diarrhea (wood attacking earth). LI-4 (hegu) combined with LR-3 (taichong) is known as the Four Gates which treats painful obstructions, pain, spasms, and ensures the free and smooth passage of qi and blood throughout the body. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 477",
      "exp_hant": "為輸（俞）穴、原穴，亦為土穴。LR-3 (taichong) 太衝 能同時治療肝臟臟腑與經絡的虛證與實證。凡屬肝病，皆可能伴隨肝氣鬱結，導致身體各部位（頭部、眼睛、咽喉、胸部、乳房、心、脅肋、上腹、腹部）脹痛。LR-3 (taichong) 太衝 是疏通肝氣鬱滯的要穴，無論肝氣鬱結是由情志抑鬱、濕熱，還是肝陰不足以濡養肝所致，皆可使用。LR-3 (taichong) 太衝 對於平抑亢盛之肝陽、平息肝風（無論因熱盛或因肝血/肝陰不足所致）亦十分重要。LR-3 (taichong) 太衝 能促進肝血與肝陰的化生，可治療一切肝虛之證，並濡養肝所主之處（眼睛、子宮、筋）。因此，LR-3 (taichong) 太衝 既能治本（血虛、陰虛），亦能治標（眼睛、子宮、脅肋等部位的症狀）。由於肝開竅於目，LR-3 (taichong) 太衝 可治療因虛（肝陰血虛）所致的視物模糊、視力減退，或因實（肝火、肝風）所致的目赤腫痛、澀痛、抽搐。由於肝經內行路線上達巔頂，LR-3 (taichong) 太衝 可治療因虛或實所致的頭暈及巔頂頭痛。由於肝藏血並與任脈相連，LR-3 (taichong) 太衝 有助於調理子宮（閉經、月經不調、崩漏）。肝的疏泄功能有助於調節膀胱與生殖器之氣機，因此 LR-3 (taichong) 太衝 可用於治療實證（尿瀦留、排尿困難、睪丸內縮、生殖器疼痛）及虛證（遺尿、尿頻、失禁）。LR-3 (taichong) 太衝 亦可用於治療便秘（氣滯或熱結）或腹瀉（木克土）。LI-4 (hegu) 合谷 配合 LR-3 (taichong) 太衝 稱為「四關」，能治療痺痛、疼痛、痙攣，並確保全身氣血暢通無阻。參考資料：《A Manual of Acupuncture》，Deadman，第2版，第477頁。"
    },
