      "exp_en": "The du mai nourishes the Brain and Marrow. The du mai is a yang vessel which brings yang energy to the head and brain. At the same time, the du mai also brings Kidney-Essence, which is yin, to the head and brain. The du mai is the \"Sea of Yang Channels\" and has an influence on all of the yang channels. Each Extraordinary Vessel has a connection to one or more of the Six Extraordinary Yang organs (Brain, Marrow, Uterus, Gall Bladder, Blood Vessels, Bones). The du mai is connected to the Brain and Marrow. The du mai connects with the Brain upward and the Kidneys downward. Kidney Essence produces Marrow which fills the spine and Brain. To nourish Kidney Essence to produce Marrow, the du mai can be used. The two points that affect the Sea of Marrow are DU-16 and DU-20 (both points enter the Brain). To activate the du mai to nourish the Brain and Marrow, the opening (SI-3) and coupled (BL-62) points are sequentially needled and then DU-16 and DU-20 are needled to treat a deficiency in the Sea of Marrow (dizziness, weak legs, tinnitus, blurred visions, desire to lie down). The needles are removed in reverse order. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 894",
      "exp_hant": "督脈能濡養腦髓。督脈為陽脈，能將陽氣帶至頭腦。同時，督脈也將屬陰之腎精帶往頭腦。督脈為「陽脈之海」，統率一身之陽經。每一條奇經八脈皆與奇恆之腑（腦、髓、女子胞、膽、脈、骨）中之一或多者相連。督脈與腦、髓相連，向上與腦相通，向下與腎相繫。腎精化生為髓，充養脊柱與腦髓。欲滋養腎精以生髓，可運用督脈。影響髓海的兩個穴位為 DU-16 (feng fu) 風府 與 DU-20 (bai hui) 百會（二穴皆入於腦）。欲啟動督脈以濡養腦髓，可依序針刺八脈交會穴之開穴 SI-3 (houxi) 後谿 與通穴 BL-62 (shenmai) 申脈，再刺 DU-16 (feng fu) 風府 與 DU-20 (bai hui) 百會，以治療髓海不足之證（頭暈、腿軟、耳鳴、視物模糊、嗜臥）。出針時則依相反順序退針。參考資料：《The Foundations of Chinese Medicine》，Maciocia，2015年版，第894頁。"
