      "exp_en": "The Large Intestine luo goes to the jaw, teeth, and ear. At LI-6 the luo channel separates from the primary channel and connects with the Lung primary channel. On the face, the Large Intestine luo separates and one branch goes to the teeth and another goes to the ear. At ST-40 the luo channel separates from the primary channel and connects with the Spleen primary. At the nape of the neck, the Stomach luo goes internally to terminate at the throat. ST-40 is an important point in treating neck pain associated with digestive issues, clearing the mind by eliminating Phlegm, and treating phlegm goiter. At BL-58 the luo channel separates from the primary channel and connects with the Kidney primary channel. The du mai luo connects with the Bladder channel at the scapular area. BL-58 is a distal point that treats sciatica and low back pain. LUO POINTS TREAT disorders of their interior-exterior related channel or zang fu. LI-6 treats acute edema which occurs when external wind disrupts the Lung function of regulating the water passages. ST-40 transforms phlegm arising when the related Spleen organ fails in transporting and transforming fluids. BL-58 treats Kidney deficiency and cold in the lower body, cold and weak legs, lower back pain. LUO POINTS TREAT disorders in areas reached by the luo-connecting channel. The Large Intestine luo channel ascends to the ears and LI-6 can treat tinnitus and deafness and other ear disorders. ST-40 treats leg atrophy, swelling and and pain in the throat, sudden loss of voice, and plumstone throat. BL-58 treats weak legs, difficulty walking, lower limb pain. LUO POINTS TREAT treat psychological and emotional disorders. LI-6 and BL-58 do not list emotional symptoms. ST-40 treats manic-depression, mad laughter, desire to ascend to high places, undress and run around, and seeing ghosts. DU-1 treats hemorrhoids, benefits the two lower yin, activate the channel and alleviate pain, and calm the Spirit. Its indications reflect du 