      ],
      "exp_en": "The chong mai has five branches. The head branch starts at the chest, flows to the throat, curves around the lips, and terminate below the eye. Through this branch, the chong mai brings Qi and Blood to the chin area and the chong mai loses some Blood with menstruation. This results in the chong mai having a little less Blood in women than in men. Blood promotes the growth of hair. This relative lack of Blood in the head branch of the chong mai in women explains why women do not grow beards. Alternatively, facial hair increases in women after menopause. This is because menses end which results in the head branch of the chong mai having a little more Blood after menopause. The head branch goes to the throat and head and when there is Rebellious Qi in the chong mai the head branch is responsible for the feeling of lump in the throat or heat in the head. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 906",
      "exp_hant": "衝脈共有五條分支。其中頭部分支起於胸部，上行至咽喉，環繞口唇，終止於眼下。透過此分支，衝脈將氣血送達下頦部位；而女性因月經而耗損部分血液，使得衝脈的血量較男性略少。血能養髮，衝脈頭部分支血液相對不足，因此女性不長鬍鬚。相反地，女性停經後臉部毛髮會增多，這是因為月經停止後，衝脈頭部分支的血量略為增加所致。頭部分支上達咽喉與頭面，當衝脈氣逆時，此分支即是造成咽喉異物感或頭面部烘熱感的原因。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia著，2015年版，第906頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 780,
      "question_en": "Which of the following are strong indications for Rebellious Qi of the Penetrating Vessel (chong mai)?",
      "question_hant": "下列何者是衝脈氣逆的有力指徵？",
