        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "qi rising from lower abdomen to throat, sense of internal urgency",
          "hant": "氣從少腹上衝咽喉、內在急迫感",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete answer. In and of itself chest tightness can be due to multiple causes and it is not particularly indicative of Rebellious Qi of the Penetrating Vessel. In order for chest tightness to be part of this pattern it needs additional symptoms, for example, in the legs (cold feet), lower abdomen (fullness, irregular/painful periods), epigastrium and hypogastrium (fullness, distension, pain, nausea), chest (breast distention, palpitations, chest tightness/oppression), throat and head (lump in throat, heat in face, dizziness). Not all symptoms need to occur, but at least 3-4 symptoms at different levels or burners need to be present. These symptoms follow the pathway of the chong mai. Importantly, the constellation of symptoms occur within a background of internal urgency that includes restlessness, fidgetiness, and vague anxiety. There are two types of Rebellious Qi of the Penetrating Vessel: primary and secondary. The primary pattern is strictly a Full condition arising from emotional stress which makes Qi rise up or stagnate in the chong mai. The secondary pattern is a mixed Empty-Full pattern. The rebellious Qi (excess) in the chong mai is a consequence that arises from a Blood deficiency or Kidney Deficiency. Due to deficiency the qi from the chong mai becomes unrooted and stagnates-rises upward. The opening (SP-4) and coupled (PC-6) are sequentially needled to activate the chong mai. Then additional points are selected are to address various aspects of the Rebellious Qi. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 909-910",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整的答案。單純的胸悶可由多種原因引起，並不特別指向衝脈氣逆。若胸悶要歸屬於此證型，還需伴隨其他部位的症狀，例如下肢（足冷）、少腹（脹滿、月經不調或痛經）、脘腹（脹滿、脹痛、噁心）、胸部（乳房脹痛、心悸、胸悶）、咽喉與頭部（咽中異物感、面部烘熱、頭暈）等。並非所有症狀都需同時出現，但至少須有3至4個不同部位或三焦層次的症狀，且這些症狀皆循衝脈循行路線分佈。值得注意的是，這些症狀往往伴隨一種內在的急迫感，包括躁動不安、坐立難安與莫名焦慮。衝脈氣逆可分為原發性與繼發性兩種類型：原發性屬純實證，多因情志壓力導致衝脈氣機上逆或鬱滯；繼發性則為虛實夾雜之證，衝脈的氣逆（實）乃因血虛或腎虛所致，因虛而使衝脈之氣失於根植，鬱滯上衝。治療時依序針刺開穴SP-4與配穴PC-6以啟動衝脈，再依氣逆的不同表現加選其他穴位。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia著，2015年版，第909-910頁"
