          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Transient infectious agents (bacteria, fungi, viruses) are on the surface of the skin and are picked up from one patient or by touching surfaces and then can possibly be transferred to another patient. Soap hand washing is sufficient for eliminating/reducing transient pathogens. Resident pathogens (example, staphylococci) are lodged deeper in the skin. When there is no sink available, an alcohol-based sanitizer can kill transient hand flora but cannot replace hand washing in removing all hand contaminants. If hands are visibly soiled or have blood or body fluids, then washing with soap and water is the best method. An antiseptic towelette can be an alternative to washing the hands when the hands are visibly soiled but is still not considered the best method. If no sink is available, then an alcohol sanitizer or an antiseptic towelettes can be used instead. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 170, 171",
      "exp_hant": "暫居性感染源（細菌、真菌、病毒）附著於皮膚表面，可能經由接觸病患或接觸物體表面而沾染，並可能傳播給其他病患。以肥皂洗手即足以清除／減少暫居性病原體；常居性病原體（例如葡萄球菌）則深藏於皮膚深層。若無洗手台可用，酒精類消毒劑可殺滅暫居性手部菌叢，但無法完全取代洗手以清除所有手部污染物。若雙手有明顯污漬或沾有血液或體液，以肥皂與清水洗手是最佳方法。若雙手有明顯污漬，消毒濕紙巾可作為洗手的替代方案，但仍非最佳方法。若無洗手台可用，則可改用酒精消毒劑或消毒濕紙巾。Clean Needle Technique，第7版，第170、171頁"
    },
