      "exp_en": "MA is a unit for electrical current known as the milliampere. One milliampere is equal to one-thousandth of an ampere. High levels of mA can cause muscular spasms. The mA level should be below the level of pain that as experienced by the patient. In most use of EA, it is best to avoid muscular contraction unless muscle stimulation is the expected outcome. With sufficient mA, skeletal, cardiac, and smooth muscle fibers can be stimulated with EA causing unwanted muscle contractions. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 44, 45",
      "exp_hant": "mA（毫安）是電流的單位，一毫安等於千分之一安培。過高的毫安數可能引起肌肉痙攣，其強度應低於患者感受到疼痛的程度。在大多數電針應用中，除非肌肉刺激本身是預期的治療效果，否則最好避免引起肌肉收縮。若毫安數足夠，骨骼肌、心肌與平滑肌纖維皆可能受電針刺激而產生非預期的肌肉收縮。Clean Needle Technique，第7版，第44、45頁"
