          "key": "D",
          "en": "chemicals that reduce the number of pathogens on inanimate objects",
          "hant": "能降低無生命物體表面病原體數量的化學物質",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Examples of disinfectants are bleach or Staphene. Both antiseptics and disinfectants eliminate disease-causing pathogens. The difference between the two is how each is used. Antiseptics are applied to living skin or tissue to prevent infection. Disinfectants are applied to surfaces or other inanimate objects. Disinfectants are stronger and more toxic. Sterilization kills or removes all living organisms (viruses, bacteria, cells) from an object. Disinfection kills disease-causing organisms, but not all organisms present on an object. Heat, radiation, or chemical processes are used to sterilize objects (medical instruments). Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 228",
      "exp_hant": "消毒劑的例子包括漂白水或Staphene消毒液。防腐劑（antiseptics）與消毒劑（disinfectants）皆能清除致病病原體，兩者差異在於使用方式：防腐劑用於活體皮膚或組織以預防感染，消毒劑則用於物體表面或其他無生命物體，且消毒劑通常效力更強、毒性也更高。滅菌（sterilization）是殺滅或去除物體上所有生物體（病毒、細菌、細胞）；消毒（disinfection）則是殺滅致病生物體，但並非物體上所有的生物體都會被消滅。醫療器械的滅菌通常使用熱、輻射或化學方法。Clean Needle Technique，第7版，第228頁"
