      "exp_en": "This is the best and most complete answer. An HIV infected person without symptoms can still spread the virus to others. HIV does not survive long outside the human body on surfaces. It cannot reproduce. HIV is not spread through air or water, insects (including mosquitoes or ticks), saliva, tears, or sweat, casual contact like shaking hands or sharing dishes, closed-mouth kissing, or toilet seats. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 146",
      "exp_hant": "此為最佳且最完整的答案。感染愛滋病毒而無症狀的人仍可能將病毒傳染給他人。HIV在人體外的物體表面存活時間不長，也無法自行繁殖。HIV不會透過空氣或水、昆蟲（包括蚊子或蜱）、唾液、淚液或汗液、日常接觸（如握手或共用餐具）、閉口親吻或馬桶座傳播。Clean Needle Technique，第7版，第146頁"
