      "exp_en": "Blood and Body Fluids interact and exchange. Blood stasis can impair the circulation of Body Fluids causing dry skin. Dry skin from chronic Blood stasis is common among the elderly. There will also be a darkening of the skin, dark-purple or dry-lusterless nails, and more general symptoms of Blood stasis (purple tongue, fixed stabbing pain, pain worse at night). The most common type of skin dryness, especially in female patients, is due to Liver Blood deficiency. Liver and Kidney yin deficiency dryness is also more common in the elderly but it is without dark skin and other symptoms and signs of Blood stasis. In some patients the dry skin can arise from a Stomach Yin deficiency.The Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 360",
      "exp_hant": "血與津液相互轉化、彼此影響，血瘀可阻礙津液的輸布運行而導致皮膚乾燥。因慢性血瘀所致的皮膚乾燥在老年患者中相當常見，並常伴隨膚色暗沉、指甲呈暗紫色或乾枯無光澤，以及其他更廣泛的血瘀症狀（舌質紫暗、痛有定處且呈刺痛、夜間痛甚）。最常見的皮膚乾燥類型，特別是在女性患者中，則是因肝血虛所致。肝腎陰虛所致的乾燥也常見於老年人，但不會伴隨膚色暗沉及其他血瘀的症狀與徵象。部分患者的皮膚乾燥則可能源自胃陰虛。The Channels of Acupuncture，Maciocia著，2006年版，第360頁"
