      "exp_en": "The Bladder luo-connecting channel starts at BL-58 (fei yang) and then immediately proceeds to connect to the Kidney primary channel, where it ends. Like other luo-connecting points, BL-58 (fei yang) can be selected to treat bleeding disorders. BL-58 (fei yang) can treat bleeding hemorrhoids, LU-7 (lie que) for coughing blood and bloody urine. SP-4 (gong sun) for bloody stools, HT-5 (tong li) for uterine bleeding, LI-6 (pian li) for epistaxis, KI-4 (da zhong) for uterine bleeding and coughing blood, TB-5 (wai guan) for epistaxis, LR-5 (li gou) for uterine bleeding and red vaginal discharges, REN-15 (jiu wei) for coughing blood, and DU-1 (chang qiang) for vomiting blood. The length of the Bladder luo-connecting channel is short. The length of the Lung luo-connecting channel (starts at LU-7 lie que and travels to the thenar eminence) and that of the Gall Bladder connecting channel (starts at GB-37 guang ming and descends a short distance to connect with the Liver primary channel) are also short.A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 253, 74, 419; The Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 261, 262",
