      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the best and most complete answer. Muscle meridians are not directly connected to the internal zangfu. However, organ problems can be transmitted to the muscle meridians. For example, Liver yang rising can cause stiff neck muscles. Deficiency of the Spleen and Stomach can cause flaccid and weak muscles. External pathogenic factors can invade the muscle meridians without causing any symptoms on the exterior of the body such as aversion to cold, fever, and sore throat. External pathogenic cold invading the muscles will cause contraction, spasm, stiffness, and pain. Cold can remain in the meridians for a long period of time. Awakening with sudden pain and stiffness in the morning can be due to a cold invasion of the muscle meridians. Pain due to cold in the muscle meridians is alleviated with the application of heat. If the pathogenic cold is not expelled from the muscles it can be the cause of repeated stiffness, especially in a deficient yang patient. Pathogenic wind invading the muscles can cause spasm, pain, and facial paralysis or tremors. Wind invasion of the muscle meridians manifest as generalized muscle aches and contraction whereas with cold invasion of the muscles the pain, contraction, and stiffness if more localized. External pathogenic dampness invading the muscle meridians results in a dull ache and a heavy feeling. The muscle pain worsens with damp weather. Dampness invading the muscle meridians is seen in chronic post-viral syndromes. Trauma can cause either qi stagnation with a feeling local distention or trauma can cause blood stagnation with more severe pain which has a stabbing quality. Trauma with blood stasis in the muscles can become chronic pain in the area. Overuse of a joint or repetitive stress syndrome can lead to joint leads to pain and tingling in the muscle meridians. This can involve typing, overusing a mouse with the computer, or arising from repeated movements in sports. The overuse can lead qi stasis in the muscles causing contraction, spasm, and pain.meridians of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 313, 314",
      "exp_hant": "此為最佳且最完整的答案。經筋並不直接聯繫內在臟腑，但臟腑病變仍可能傳導至經筋，例如肝陽上亢可導致頸部肌肉僵硬，脾胃虛弱則可導致肌肉痿軟無力。外邪可侵犯經筋而不引起惡寒、發熱、咽痛等體表症狀。外寒侵犯經筋會造成拘攣、痙攣、僵硬與疼痛，寒邪可能長期滯留於經脈之中；晨起突然感到疼痛僵硬，可能即是經筋受寒所致，此類寒性疼痛可因熱敷而緩解。若寒邪未能自肌肉中袪除，可能造成反覆僵硬，尤其在陽虛體質的患者身上更為明顯。外風侵犯經筋可導致痙攣、疼痛及面癱或面部顫動，風邪侵犯經筋多表現為全身性的肌肉痠痛與拘攣，而寒邪侵犯經筋所致的疼痛、拘攣與僵硬則較為局限。外濕侵犯經筋則表現為隱痛與沉重感，肌肉疼痛在潮濕天氣中會加重，濕邪侵犯經筋常見於慢性病毒感染後症候群。外傷可導致氣滯，出現局部脹滿感；亦可導致血瘀，疼痛較為劇烈並呈刺痛性質，外傷伴血瘀留滯於肌肉中可演變為該部位的慢性疼痛。關節過度使用或重複性勞損可導致經筋出現疼痛與麻刺感，常見於打字、過度使用滑鼠或運動中反覆動作所致，過度使用可造成肌肉氣滯，出現拘攣、痙攣與疼痛。meridians of Acupuncture，Maciocia著，2006年版，第313、314頁"
    },
