          "key": "D",
          "en": "they have a more direct relationship to the zangfu",
          "hant": "它們與臟腑的關係更為直接",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Other than the six Extraordinary Yang Organs (Uterus, Brain, Marrow, Gall Bladder, Bones, Blood Vessels) the extraordinary vessels do not have a direct relationship to the zangfu. However, the ren mai, du mai, and chong mai do have an intimate connection to the Kidneys. Various authors have given different reasons to explain why they are extraordinary. Classic of Difficulties says that they are extraordinary because they are not constrained by the primary channel system and can act independently. Li Shi Zhen says that they do not have an interior-exterior relationship like the primary channels do. Modern textbooks say they add something extra to the channel system as they are a reservoir of qi and can transfer qi to the primary channels when needed.The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 868",
      "exp_hant": "除了六個奇恆之腑（子宮、腦、髓、膽、骨、脈）之外，奇經八脈與臟腑並無直接關係；不過任脈、督脈與衝脈確實與腎有著密切的聯繫。歷代醫家對於奇經八脈為何被稱為「奇」，各有不同見解：《難經》認為奇經不受正經系統的約束，能夠獨立運作；李時珍則認為奇經不像正經那樣具有表裡關係；現代教材則認為奇經為經絡系統增添了額外的功能，因其作為氣的儲存庫，能在正經需要時提供氣的補充。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia著，2015年版，第868頁"
    },
