      ],
      "exp_en": "The yuan qi flows through the extra-ordinary meridians. The qi (ying qi) of the primary meridians flows through the divergent meridians. The superficial luo meridians (regular luo, minute luo, and superficial luo) occupy the space between the skin and the muscles which is called \"cou li\". The superficial luo meridians are above the primary meridians and it is through these luo meridians that the wei qi circulates and protects. The primary meridians circulate ying or nourishing qi. The deep luo meridians are located below the primary meridians and are associated with Blood and blood vessels. As the luo (superficial and deep) are located between the primary meridians, the luo meridians are important in the communication between the exterior, more superficial aspect of the body and the internal, deeper aspect of the body. For example, during the day wei qi circulates on the body surface and at night flows into the interior.Meridians of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 238",
      "exp_hant": "元氣運行於奇經之中。正經之氣（營氣）則運行於經別之中。淺部絡脈（包括別絡、孫絡與浮絡）位於皮膚與肌肉之間，此空間稱為「腠理」。淺部絡脈位居正經之上，衛氣即透過這些絡脈循行並發揮護衛作用。正經運行的是營氣，亦即滋養之氣。深部絡脈則位於正經之下，與血及血脈相關。由於絡脈（淺部與深部）位於正經之間，絡脈在人體外部較淺層與內部較深層之間的溝通上極為重要。例如，衛氣白天行於體表，夜間則流入體內。（出處：Meridians of Acupuncture，Maciocia，2006年版，第238頁）"
