    {
      "number": 855,
      "question_en": "A 25 year-old female volleyball athlete complained of shoulder pain. She thought she had a rotator cuff injury. She did a course of remedial exercises which did not improve the shoulder pain. She said that she recently noticed mild swelling in the hand and arm. The physical exam showed mild swelling of the right hand and arm. The ROM of the right shoulder was normal. The right radial pulse was normal. Which action would you take for this patient?",
      "question_hant": "一位25歲的女性排球運動員主訴肩部疼痛。她認為自己可能是旋轉肌袖損傷，因此進行了一個療程的矯正運動，但肩痛並未改善。她表示最近注意到手部與手臂有輕微腫脹。理學檢查發現右手與右臂有輕微腫脹。右肩活動範圍（ROM）正常。右側橈動脈搏動正常。針對此病患，您會採取下列何種處置？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "semi-urgent referral to primary care physician",
          "hant": "半緊急轉診至基層照護醫師",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "have a family member drive patient to ED",
          "hant": "請家屬開車送病患至急診室",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "treat with acupuncture 1x per week for 5 weeks",
          "hant": "以針灸治療，每週一次，共五週",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "call 911 for emergency assist",
          "hant": "撥打911請求緊急救護",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is swelling of one arm with shoulder and/or axillary pain. Subclavian vein deep venous thrombosis (SVDVT) is assumed present until proven otherwise. SVDVT can occur in young athletes who use their arms a lot. In the early stages there are no symptoms or mild shoulder pain. In later stages, there is moderate arm swelling and pain which worsens with activity and improves with rest. Trauma patients with SVDVT have a history of neck and/or shoulder trauma. In SVDVT clot formation causes pressure in the distal veins of the arm and cause swelling. In this condition there are no changes in the pulses because this is a venous and not an arterial problem. In SVDVT, unlike DVT of the calf, there is no danger of a pulmonary embolus. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 177-178",
      "exp_hant": "此處的紅旗警訊為單側手臂腫脹合併肩部及／或腋窩疼痛。在排除其他可能性之前，應假定為鎖骨下靜脈深部靜脈血栓（SVDVT）。SVDVT可能發生於經常大量使用手臂的年輕運動員身上。早期可能沒有症狀，或僅有輕微肩痛。到了後期，則會出現中度的手臂腫脹與疼痛，活動時加重、休息時緩解。因外傷導致SVDVT的病患，通常有頸部及／或肩部外傷病史。在SVDVT中，血栓形成會對手臂遠端靜脈造成壓力，因而引起腫脹。由於這是靜脈而非動脈的問題，因此脈搏並不會出現改變。與小腿的深部靜脈血栓不同，SVDVT並無肺栓塞的危險。（出處：An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals，2012年，Anzaldua，第177-178頁）"
    },
