      "number": 862,
      "question_en": "A 70 year-old female reports dizziness and shortness of breath. As she walks to rest on the table she feels very weak. Her pulse rate is very slow. A pulse rate of _____ beats per minute is a red flag referral for this patient..",
      "question_hant": "一位70歲女性主訴頭暈與呼吸急促。當她走向治療床休息時，感到非常虛弱。她的脈搏速率非常緩慢。對此病患而言，脈搏速率為每分鐘_____下，屬於需要轉診的紅旗警訊。",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "65 to 70",
          "hant": "65至70",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "40 to 50",
          "hant": "40至50",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "70 to 80",
          "hant": "70至80",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "55 to 60",
          "hant": "55至60",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Bradycardia is a heart rate slower than normal. For an adult the resting heart rates is between between 60 and 100 times a minute. With bradycardia, the rate is less than 60 beats a minute. Some individuals (athletes) have a naturally slow heart rate. However, if the heart rate drops suddenly to 40 to 50 per minute it means that the heart becomes unable to transmit electrical impulses to the ventricles. With bradycardia the brain and organs will have insufficient oxygen that can cause syncope (fainting), dizziness, fatigue, shortness of breath, confusion, chest pain, and becoming easily tired with activities. If the patient has bradycardia and faints or has difficulty breathing lasting more than a few minutes, then the patient needs a high priority emergency referral. The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 35",
      "exp_hant": "心搏過緩是指心跳速率低於正常值。成人靜止心跳速率一般介於每分鐘60至100下之間。心搏過緩時，心跳速率則低於每分鐘60下。有些人（如運動員）天生心跳速率就較慢。然而，若心跳速率驟降至每分鐘40至50下，則意味著心臟已無法將電衝動正常傳導至心室。心搏過緩時，腦部及各器官會出現供氧不足，可能導致昏厥（暈厥）、頭暈、疲勞、呼吸急促、意識混亂、胸痛，以及活動時容易疲倦。若病患出現心搏過緩並伴有暈厥，或呼吸困難持續數分鐘以上，則需要高優先等級的緊急轉診。（出處：The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals，Stephenson，2013年版，第35頁）"
    },
