    {
      "number": 877,
      "question_en": "An active 40 year-old male has back pain as the chief complaint. He describes that he was lifting boxes and at one point felt his lower back \"catch\". Later during the day he could not comfortably sit, lie down, or stand. Two days later he experienced electric \"shocks\" and tingling sensations down the right leg and ball of foot. During the examination he could only flex the lumbar spine about five degrees. If he went further than that, he would feel a jolt down the right leg and foot. The right plantar reflexes were diminished as compared to the left side. There was no muscle atrophy or loss of muscle tone in the right leg. There was numbness of sensation around his right ankle. What would you do?",
      "question_hant": "一位活動量大的40歲男性以背痛為主訴前來就診。他描述自己在搬運箱子時，腰部突然感到「卡住」的感覺。當天稍晚，他無論坐、臥或站立都感到不適。兩天後，他的右腿及腳掌前部出現如電擊般的「觸電感」及麻刺感。理學檢查時，他的腰椎只能前屈約五度，若再繼續前屈，右腿與右腳便會出現觸電般的抽痛感。與左側相比，右側的蹠反射減弱。右腿並無肌肉萎縮或肌張力喪失的情形。右腳踝周圍有麻木感。針對此情況，您會怎麼做？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "treat with acupuncture with a semi-urgent referral to their physician",
          "hant": "以針灸治療，並半緊急轉診至其醫師",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "treat with acupuncture with a non-urgent referral to a neurosurgeon",
          "hant": "以針灸治療，並非緊急轉診至神經外科醫師",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "treat with acupuncture with an urgent referral to a neurosurgeon",
          "hant": "以針灸治療，並緊急轉診至神經外科醫師",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "do not treat with acupuncture; call 911",
          "hant": "不進行針灸治療；撥打911",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is low back pain with progressive leg numbness, tingling, and weakness. Compression neuropathy from lumbar nerve root pressure (radiculopathy) is assumed until proven otherwise. The type of referral depends on the severity. GRADE 1: the back is mildly painful with intermittent paresthesia in buttock, hip, and/or leg. There are no sensory, motor or reflex impairment in the lower extremity. In grade 1 there is no compression of motor fibers and sensory fibers are minimally compressed. ACTION: no immediate referral is necessary. GRADE 2: back moderately painful with constant paresthesia and objective sensory loss in buttock, leg and/or foot. In grade 2 sensory fibers are significantly compressed with no significant compression in motor fibers. ACTION: aggressive treatment and possible co-treatment with the primary care physician on a timely basis. GRADE 3: the back is very painful with paresthesia, constant numbness, weakness, and loss of reflex in the leg and/or foot, but no atrophy present. In grade 3 the sensory fibers are compressed and the motor fibers are mildly compressed. ACTION: aggressive treatment and referred on a semi-urgent basis to their physician or a spine specialist. GRADE 4: back is severely painful and/or numbness and/or paresthesia with inability to move some muscles. Muscle atrophy in buttock, hip, leg, and/or foot. In grade 4 there is major compression of sensory and motor fibers. ACTION: acupuncture treatment should not delay a semi-urgent referral to their physician or a neurosurgeon. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 96-97",
      "exp_hant": "此處的紅旗警訊為下背痛合併進行性的下肢麻木、麻刺感及無力。在排除其他可能性之前，應假定為腰椎神經根受壓所致的壓迫性神經病變（神經根病變）。轉診的類型取決於嚴重程度。第一級：背部輕度疼痛，臀部、髖部及／或腿部有間歇性感覺異常，下肢無感覺、運動或反射功能的損害。第一級中，運動神經纖維未受壓迫，感覺神經纖維僅受到極輕微壓迫。處置：無須立即轉診。第二級：背部中度疼痛，臀部、腿部及／或足部有持續性感覺異常及客觀可測得之感覺喪失。第二級中，感覺神經纖維受到明顯壓迫，而運動神經纖維並無明顯受壓。處置：積極治療，並可能需要與基層照護醫師適時共同照護。第三級：背部劇烈疼痛，伴有感覺異常、持續性麻木、無力，以及腿部及／或足部反射喪失，但尚無肌肉萎縮。第三級中，感覺神經纖維受壓，運動神經纖維則輕度受壓。處置：積極治療，並半緊急轉診至其醫師或脊椎專科醫師。第四級：背部劇痛及／或麻木及／或感覺異常，並伴有部分肌肉無法活動；臀部、髖部、腿部及／或足部出現肌肉萎縮。第四級中，感覺與運動神經纖維皆受到嚴重壓迫。處置：針灸治療不應延誤半緊急轉診至其醫師或神經外科醫師的時機。（出處：An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals，2012年，Anzaldua，第96-97頁）"
    },
