      "exp_en": "This is the most complete answer. Intubation, an emergency procedure, is the placement of a flexible plastic tube into the trachea to maintain an open airway so that the patient can breathe or to serve as a conduit through which to administer certain drugs. It is not part of the scope of practice for an acupuncurist to perform this procedure which is done by EMTs or doctors. Whenever there is bleeding, first responders must put on gloves. Either a disposable mouth shield or ventilation bag as a resuscitation barrier. Include CPR one page instruction to refresh your memory of the CPR steps. For removing broken needles with forceps, California acupuncturists are required to immediately consult a physician. Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 113",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整的答案。插管是一種緊急處置，是將一條柔軟的塑膠管置入氣管，以維持呼吸道暢通，使病患能夠呼吸，或作為投予特定藥物的通道。此項處置並不屬於針灸師的執業範圍，而是由緊急救護技術員（EMT）或醫師執行。凡有出血情形，第一線急救人員皆須配戴手套。復甦防護膜可使用拋棄式口部防護罩或通氣袋。應備有CPR單頁說明，以便隨時複習CPR步驟。至於以鑷子取出斷針，加州針灸師依規定必須立即諮詢醫師。（出處：Acupuncture Risk Management，CMS Press，Kailin，1997年版，第113頁）"
