          "hant": "列缺、照海、血海、膈俞、曲池、三陰交",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "LU-7 (lie que), KI-6 (zhao hai), REN-4 (guan yuan), BL-18 (gan shu), KI-2 (ran gu)",
          "hant": "列缺、照海、關元、肝俞、然谷",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "SP-6 (san yin jiao), LR-8 (qu quan), REN-4 (guan yuan), BL-18 (gan shu), KI-6 (zhao hai)",
          "hant": "三陰交、曲泉、關元、肝俞、照海",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The original assessment and treatment was Kidney Qi Deficiency. KI-7 and BL-23 were selected to tonify and warm the Kidneys. REN-6 and ST-36 tonify the overall body qi. That her menstrual period did not improve could mean that some important elements in the diagnosis were missed. The lack of tongue coating indicated a deficient yin condition. The drug Restasis is for chronic dry eyes, another yin deficiency symptom. The practitioner did not know or ask about the reason for the prescription. Eye dryness is a key symptom of Liver yin deficiency. The back pain and tinnitus point to the Kidneys. The dizziness can be caused by either the Liver or the Kidneys. There are not enough symptoms or strong enough symptoms to point to a Kidney yang deficiency (sometimes feels cold). What we are looking at is a Liver and Kidney yin deficiency as the root pattern for the early and scanty periods. SP-6, LR-8 and BL-18 tonify Liver yin. SP-6, KI-6, and REN-4 tonify Kidney yin. REN-4 regulates the Penetrating Vessel to strengthen the Uterus. SP-6 is a major point for regulating menstruation. The Rx with KI-2 would be selected if the Liver and Kidney yin deficiency generated Empty Heat, of which there are no symptoms. The Rx with LI-11 would be selected if the pattern was Hot Blood. The LU-7 and KI-6 can often be selected to treat menstrual problems as these two points regulate the Directing Vessel which nourishes Blood and Yin, Regulates the Uterus, promotes conception, maintains pregnancy, and promotes lactation. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 640",
      "exp_hant": "最初的辨證與治療為腎氣虛。選用復溜（KI-7）與腎俞（BL-23）以溫補腎氣，氣海（REN-6）與足三里（ST-36）則用以補益整體元氣。月經未見改善，可能意味著辨證時遺漏了某些重要線索。舌無苔提示陰虛之候。Restasis此藥用於治療慢性乾眼症，這也是陰虛的另一項表現。原執業者並不清楚，也未詢問此藥的用途。眼乾是肝陰虛的關鍵症狀之一。腰痛與耳鳴則指向腎。頭暈則可能由肝或腎所致。目前的症狀不足以，也不夠明顯地指向腎陽虛（偶爾怕冷）。我們此處所應辨識的，是以肝腎陰虛作為經量少、經期提前的根本病機。三陰交（SP-6）、曲泉（LR-8）與肝俞（BL-18）可補肝陰；三陰交（SP-6）、照海（KI-6）與關元（REN-4）可補腎陰。關元能調理衝脈以強健子宮。三陰交是調理月經的重要穴位。若肝腎陰虛已化生虛熱，則應選用含然谷（KI-2）的處方，但本案並無此類症狀。若證屬血熱，則應選用含曲池（LI-11）的處方。列缺（LU-7）與照海（KI-6）常用於治療經期問題，因這兩個穴位能調理任脈，任脈具有滋養血與陰、調理子宮、助孕、安胎及促進泌乳等功能。（出處：Foundations of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia，2015年版，第640頁）"
    },
    {
      "number": 886,
      "question_en": "A 38 year-old female patient has had bleeding between periods for the past three years. The mid-cycle bleeding was scanty but also sticky-thick and without clots. She reported thick-yellow vaginal discharges. She also had frequent fatigue, achy joint pain, a feeling of oppression in the chest, and poor appetite. She said that her urination was scanty and dark. She reported feeling hot but without desire to drink. The tongue had a sticky-yellow coating and the pulse was slippery-rapid. She was treated six times over a three month period with BL-22 (san jiao shu), SP-9 (yin ling quan), GB-41 (zu lin qi), TB-5 (wai guan), ST-29 (gui lai), and SP-8 (di ji). On the follow up visit, she reported improvement in the vaginal discharge, the urine was not as dark, an improvement in appetite. The mid-cycle bleeding improved only a little. Which point would you have added to the prescription?",
      "question_hant": "一位38歲女性病患經間期出血已持續三年。經間期出血量少，質地黏稠且無血塊。她主訴陰道分泌物黏稠色黃。此外還有經常性疲倦、關節痠痛、胸悶及食慾不振。她表示小便量少且色深。自覺身熱但不欲飲水。舌苔黃膩，脈滑數。她在三個月內接受了六次治療，選用三焦俞（BL-22）、陰陵泉（SP-9）、足臨泣（GB-41）、外關（TB-5）、歸來（ST-29）及地機（SP-8）。回診時，她表示陰道分泌物已改善，小便顏色不再那麼深，食慾也有進步。經間期出血則僅稍有改善。您會在處方中加入哪一個穴位？",
      "image": null,
