      ],
      "exp_en": "The original presentation points to Liver yang rising (migraine, insomnia, red tongue, deep pulse). LR-3 smooths Liver qi. TB-5 and GB-20 treat the shaoyang channels to move the qi blockage. SP-6 tonifes the yin to nourish wood. The results of the treatment indicated that the Liver qi was moving and that the yin deficiency was improving. However, the root of the problem (migraine) was more stubborn. The lower 2/5 of the sensory area line treats migraine and trigeminal neuralgia. This is an appropriate point for this patient. The point lateral to the occipital protuberance is the Balance area. This point treats balance disorders. The point that is the upper 1/5 of the motor area treats lower limb paralysis. The point above the ear apex is the Vertigo and Hearing area that treats tinnitus, vertigo, and Meniere's syndrome. Bensky, 1981, page 499-512",
      "exp_hant": "最初的臨床表現指向肝陽上亢（偏頭痛、失眠、舌紅、脈沉）。太衝能疏肝理氣。外關與風池能調理少陽經以疏通氣機的阻滯。三陰交能滋陰以養肝木。治療結果顯示肝氣已見疏通，陰虛也有所改善。然而，此病之根本（偏頭痛）較為頑固難癒。感覺區下2/5處能治療偏頭痛與三叉神經痛，對此病患而言是合適的選穴。枕外隆凸旁的穴位為平衡區，用於治療平衡障礙。運動區上1/5處用於治療下肢癱瘓。耳尖上方的穴位為暈聽區，用於治療耳鳴、眩暈及梅尼爾氏症。（出處：Bensky，1981年版，第499-512頁）"
