    {
      "number": 900,
      "question_en": "A patient has aversion to cold, slight fever, absence of sweating, headache, stiff neck, sneezing, runny nose with white discharge, breathlessness, and a floating-tight pulse. What is the pattern?",
      "question_hant": "一位病患惡寒、輕微發熱、無汗、頭痛、頸項僵硬、打噴嚏、流清白鼻涕、呼吸短促，脈浮緊。此屬何種證型？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Invasion of Wind-Cold with Prevalence of Wind",
          "hant": "風寒外襲，風重於寒",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Invasion of Wind-Cold",
          "hant": "風寒外襲",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Invasion of Wind-Cold with Prevalence of Cold",
          "hant": "風寒外襲，寒重於風",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Invasion of Wind-Heat",
          "hant": "風熱外襲",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the tai yang or Greater Yang stage with Wind-Cold with more cold than wind. In the pattern of Invasion of Wind-Cold with Prevalence of Cold the emphasis is on Cold more than Wind. The ying qi and the wei qi are both in excess. This is an external-excess-cold pattern (8 Principles). There is a lack of sweating because the excess Cold contracts the skin pores and prevents sweating. As this is an excess Cold, covering oneself with blankets does not eliminate the cold feeling in the body. The pathogenic Cold can impair the descending of the Lung qi with the Lung unable to transform Fluids in the Upper Jiao. This leads to a runny nose with a white discharge. The pulse is tight because the pathogenic Cold, tightens-contracts the pulse. When the pathogenic factor obstructs the wei qi in the space between the skin and muscles (exterior of the body), the warming function of the wei qi is impaired and causes aversion to cold. When external Wind obstructs the tai yang channels (Bladder, Small Intestine) the muscles of the neck contract causing a stiff neck or occipital headache. The floating pulse results from the wei qi increasing on the surface of the body to resist the pathogenic factor. The treatment principle is to Release the Exterior, Expel Wind-Cold, Restore the Lung functions of descending and diffusion. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 755; 2005 Edition, page 712",
      "exp_hant": "此為太陽（表陽）階段，風寒之邪中寒重於風。在「風寒外襲、寒重於風」之證中，病機著重於寒邪而非風邪。營氣與衛氣皆呈現有餘之象，此屬八綱辨證中的表、實、寒證。由於寒邪過盛使皮膚毛孔收縮，故無汗。由於此為實寒，蓋被取暖並不能消除體內的寒冷感。寒邪能妨礙肺氣的肅降，使肺無法正常運化上焦水液，因而導致流清白色鼻涕。脈緊則是因寒邪使脈道收緊拘急所致。當邪氣阻遏衛氣於皮膚與肌肉之間（體表）運行時，衛氣的溫煦功能受損，因而導致惡寒。當外風阻滯太陽經（膀胱經、小腸經）時，頸部肌肉收緊拘急，因而出現頸項僵硬或後枕部頭痛。脈浮則是由於衛氣增強於體表以抵抗邪氣所致。治療原則為解表、袪風寒，並恢復肺之肅降與宣發功能。（出處：Foundations of Chinese Medicine，Maciocia，2015年版，第755頁；2005年版，第712頁）"
    },
