      "exp_en": "Liver Fire. LR-3 (tai chong) and BL-18 (gan shu) neutralize the Fire in the Liver and Gall Bladder. In acute cases, LR-2 (xing jian), BL-62 (shen mai) and BL-63 (jin men) can be added to drain the Liver Fire. GB-20 (feng chi), BL-2 (zan zhu), and GB-1 (tong zi liao) are selected as local points near the eyes. The yuan-source point LI-4 (he gu) disperses Wind and clears the vision. In TCM, glaucoma can be due to Kidney yin xu with empty fire or it can be fire in the Liver to ascending and injuring the qi in the channels.Acupuncture a Comprehensive Text, Bensky, 1981, in section starting on page 681",
      "exp_hant": "肝火。LR-3 (tai chong) 太衝與 BL-18 (gan shu) 肝俞可清瀉肝膽之火。急性發作時，可加用 LR-2 (xing jian) 行間、BL-62 (shen mai) 申脈及 BL-63 (jin men) 金門以瀉肝火。GB-20 (feng chi) 風池、BL-2 (zan zhu) 攢竹及 GB-1 (tong zi liao) 瞳子髎為眼周局部取穴。原穴 LI-4 (he gu) 合谷可疏散風邪、清利目竅。中醫認為青光眼可因腎陰虛而生虛火，或因肝火上炎、損傷經氣所致。參考資料：《Acupuncture a Comprehensive Text》，Bensky，1981年，第681頁起。"
