      ],
      "exp_en": "Strabismus (crossed eyes) is misalignment of the eyes that is most often caused by a disorder in the eye muscles. Strabismus is classified by the direction the eye turns. Internal turning is called esotropia. External turning is called exotropia. Upward turning is called hypertropia. Jian ming is 0.4 units below BL-1 (jing ming) and slightly lateral, just inside the inferior margin of the orbit. Qiu hou is at the inferior border of the orbit, about 1/4 the distance from the lateral to the medial side of the orbit, and is used for the treatment of internal strabismus. Though tai yang can treat eye disorders, it is not the best possible choice here as there are more effective local points. The method is to slowly insert the local needles with slight rotation to produce a mild electrical sensation for a short time. For the distal points, use moderate stimulation and keep needles in for 10-15 minutes.Acupuncture A Comprehensive Text, Bensky, 1981, page 684",
      "exp_hant": "斜視是眼位不正，多由眼肌病變所致，依偏斜方向可分類：內偏稱為內斜視，外偏稱為外斜視，上偏則稱為上斜視。健明穴位於 BL-1 (jing ming) 睛明穴下方0.4寸並稍偏外側，恰在眶下緣內側。球後穴位於眶下緣，約在眶外側緣至內側緣距離的四分之一處，主治內斜視。雖然太陽穴亦可治療眼疾，但此處並非最佳選擇，因尚有更有效的局部穴位可用。操作方法為局部穴位緩慢進針並輕微捻轉，使產生短暫輕微的觸電感；遠端穴位則採中等刺激，留針10至15分鐘。參考資料：《Acupuncture A Comprehensive Text》，Bensky，1981年，第684頁。"
    },
    {
      "number": 915,
      "question_en": "A 32 year-old male has seven year history of headaches which initially began from striking his head from a fall from a ladder. He was unconscious for a short amount of time immediately after striking his head. When he regained consciousness, he had a severe headache and dizziness. He was diagnosed with a cerebral concussion and given symptomatic treatment. After treatment, he only had occasional occipital headaches. Six months the headaches became more frequent, caused by overworking and had not having enough sleep. The occipital headaches were similar to what he originally experienced when he fell. He also has had dizziness, insomnia, and lassitude. He was hospitalized with the diagnosis of sequelae from head injury. Presently, he reports that reading greatly worsens his headache and that he cannot concentrate. His complexion looks sallow and dry. Appetite, urination, and bowel movements are normal. The tongue body is slightly red with ecchymosis at the tip with normal tongue coating. The pulse is sunken and slightly thin. Blood Pressure is 128/80, Pulse 72, Respirations 18, and Temperature 99 F. MRI of the brain shows white spots are visualized in the cerebrum. MRI, temporal bone , is within normal limits. He was treated with DU-16 (feng fu), BL-12 (feng men), and BL-10 (tian zhu). After three treatments, he showed little improvement. Which point would you add to the prescription?",
      "question_hant": "一名32歲男性有七年頭痛病史，起因於從梯子摔落撞擊頭部。撞擊頭部後曾短暫昏迷，恢復意識後出現劇烈頭痛與頭暈，經診斷為腦震盪並給予症狀治療。治療後僅偶爾出現枕部頭痛。六個月前因過度勞累及睡眠不足，頭痛發作變得更頻繁，其枕部頭痛與最初摔傷時相似，並伴有頭暈、失眠及倦怠乏力。因診斷為頭部外傷後遺症而住院。目前他表示閱讀會使頭痛明顯加劇，且無法集中注意力。面色萎黃而乾燥，食慾、大小便均正常。舌質微紅，舌尖有瘀點，舌苔正常。脈沉略細。血壓128/80，脈搏72，呼吸18次，體溫華氏99度。腦部核磁共振顯示大腦內可見白色斑點，顳骨核磁共振則屬正常範圍。曾以風府、風門、天柱治療，三次治療後改善甚微。應於處方中加入下列何穴？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
