      "exp_en": "This is a tai yang organ pattern with Accumulation of Blood. The tai yang stage is associated with the pathogenic factor (wind-cold) lodged on the exterior of the body (space between skin and muscles). But the tai yang stage also has two organ patterns that has the pathogenic factor with a deeper location in the body. These two tai yang organ patterns are Accumulation of Blood and Accumulation of Water. In the tai yang organ pattern with Accumulation of Blood there is stasis and excess Heat in the Lower Burner and the Bladder. The Bladder becomes disordered and manifests the symptoms of hypogastric distention, a sense of bladder fullness, and urgency to urinate. The excess Heat affects the Blood causing it to spill out (blood in the urine). As the Mind is rooted in Blood, the excess Heat in the Blood leads to mental restlessness. The pulse can be deep-fine-rapid or deep-choppy. The treatment principle is to Invigorate Blood, Eliminate Stasis in Lower Burner, Clear Bladder Heat.Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 756; 2005 Edition, page 714",
      "exp_hant": "此為太陽腑證之蓄血證。太陽病階段通常與病邪（風寒）滯留於體表（皮膚與肌肉之間）有關；然而太陽階段亦有兩種病邪深入體內的腑證，即蓄血證與蓄水證。太陽蓄血證是下焦與膀胱有瘀血與熱邪壅盛，膀胱功能失調，出現小腹脹滿、膀胱脹滿感及小便急迫等症狀。熱邪迫血妄行，故見尿血。因神志根植於血，血中熱盛則導致心神不寧。脈象可見沉細數或沉澀。治療原則為活血化瘀、清下焦蓄熱、清膀胱熱。參考資料：《Foundations of Chinese Medicine》，Maciocia，2015年版，第756頁；2005年版，第714頁。"
